window.FWN_HERO_SUMMONING_PEACE_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_HERO_SUMMONING_PEACE_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":2601,"title":"Chapter 2601 - Demon Realm Amusement Park 32","paragraphs":["The World King Lillywood Yggdrasil was said to be the gentlest of the Six Kings, and at the very least, the chances of angering her enough to earn a reprimand or punishment were extremely low.","That said, whether she was someone one could comfortably speak with was another matter entirely...... Lillywood was the Six King most closely associated with the Symphonia Kingdom and had relatively little interaction with the nobility of the Archlesia Empire.","If that were the case, then an exchange between Eris...... a member of the Archlesia Empire’s nobility, and moreover the heir to the immensely influential Hamilton Marquisdom and Cornelia, the eldest daughter of the Sharon County, would become a major topic of discussion within high society.","Especially lately, Eris’s reputation had been rising so rapidly that she had begun attracting increasing amounts of envy. Even so, Eris was the heir to the Hamilton Marquisdom and possessed talents worthy of being called a prodigy.","Anyone trying to drag her down out of jealousy could easily be dealt with...... but even so, finding herself repeatedly becoming acquainted with beings who stood at the very pinnacle of the world was enough to give anyone a terrible stomachache.","Her stomach was already hurting after learning earlier that day that Fate had taken enough notice of her to remember her name, even if it had taken a little time to recall it, and now, immediately afterward, she had encountered the World King herself.","If possible, she wished Kaito would simply continue chatting with Lillywood without bringing her into the conversation...... but unfortunately, even Eris herself believed the chances of that happening were slim.","As though confirming her expectations, the moment the conversation between Lillywood and Kaito came to a natural pause, Tirtania spoke up.","[Lillywood-sama! This is Eris-san!]","“Ahh, I’ve heard about you from the others, and I also saw you at the gathering celebrating Kaito-san’s birthday, but this is the first time we’ve spoken directly. It’s a pleasure to meet you. My name is Lillywood Yggdrasil.”","Responding to Tirtania’s introduction, Lillywood smiled gently as she introduced herself to Eris. By introducing herself first, she was also implicitly granting Eris permission to introduce herself in return. Understanding her intent, Eris straightened her posture and offered a graceful bow.","[It is an honor to greet the benevolent King of Spirits. I am Eris Dia Hamilton, heir to the Hamilton Marquisdom of the Archlesia Empire. Miyama Kaito-sama has always shown me exceptional kindness, and through the bond I have formed with him, Tirtania-sama and the other members of the Seven Princesses have likewise treated me with great generosity. It is with the deepest honor that I have been granted the privilege of offering my greetings to the great World King here today.]","“Thank you for such a courteous greeting. As a friend of Kaito-san, I personally hope that we can build a good relationship as well. Would it be alright if I called you Eris-san?”","[Yes.]","“Thank you...... Then please feel free to call me Lillywood as well.”","[I gratefully accept your kindness, Lillywood-sama.]","As expected of the heir to one of the empire’s great noble houses, her greeting was composed enough to exude genuine elegance. Watching nearby, both Kaito and Tirtania wore expressions of admiration.","Of course, that was only her outward appearance. Inside, she was desperately enduring the stomachache brought on by overwhelming nervousness and intimidation, her insides feeling as though they were being tightly squeezed......","[...................]","Among everyone present, the only ones who understood exactly what Eris was feeling were Eris herself, Lilia and Cornelia, who knew that same pain firsthand...... and Lillie, who habitually read the surface thoughts of those around her.","However, Lillie made no move to intervene. There was no reason for her to do so...... It was true that she could tell Eris was feeling intimidated and tense in certain respects, and that the resulting stress was giving her quite the stomachache.","However, from Lillie’s perspective, this was nothing more than a perfectly natural reaction. Lillywood stood among the very pinnacle of the Demon Realm and was the great sovereign who ruled over them all. Naturally, standing before Lillywood would inspire awe and nervousness in anyone. In fact, Lillie could only see it as proof that Eris held proper respect for her king, which left her with an even more favorable impression.","Likewise, Cornelia, who was silently praying that Lillywood wouldn’t speak to her if possible, was simply reacting as anyone naturally would when faced with someone so exalted. She saw nothing unusual or problematic about her feeling that the situation was far too overwhelming.","In truth, however...... there were also members of the World King’s camp who understood exactly what those suffering from stomachaches were going through.","(......Eris-chan seems incredibly intimidated. I wonder if her stomach’s hurting too? I’m worried about her...... And that girl over there...... errr, I’ve never seen her before, but she looks even more nervous, like she’s about to cry. Maybe someone should step in and help her relax a little......)","That person was none other than the Rose Princess, Rosemary. She was an extreme introvert, making her particularly sensitive to the mental stress and anxiety others experienced when speaking with people. She could tell that both Eris and Cornelia were suffering from stress-induced stomachaches.","She especially felt that someone ought to do something to put Cornelia at ease.","(......I- I wish we weren’t meeting for the first time......)","Unfortunately, Rosemary was far too shy to approach someone she had just met. In fact, she felt it would probably take another several months before she could even bring herself to speak directly to Eris. As such, there was simply no way she could step in to help.","No, on the contrary......","(H- Hyiiih, w- why is this happening? Rosemary-sama has been glaring at me this whole time...... D- Did I commit some sort of disrespect......? Have I done something to offend her? I’ve heard Rosemary-sama is an extremely difficult person to please...... W- W- W- What should I do......?)","Rosemary herself merely believed she was watching over Cornelia out of concern. However, because her face completely froze whenever she met someone for the first time, Cornelia saw it very differently...... For reasons she couldn’t understand, it looked as though Rosemary was silently glaring at her. As a result, instead of easing her anxiety, Rosemary unintentionally made Cornelia’s stomachache even worse, a rather ironic turn of events.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Her concern is completely backfiring. And Eris is so capable as always that Kaito hasn’t stepped in to help. If anything, he’s probably thinking “As expected of Eris-san, she’s so poised”, and raising his opinion of her even higher.]"]},{"number":2602,"title":"Chapter 2602 - Demon Realm Amusement Park 33","paragraphs":["For a while, Rosemary continued glaring...... or rather, watching Cornelia with concern, but eventually turned her gaze back to Eris.","(......I really should do something to help, shouldn’t I? I can’t do it myself, so maybe I should ask Lia......)","Just as that thought crossed her mind, someone gently placed a hand on Rosemary’s shoulder. She turned around to find Lillie standing close behind her, quietly shaking her head.","A moment later, Lillie’s voice echoed directly in Rosemary’s mind through Telepathy Magic.","(Rosemary, I consider your kindness and consideration to be virtues. However, there are times when they can become an insult. This is not the time to act.)","(Lillie-sama? Errr, do you mean...... toward Eris?)","(Yes. Naturally, your concerns are valid. While she may be maintaining her composure on the surface, she is certainly experiencing turmoil and intimidation within. I can only read surface thoughts, so she may be suffering even more deeply than I can perceive...... However, if we carelessly extend a helping hand now, we would only trample upon her resolve.)","While praising Rosemary’s kindness and compassion as admirable qualities, Lillie also cautioned her against taking action.","Lillie possessed the ability to read the surface thoughts of others. She had read not only Eris’s and Cornelia’s thoughts but Rosemary’s as well, fully understanding what she was thinking before concluding that intervening would be the wrong choice.","(She is a noble. Moreover, because she was already acquainted with all of you, she had resolved herself to speaking directly with Lillywood-sama the moment we met. She is a strong girl. She understands what it means, as a noble, to bear her family’s name upon her shoulders. Though shaken inwardly, she refuses to show it, and even now she is conducting herself before Lillywood-sama with remarkable composure. If we were to step in so thoughtlessly, we would only stain the resolve she has shown.)","(I- I see...... I’ve heard that things like honor and pride are important to nobles, so trying to help her might actually end up hurting Eris instead.)","(Indeed. Rather than her...... I believe the one who truly needs help is the other young lady.)","(Errr...... that girl over there? I’ve never seen her before, but she definitely looks incredibly nervous.)","In truth, the moment Eris encountered Lillywood and the others, she had already expected, and prepared herself, to greet Lillywood personally. As the heir to the Hamilton Marquisdom, she understood that her every word and action reflected directly upon her family’s reputation, and she was fully aware of that responsibility.","That was precisely why, even when faced with figures of such overwhelming status that her stomach felt like it was tying itself into knots, she relied on an iron will to conceal every trace of anxiety and distress, maintaining a flawless outward composure.","Perhaps that itself was a noble’s pride. If so, then offering her an easy escape would only wound that pride.","Rosemary nodded in understanding, and Lillie, having concluded that Eris would be fine, stated that it was Cornelia who should be helped instead.","(She...... Cornelia-san is far more shaken than Eris-san. I haven’t read deeply enough to be certain, but my hypothesis is that although she is also a noble, she is not the heir. Compared to Eris-san, her lack of experience is apparent, and unlike Eris-san, her anxiety is beginning to show not only internally but outwardly as well.)","(......Y- Yeah, she really does look so nervous that it’s painful to watch. I’d like to help her, but...... I- I don’t know her, so...... m- maybe you could help her, Lillie-sama......?)","(I have never met her either. If we suddenly approached her now, we would only make her shrink back even further. However, fumu...... if Lillywood-sama happens to take an interest in her, or if Kaito-san introduces her to us, then there may be nothing we can do about it......)","Naturally, there was no way Rosemary could simply strike up a conversation with Cornelia, whom she had only just met. Since Lillie understood the situation, Rosemary looked at her with a silent plea to act in her stead.","However, if one of the Seven Princesses suddenly spoke to Cornelia, it would probably only make her stomach ache even more...... After wearing a thoughtful expression for a moment, Lillie finally spoke just as the conversation between Lillywood and Eris came to a natural pause.","[......Lillywood-sama, I believe it’s about time we stopped standing here with so many people......]","“Ahh, you’re right. We’re blocking the way...... Kaito-san, if you’re all planning to enter that attraction, shall we head over there instead?”","[She’s right. If we keep chatting here, we’ll only be in everyone’s way. Let’s move.....]","With both Lillywood and Kaito agreeing to Lillie’s suggestion, everyone decided to move to the nearby Forest Castle. As a result, the situation in which Cornelia would have been introduced to Lillywood was successfully avoided.","(T- Thank you very much, Lillie-sama.)","(......Regardless of what happened today, I do think you should at least become capable of holding a simple conversation with someone you’ve just met......)","(Fuguu...... I- I’m scared of people I don’t know...... I- I need time to prepare myself mentally before I can talk to someone for the first time...... Um...... somewhere between ten days and a month......)","(If you don’t speak to them until a month later, I’m not sure they still count as someone you’ve just met......)","Watching the extremely shy Rosemary, Lillie let out a wry smile. And so, Cornelia ended up never greeting Lillywood on this occasion.","......And that, in turn, would soon lead to a stomach tragedy.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [The ending...... No, seriously, that ending there......]","? ? ? : [See? Just like Lilia said, whenever you try to avoid it, it’ll stab you from somewhere you never expected......]","Serious-senpai : [That even applies to other people’s attempts to help...... The Stomachache Warriors really are too pitiful......]"]},{"number":2603,"title":"Chapter 2603 - Demon Realm Amusement Park 34","paragraphs":["Together with Lillywood-san and all of the Seven Princesses, our entire group headed to the Forest Castle. As the name suggested, it really had the appearance of a magnificent castle built entirely of wood.","It seemed to blend seamlessly with the enormous trees surrounding it, yet it also possessed an air of nobility and refinement...... the kind of castle that wouldn’t seem at all out of place as Lillywood-san’s residence.","Well, Lillywood-san herself doesn’t like flashy castle-like buildings, so she’d probably never actually live in a place like this. Still, the atmosphere suited her perfectly.","More importantly, our group had grown much larger than I’d expected. Our original party of 10 was joined by Fate-san and Fortune-san, Eris-san and Cornelia-san, and finally Lillywood-san together with the Seven Princesses, bringing us to a total of 22 people.","22 people...... that’s a lot. I mean, the Forest Castle is large enough that we can all enter together, but having more than twenty people moving around together in an amusement park is pretty incredible. It almost feels like a school field trip...... though, come to think of it, my high school’s graduation trip was decided by a vote between Hokkaido and Okinawa, and my year went to Hokkaido, so we never visited an amusement park...... Still, I’m pretty sure there are schools that do graduation trips to amusement parks...... probably.","More importantly, what kind of attraction is this Forest Castle anyway? Judging from the atmosphere, it doesn’t seem like it’s a thrill ride......","Thinking that, I stepped inside the building, where I found a spacious hall. Barriers divided the area, and it looked like we’d check in before proceeding deeper into the castle.","As I looked around with interest, one of the attendants standing near the entrance approached us.","[Welcome to the Forest Castle. Would you mind if I gave you a brief explanation of the attraction?]","[Ah, yes. Please.]","......Unn? Arehh? Isn’t this attendant...... Alice in disguise? I didn’t really have any proof, but somehow I just had that feeling.","Well, with Fate-san and Lillywood-san here, it would probably be difficult for an ordinary employee to handle things, so maybe she disguised herself to take care of us.","[This attraction, the Forest Castle, challenges guests to solve puzzles and mechanisms hidden throughout each room as they make their way toward the throne room. If you stand on the magic circle in the center over there, you will be randomly divided into several rooms and teleported there. From that point, you’ll clear each room one by one as you advance.]","[Errr...... is it really okay for a group this large?]","[Yes, there won’t be any problem. With a group of your size...... you’ll be randomly divided into groups of 4 and 5. The challenges are designed so that differences in group size provide little to no advantage or disadvantage, so you needn’t worry about that.]","[I see......]","Since Alice was speaking directly to me, I naturally ended up responding on behalf of everyone, but it seemed this attraction was designed to accommodate all of us at once.","The closest comparison would be a much larger-scale version of that attraction in Shiro-san’s amusement park where you cleared challenges to advance through different rooms. Though Shiro-san’s version focused primarily on romance, this one seemed to revolve around solving puzzles instead...... more like an escape room, I guess?","[......And that’s how it works.]","[Sounds good to me. Kai-chan, I’m going to use my Authority, so just accept it, okay? Let’s go through it together~~]","[Unn? What do you mean?]","[Well, my Authority normally doesn’t work on Kai-chan, but if you willingly accept it, then there’s no problem. So I’m going to use my Authority to make sure you and I get assigned to the same group, and I want you to consciously accept that...... Though, with your luck, if you just wish to be in the same group as me, it’d probably happen anyway......]","[Ah, I see...... Understood.]","Fate-san immediately declared that she was going to cheat the random group assignment with her Authority...... but when I thought about it calmly, it was probably better for her to be with me.","I mean, Fate-san has matured a lot, so she probably wouldn’t treat the people assigned to her group coldly anymore...... but there was still a good chance she’d decide it was too much trouble and stop putting in any effort. And more simply, there were probably people who would be nervous just being in the same group as her.","By that logic, maybe it would be better if Lillywood-san was with me as well? Well, Lillywood-san is kind enough that she’d be fine with anyone...... As for Lilia-san, if nothing influenced the assignment, she’d probably end up with a bizarre group, so I silently wished that she’d at least get a favorable grouping.","While thinking that over, everyone else agreed as well, so all 22 of us entered the attraction together and made our way to the enormous magic circle in the center.","The staff had mentioned that anyone prone to teleportation sickness should let them know beforehand, but fortunately, no one here had any issues with teleportation.","The magic circle slowly began to glow, and just as I figured we’d be teleported at any moment, I happened to catch sight of Cornelia-san out of the corner of my eye.","Come to think of it, because all 22 of us were bunched together in the middle of the walkway, I never got the chance to introduce Cornelia-san to Lillywood-san and the others...... Maybe after we finish this attraction? No, even then, a group of 22 people standing around would just get in the way of the other guests...... Hmmm, maybe it’d be better to give up on it this time and wait for another opportunity.","The moment that thought crossed my mind, the magic circle emitted a brilliant light, and we were enveloped by it as the teleportation took place.","When the light faded, I found myself in a fairly spacious room. Nearby were Fate-san, Lillywood-san...... and...... Cornelia-san, whose complexion was so pale it looked as though every last drop of blood had drained from her face.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [He actually did it!? Not introducing her beforehand completely backfired...... Because the guy with absurd luck started thinking “When should I introduce her?”, she ended up getting thrown into that hellish group!?]"]},{"number":2604,"title":"Chapter 2604 - Demon Realm Amusement Park 35","paragraphs":["As Cornelia Sharon stood there, what came to mind was the time she had gone out with Kaito before. Back then, they had run into both Megiddo and Magnawell at the same time, and now she had once again been placed in the same group as Fate and Lillywood.","She found herself wondering if she was somehow fated to always encounter pairs of overwhelmingly intimidating people, a thought that bordered on outright escapism, even while standing before the Goddess of Fate herself.","(C- C- Calm down. I’ve already finished greeting Goddess of Fate-sama. I- I can’t avoid greeting World King-sama here, but if I can just get through that...... Even if I do, I’ll be spending the entire time between attractions with this group......?)","At this point, there was no avoiding greeting Lillywood.","[Oh, besides Kai-chan, we’ve got the World King and Konekone!]","“Indeed. However, it seems I have not yet introduced myself to this young lady.”","Naturally, this was how things were bound to proceed. They had no idea how long it would take, but they would be together until they finished the attractions, and depending on the situation, they might even need to cooperate with one another.","In that case, introducing themselves beforehand was only proper. It just happened to be happening now.","[Ahh, this is Cornelia-san. She’s a friend of mine.]","“I see. Then allow me to introduce myself. I am Lillywood Yggdrasil. It is a pleasure to meet you. You seem quite nervous, but in this setting, we are simply both friends of Kaito’s and therefore equals. Please don’t worry so much, just relax.”","[Y- Yesh! It is an honor to make your acquaintance. I am Cornelia Sharon, eldest daughter of the Sharon County.]","She hadn’t been able to introduce herself as calmly as Eris would have, but thanks to Lillywood’s gentle demeanor, she managed to stammer through her greeting and raise her head afterward.","“......Cornelia Sharon? That name sounds familiar.”","[Ahh, Megiddo-san mentioned that too. Apparently her name was inherited from a famous family head several generations back.]","“Ahhh, I see. Now that you mention it, I do recall seeing that name associated with several commercial ventures. But she’s acquainted with Megiddo as well?”","[When we went out together before, we happened to meet both Megiddo-san and Magnawell-san.]","Fortunately, Cornelia’s nervousness and feelings of intimidation were so obvious that Kaito actively stepped in to support her. Even now, he naturally carried the conversation with Lillywood for her, and inwardly, Cornelia let out a sigh of relief.","(This situation is utterly unbelievable, and honestly enough to make me dizzy...... But having Kaito-sama here is truly a blessing in disguise. Since Goddess of Fate-sama wished to accompany Kaito-sama, it isn’t impossible for this to happen, but just imagining being grouped with these two without Kaito-sama is terrifying.)","Since Fate had used her Authority and Kaito had willingly accepted it, there was never any possibility of Cornelia ending up in Fate’s group without Kaito. Even so, merely imagining such a scenario made it feel as though her stomach were being tightly squeezed.","(Things have really escalated beyond belief. Becoming acquainted with Goddess of Fate-sama and receiving the Blessing of Goddess of Fortune-sama was already incredible enough, and now I’ve even become acquainted with World King-sama...... At this rate, I’ve met almost all of the Six Kings...... And this is only a few months after meeting Kaito-sama...... At this pace, by this time next year...... will my stomach even still exist?)","Ever since meeting Kaito, one unimaginable event after another had come her way. The benefits were enormous, beyond anything she could have hoped for, but in equal measure, so too had the stomachaches continued to grow.","[......And because Sharon County itself has always been deeply involved in commerce, Cornelia-san is very knowledgeable in that area as well. She’s someone I rely on a great deal.]","“Is that so? If Kaito-san says that much, then she must truly be an exceptional person.”","[Hehh~~ so Konekone’s amazing! Since you said you weren’t the heir, I figured you didn’t really have much to do with the family business.]","Hearing the conversation, Cornelia instinctively looked at Kaito twice in disbelief.","(......Knowledgeable in commerce? Me? I’m really not...... I mean, as a member of a noble household that owns a trading company, I did have the bare minimum of knowledge...... but it really was just the bare minimum...... Most of what I know now is only because I had to hurriedly study after getting involved with the Victor Trading Company...... K- Kaito-sama? Kaito-sama!?)","Before she realized it, the conversation had gone in a very strange direction. Cornelia’s knowledge of commerce really was only at the most basic level...... but Kaito’s own knowledge was even less than that. Combined with the fact that she had guided him around a trading company before, the image Kaito had formed of her had somehow become that of an expert in business.","[She’s also really knowledgeable about the entertainment industry, music especially, that even Megiddo-san was impressed.]","“......You’re well versed in music as well? That’s truly wonderful.”","Kaito wasn’t lying. It was true that when they had gone out together before, Cornelia had known about a promising up-and-coming orchestra, and Megiddo had praised her for having a good eye.","That much was certainly true but......","(Kaito-sama? Kaito-sama!? U- Umm, you’re seriously saying that...... to one of the most world-renowned figures in the field of music......?)","At this rate, Cornelia felt that her stomach was going to disappear long before next year arrived.","<Afterword>","Stomachache Devil : [Promote how knowledgeable Cornelia is about music so Lillywood can get into a lively conversation with her about it...... Perfect!]","Serious-senpai : [......W- What a devil......]"]},{"number":2605,"title":"Chapter 2605 - Demon Realm Amusement Park 36","paragraphs":["If you had to say whether the situation was good or bad...... it was bad. If you had to say whether everything was okay...... it absolutely wasn’t. There wasn’t the slightest bit of malice involved, and the benefits to be gained were immense. Even so, there was no escaping the stomachache.","In a sense, Cornelia was currently in a critical situation.","(K- Kaito-sama has always seemed to think highly of me for some reason, but...... whether I’ll be able to make it through a conversation with World King-sama and Goddess of Fate-sama......)","Thanks to Kaito’s introduction, Cornelia was currently regarded by Lillywood and Fate as an exceptionally capable young noble lady. And most likely, the person the two of them were subconsciously comparing her to was Eris.","In other words, Lillywood and Fate viewed Cornelia as a noble lady every bit as capable as Eris...... but Cornelia herself was well aware that she didn’t possess abilities on Eris’s level.","(Knowledge, conversational skills, manners...... I know full well that I’m inferior to Eris-sama in every one of those areas. I might be able to hold my own when it comes to music and the arts, but enough to meet the expectations of World King-sama and Goddess of Fate-sama......? T- T- That’s just impossible......)","At the moment, Cornelia was desperately keeping up with every topic Lillywood and Fate threw her way. Kaito stepped in to help from time to time, but Cornelia had no room to breathe. To her, it felt like desperately dodging a barrage of swords flying toward her at incredible speed.","Even if she were to make a verbal gaffe, neither Lillywood nor Fate would actually make an issue of it. Lillywood was exceptionally gentle and kind-hearted, and Fate wasn’t the sort to sweat the small stuff.","But that wasn’t the real problem. Cornelia was already at her limit. Mentally, she felt like she was tightrope walking across a single rope stretched taut to its breaking point. If she made even one slip of the tongue, the fragile composure she was barely maintaining could shatter completely, causing one blunder after another.","That was precisely why she had to hold on...... but she was already nearing her breaking point.","[So, Konekone, are you close with Eririn? You came together after all.]","[Y- Yes. Our families have been acquainted for quite some time, and recently we’ve had even more opportunities to meet, so we’ve become quite close.]","[Hehh~~ so the family connection is one of those noble things huh......? Sounds like a pain.]","At some point...... without Cornelia even realizing it, something had changed. If she had to describe it, it was as though she had heard “the sound of a thread snapping somewhere inside her”.","“......Kaito-san mentioned that you’re quite knowledgeable about music. Have you attended the Harmonic Symphony as well?”","[Yes. Given my age, I’ve only had the opportunity to attend a handful of times, but I’ve made sure to go every year. Rather than performing myself, I’m almost always there simply to listen. The Harmonic Symphony truly deserves to be called a festival of music, and I’ve thoroughly enjoyed it every time.]","[I took part in the Harmonic Symphony too, so maybe we actually passed each other somewhere without realizing it.]","[That’s certainly possible. What a shame. If we’d known each other back then, perhaps we could have gone around together, Kaito-sama......]","Before anyone realized it, she had begun handling both Lillywood’s conversation and her exchanges with Kaito with effortless ease. More than that, the expression on her face had become remarkably gentle and cheerful.","Seeing that, Kaito relaxed, thinking “Looks like she’s finally gotten over her nerves.”, but in reality, that wasn’t what had happened at all.","(......How strange. Before I knew it, I couldn’t even feel the stomachache anymore. My mind feels so light...... My thoughts are flowing clearly, and I’m actually enjoying this conversation!)","The stomachache that had been pounding away only moments earlier had completely disappeared. Her once-constricted mind had opened up, becoming clear and sharp, leaving her with an almost refreshing sense of exhilaration.","[I think it would be a lot of fun to look around with you too, Cornelia-san. If we get the chance, let’s go together.]","[Yes. While it’s not on the same scale as the Harmonic Symphony, the Archlesia Empire also holds a music festival. If it wouldn’t inconvenience Kaito-sama, would it be alright if I invited you when the time comes?]","[Of course. I’d love to.]","She stepped effortlessly into a realm of certain death and danced through it with graceful ease. Under normal circumstances, she would have been overwhelmed with nervousness, yet now she wasn’t intimidated in the slightest, in fact, she had even managed to make plans to go out with Kaito.","A bright smile adorned her face, and she looked genuinely happy...... And from all of that, only one conclusion could be drawn......","Yes, Cornelia’s mind, pushed to its absolute limit, had entered a state where it was desperately averting its eyes from everything that could possibly lead to a stomachache.","She shoved every stomachache-inducing thought to the very back of her mind, pouring her entire body and soul into escaping reality.","It was, by pure coincidence, the exact same state Marie had fallen into when she once went out together with Kaito. Once everything was over and she came back to her senses, there was little doubt that the stomachache she had postponed would crush her all at once, whether that meant vomiting on the spot or collapsing unconscious with foam at the mouth.","Even so, at this very moment, she truly soared with effortless freedom.","......Cornelia Sharon...... had entered her Invincible State.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [T-There it is! The Invincible State where you shove everything aside and charge headfirst into certain death! She’s already gone and pulled something huge, she actually managed to invite Kaito out!]"]},{"number":2606,"title":"Chapter 2606 - Demon Realm Amusement Park 37","paragraphs":["Cornelia’s current state bears a striking resemblance to the one Baron’s daughter Marie Ritch once found herself in. That said, there are, of course, some key differences.","Marie experienced such an overwhelming succession of utterly unrealistic events that she convinced herself everything happening was just a dream. By accepting that delusion, she established the ultimate form of self-preservation, escaping reality and temporarily attaining an incredibly optimistic mindset that simply ignored every troublesome situation.","Cornelia, on the other hand, does not believe her current circumstances are a dream. She fully recognizes them as reality. Even so, she has always coped with situations beyond her ability by deliberately setting them aside for later, preventing them from exceeding the limits of what her mind could handle.","Someone as mentally resilient as Eris could face the relentless torrent of events head-on, no matter how overwhelming they became, but Cornelia simply doesn’t possess that level of strength or mental fortitude.","As a result, she developed a kind of survival strategy: separating what she could deal with immediately from what was beyond her capabilities, postponing the latter until later.","This time, however, everything happened far too quickly———– the encounter with Kaito, greeting Fate, receiving Fortune’s blessing, the appearance of Lillywood and the Seven Princesses, and then being randomly teleported into Lillywood and Fate’s group. The chain of events was so relentless that it exceeded her limits before she even had the chance to realize she had reached them. As a result, a kind of self-defense instinct kicked in.","By instinctively putting her long-practiced “deal with it later” survival technique into effect the moment her brain recognized it, she completely stopped thinking about every stressful situation. She entered a state where she simply looked away from all of it.","Unlike Marie, however, she wasn’t walking around in a dreamlike haze. She was simply no longer feeling the stomachache and was able to rely on the social skills she had cultivated to carry on conversations normally. To an outside observer, she appeared calm while interacting with Fate and Lillywood, and indeed, she seemed perfectly composed.","Of course, all she was really doing was piling up an invisible mountain of emotional debt. So when she eventually came back to her senses, the aftermath would be absolutely disastrous......","While Cornelia was, in a sense, sprinting headlong toward certain doom thanks to her invincible state, there was another group that could hardly be called peaceful.","Yes, Eris had also ended up in a rather troublesome group, and a bead of cold sweat unconsciously ran down her cheek.","[......Ah, Theta ended up in the same group as me.]","[It appears so.]","To begin with, besides Eris, the group included Caraway and Theta. As far as those two were concerned, there wasn’t a problem at all.","Although Eris had never spoken to them directly before, she knew they were Kaito’s attendant and maid. Likewise, the two of them greeted her as soon as they noticed her.","[Allow me to introduce myself. My name is Caraway, and I serve as Kaito-sama’s attendant. This is our first time speaking, but since fate has placed us in the same group, I look forward to working with you until the end.]","[Maid, Theta. Pleased to meet you.]","[Thank you both for your courteous introductions. My name is Eris Dia Hamilton. I’d appreciate it if you treated me not as a noble of Hamilton Marquisdom, but simply as one of Kaito-sama’s friends.]","Smiling, Eris returned their greetings, and for a brief moment, a warm, friendly atmosphere settled over the group...... Then, all three of them turned to look in the same direction...... at the fourth member.","The pressure emanating from her was overwhelming. Standing there silently with her arms folded, eyes narrowed into a fierce glare...... she radiated such an oppressive aura that it almost seemed as though ominous ゴゴゴゴ sound effects were rumbling around her...... It was Rosemary.","[......Um, the last time I visited Kaito-sama’s house, I heard Nebula handled the reception...... I’ve actually never spoken to Rosemary-sama before but...... isn’t she angry about something?]","[S- Such overwhelming pressure. As expected of a Peak Count-rank.]","[Rosemary-sama is quite famous for being difficult to approach. It’s possible we’ve unknowingly done something to offend her......]","Overwhelmed by Rosemary’s terrifying presence, the three of them instinctively lowered their voices. After all, none of them had ever properly spoken with Rosemary before.","Neither Camellia nor Kaito, who would normally have acted as interpreters, were present. In fact, none of the Seven Princesses were here either. As the person who was obviously of the highest standing in the group, Rosemary already appeared to be in a foul mood, causing anxiety to spread among the other three.","In reality, however, the one giving off that overwhelming aura...... was panicking internally.","(Abababa...... T- T- T- They’re all people I’ve never talked to before!? None of the Seven Princesses, Lillywood-sama, or Kaito-kun are in my group!? Awawawa, I- I- I- I’m scared...... I haven’t even spoken directly to Eris-chan before...... At this rate, it’ll probably take me...... 20 days before I can manage to talk to her...... W- W- What am I supposed to do......? Lia, Kaito-kun...... Help meeeee......!)","Yes, Rosemary had an extreme case of stranger anxiety, and being thrown into a group with three people she’d never once spoken to directly had sent her into a mild panic. As a result, her body had stiffened completely, and the overwhelming magic power she unconsciously emitted had become an oppressive aura...... Unfortunately, there was no one present to explain that.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Things are just as bad over here, the chihuahua’s going all out intimidating everyone!?]","? ? ? : [As long as there’s someone around to interpret for her, there’s absolutely no problem, but the tragedy is that not a single one of the Seven Princesses ended up in the same group...... Well~~ the wine sure is delicious!]"]},{"number":2607,"title":"Chapter 2607 - Demon Realm Amusement Park 38","paragraphs":["While being overwhelmed by the tremendous pressure emanating from the extremely shy Rosemary, Eris carefully considered the situation. If possible, she would have liked someone like Kaito to step in as a mediator, but unfortunately, he was not here.","(The pressure is incredible...... but she doesn’t seem to have any intention of speaking? This is troublesome. Even when I met Rosemary-sama before, we never exchanged a single word. From what I’ve heard, she’s said to be an exceedingly difficult person who only associates with those she personally acknowledges......)","That assessment was not entirely inaccurate. In the first place, being able to speak with Rosemary required overcoming an extraordinarily high hurdle.","Rosemary’s stranger anxiety meant that it took an exceptionally long time for her to grow accustomed to someone. In Eris’s case, by Rosemary’s own estimate, it would take about 20 more days...... though that referred to cumulative time, meaning Eris would still need to spend another 480 hours with her before Rosemary would feel comfortable enough to speak directly.","As Kaito’s friend who had smoothly introduced herself to the other Seven Princesses, Eris was already held in remarkably high regard, and the amount of time Rosemary deemed necessary before speaking to her was actually quite short. Even so, it still amounted to 20 days in total...... a goal that would likely take years to reach unless they met extraordinarily often. In fact, there were only a handful of people outside the Six Kings’ subordinates whom Rosemary could speak to directly.","(Since this attraction requires us to act as a group, someone should take command...... someone should decide our course of action. Normally, that responsibility should fall to the person of highest standing...... However, Caraway-sama and Theta-sama introduced themselves as Kaito-sama’s attendant and maid. Judging by their abilities, the two of them probably have the strength of a Peerage Holder and is stronger than I am, but in terms of social standing, I rank above them. However, Rosemary-sama, as one of the Six Kings’ Executives, outranks even me...... which means she should be the one deciding our course of action here......)","(T/N: Raw states Eta last chapter, but I’m gonna edit that. Yes, Theta is actually the character here, just didn’t realize it since I sometimes confuse the twins with each other. Eta is the outspoken, long-haired one. Had to check the wiki.)","If one were to rank everyone in this group by status, Rosemary, as one of the Six Kings’ Executives, stood at the top. Next came Eris, the heir to a Marquisdom, followed by Caraway and Theta, Kaito’s attendant and maid.","That being the case, Rosemary ought to serve as the group’s leader...... but of course, there was no way she could actually do that.","(......Awawawa, w- why are all three of them looking at me!? D- Does this mean I have to say something? No way, no way, no way, no way! I- I’d really rather everyone just pretend I’m not here...... or better yet, have Eris-chan take charge already so we can get going......)","Although Rosemary was practically panicking inside, her expression remained stiff, making the aura of intimidation around her seem even stronger.","(Rosemary-sama doesn’t appear to have any intention of speaking. She’s simply staring at me with eyes filled with unwavering resolve.)","It was a complete misunderstanding. What filled her eyes was nothing more than fear of unfamiliar people, like a timid little animal. It was akin to a tiny puppy barking at the top of its lungs to scare away something frightening.","However, misunderstandings sometimes lead to unexpectedly favorable outcomes. As Eris remained under Rosemary’s unwavering gaze, her eyes suddenly widened in realization.","(S- So that’s what this is!? Rosemary-sama is deliberately remaining silent and allowing me to handle the situation...... she’s testing me! She’s judging whether or not I’m worthy of associating with her...... No, this is how it should be. Kaito-sama’s existence is simply so extraordinary that I’ve been able to interact with the other Seven Princesses far too easily. Under normal circumstances, anyone wishing to associate with one of the Six Kings’ Executives should first prove that they possess the worth to stand beside them.)","The situation began to take a rather strange turn. Since Rosemary stubbornly remained silent, Eris concluded that she was intentionally refraining from speaking in order to test how Eris would conduct herself.","In reality, Rosemary had simply frozen up due to her stranger anxiety. However, Eris, earnest by nature and having rapidly formed connections with powerful figures thanks to Kaito’s influence, accepted this as how things ought to be.","(Rosemary-sama, I understand your intentions perfectly. I shall do everything in my power to meet your expectations.)","Needless to say, she had understood absolutely nothing. Their thoughts remained completely off...... yet by some miracle, what each of them wanted happened to align.","[Everyone, considering the nature of this attraction, I believe we should act together and cooperate as a group rather than split up. Though I am the youngest and least experienced among us, would it be acceptable if I took the initiative in guiding us to some extent? Of course, I don’t mean issuing orders, only deciding on a general course of action.]","[I have no objections.]","[Neither do I.]","Caraway and Theta readily voiced their approval. Hearing that, Eris turned toward Rosemary. Rosemary’s expression was still as stiff as ever, but the oppressive aura surrounding her had eased ever so slightly. Eris took that as proof that she had acted in accordance with Rosemary’s wishes.","(It seems I chose correctly. This tension, it feels as though cold sweat is running down my back. My abilities as a noble are being tested by none other than the famed Rose Princess...... The pressure is immense, but as the heir to Hamilton Marquisdom, I will conduct myself in a manner worthy of my family’s name. Please, judge me as strictly as you see fit.)","(T- Thank goodness...... Thank you, Eris-chan! Keep it up, just keep acting like I’m not even here!!!)","To reiterate, neither of them had managed to convey their true thoughts to the other in the slightest. It was simply that, by sheer coincidence, the results happened to align.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [By not saying anything (because she’s too nervous to speak), everyone around her ends up interpreting her silence in the most favorable way possible. In a sense, this has turned into one of those classic misunderstanding scenarios. And once again, it really drives home just how absurdly difficult it is to reach the point where you can actually have a direct conversation with Rosemary......]"]},{"number":2608,"title":"Chapter 2608 - Demon Realm Amusement Park 39","paragraphs":["The Forest Castle, an attraction in the Forest Area, was, according to Alice, an attraction where you advanced through rooms by clearing various challenges.","I ended up in the same room as Fate-san, Lillywood-san, and Cornelia-san, so the four of us would be working together as we made our way through.","At first, Cornelia-san was extremely intimidated, and I thought I’d have to step in and smooth things over whenever necessary, but as we talked, she seemed to get used to things, and she was now conversing normally with both Lillywood-san and Fate-san. Even through Sympathy Magic, I couldn’t sense any emotions like stress coming from her, so it looked like she’d be fine.","[Errr, for now, I guess we just open the door and keep going?]","[......It looks like there’s a picture and some writing on the door.]","As I murmured and looked toward the door that was presumably the way forward, Cornelia-san noticed the same thing. Sure enough, just as she said, the door had...... a large jigsaw puzzle on it...... with about two pieces missing.","And written on the door were the words “Complete the Forest Picture”. Since this was the very first room, I figured it was meant to serve as a tutorial, so the challenge would be something simple. Looking around the room, I quickly spotted the missing pieces, one was on a table, while the other had been placed in an unnaturally large gap on a bookshelf.","[I’ll fit these in...... Ah, the door opened.]","[So that’s it? That was pretty easy.]","[No, I think this attraction is about progressing through room after room like this, so that was probably just the very first challenge.]","“Is it...... something like solving riddles?”","It seemed Fate-san and Lillywood-san had never experienced an attraction like this before, and they watched with expressions of genuine curiosity.","The door with the completed puzzle opened automatically, and after passing through it, we entered the next room...... This one was circular, with pictures of animals covering the walls.","“Touch the Odd One Out”","Fumu, I see...... The various animals and monsters in the pictures probably all followed a certain pattern, and we’d have to touch the one that didn’t fit to proceed.","Since this was only the second room, I imagined we’d probably be allowed to keep trying even if we got it wrong. Even if we couldn’t figure out the odd one out, it seemed likely that brute-forcing every option would eventually get us through.","[The odd one out...... Which one could it be?]","“In that case, wouldn’t it be that Sea Horse over there? It’s the only monster that’s a sea creature.”","[Ahh~ I see.]","The picture Lillywood-san pointed to depicted...... a monster that looked like a fusion of a fish and a horse. So it wasn’t a seahorse in the ordinary sense, but actually a monster called a Sea Horse......","I reached out and lightly touched the picture, and apparently it was the correct answer, because the door opened.","[The challenges are pretty easy~~]","[Well, it is an attraction at an amusement facility. They’ve probably lowered the difficulty so people of all ages can enjoy it. Though it’s possible we’ll encounter more difficult puzzles farther ahead......]","Before I knew it, Cornelia-san had become able to speak calmly with Fate-san. Considering how nervous she’d been at first, it felt like an incredible leap forward.","It certainly did, but...... I don’t know. She seemed perfectly calm, and the emotions I sensed through Sympathy Magic weren’t strange either...... But somehow...... it felt less like she’d simply settled down and more like she’d completely let go of something, almost too completely...... Was I just overthinking it?","[Kaito-sama? Is something the matter?]","[Ah, no. It’s just that Cornelia-san seemed really nervous at first, so I was worried. I’m relieved to see you’ve calmed down.]","[Ahhh, I see. I’m sorry for making you worry. It’s simply my noble upbringing, I suppose. I kept thinking about my family’s circumstances and my position in noble society going forward, imagining one unpleasant scenario after another, and my thinking became rather rigid. But for now, I’ve decided to set all of that aside and simply enjoy the attraction. Perhaps that’s why I feel so much more at ease.]","I suppose that made sense. For nobles, connections and reputation among their peers were probably very important. Getting to know Fate-san and Lillywood-san and building those connections was certainly a good thing, but perhaps attracting too much attention could also become a problem. I could relate, I hadn’t intended it, but I’d somehow ended up being hailed as a hero in Rigforeshia, leaving me in a rather awkward position. Being put on too high a pedestal could definitely become troublesome......","[I guess noble society really is rough.]","[There is certainly an aspect of constantly keeping one another in check. Of course, it has its glamorous side as well, but it’s quite different from the world commoners tend to imagine. If, by chance, Kaito-sama were ever to attend a soirée, then given that esteemed one’s warning, no noble would carelessly approach to greet you. However, you yourself might have to be careful about whom you choose to speak to. In that case, it would be best if you attended together with a noble acquaintance.]","[I don’t know if I’ll ever have the opportunity, but if I do, maybe I’ll ask you to come with me, Cornelia-san.]","[Fufu, that would certainly be an important responsibility. If such an opportunity arises, I’ll do my utmost.]","I couldn’t say with certainty that I’d never have a chance to attend a soirée. For example, if it were something like Chris-san’s birthday party...... Since everyone had celebrated mine, I might very well decide to attend and celebrate hers.","It had been a joking exchange, but she’d agreed nonetheless. If the opportunity ever arose, relying on Cornelia-san might not be such a bad idea after all.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [She’s steadily paving the road straight to hell......]"]},{"number":2609,"title":"Chapter 2609 - Demon Realm Amusement Park 40","paragraphs":["When we arrived at the third room, the layout was a little different. Specifically...... there were two exit doors.","[There are two doors.]","[Kai-chan, Kai-chan, does this mean one of them’s the wrong one?]","[No, I don’t think it’s the kind of wrong path you’d find in a maze...... It’s probably more like a branching route. I imagine the difficulty changes depending on which path you choose.]","If you were designing an amusement park attraction that both children and adults could enjoy, the biggest issue with puzzle-based attractions would be the difference in each person’s abilities.","If you designed it around children or people who weren’t good at puzzles, adults and experienced puzzle-solvers would find it too easy. But if you made it too difficult, there would be plenty of people who couldn’t clear it.","Taking that into account, this was probably their way of adjusting the difficulty. Thinking that, I looked at the challenge written on each door...... One was the same missing puzzle piece challenge as before, except this time there were four missing pieces to find.","The other wall, on the other hand, had a sliding panel puzzle.","[......I think this sliding puzzle is probably the higher-difficulty route.]","“Based on the puzzles we’ve encountered so far, I must admit they felt a little too easy. In that case, shouldn’t we take the more difficult path?”","[Yeah. I agree it’d be nice if there was a bit more challenge...... I think there are probably several of these branching points, letting people choose the difficulty that suits them.]","[I see. So if you find the current difficulty lacking, you can take the harder path, and if you’re struggling, you can choose an easier one as you go. That’s a very well-designed attraction.]","Just as Lillywood-san said, the puzzles up to this point had honestly been a bit too easy, so the harder route seemed like the better choice.","Cornelia-san sounded impressed that the attraction let visitors choose the difficulty while they played, and just like that, we decided to take the high-difficulty route.","A certain someone did grumble “Wouldn’t the easier route let us finish faster......?”, but the majority vote settled it, we were taking the hard route.","The next room we entered had only a single exit. It was a large circular chamber, and this time, instead of pictures on the walls, there were window-like openings, each marked with a number.","Not really knowing what to expect, we headed to the center. The moment we did, animal cries echoed simultaneously from all the surrounding windows, and glowing letters appeared in the air.","“Press the number of the window where you heard the dog bark. If you missed it, the sounds will play again after two minutes.”","Oh, this was clearly a step up from the previous puzzles. Distinguishing all those animal sounds when they came from every direction at once wouldn’t be easy. Even I could only tell that it seemed to have come from somewhere on the right...... so I wasn’t confident.","Still, it looked like the sounds would play again if we waited two minutes, so as long as you were patient, clearing it shouldn’t be impossible.","[Cornelia-san, did you catch it?]","[I believe it was somewhere around numbers 4 through 7, but...... I’m afraid I can’t be certain.]","[I could only tell it came from around that area too.]","Cornelia-san was in much the same situation as I was. She seemed convinced the bark had come from one of the windows on our right, but she couldn’t narrow it down to a specific one.","[Number 6.]","“It was number 6.”","I think this is one of those cases where the difference in raw ability really shows. Fate-san and Lillywood-san seemed to have no trouble distinguishing the sounds on the first try, answering without hesitation.","Since Cornelia-san and I had both narrowed it down to somewhere between numbers 4 and 7, we walked over to the door and pressed the button marked 6...... and the door opened, allowing us to proceed to the next room.","The room beyond had...... this time, three doors.","[......Three? Arehh? This looks like the routes branch a lot more than I expected.]","[Do you think this is also based on difficulty? If there are three choices, perhaps one lowers the difficulty, one keeps it the same, and one raises it?]","As we talked, we examined the challenge in front of each door...... One required solving a 3D puzzle placed before the door, while another involved disentangling what looked like a fairly difficult metal ring puzzle.","The 3D puzzle was probably the current difficulty, or perhaps a little easier. The ring puzzle was clearly the higher-difficulty option. However, the third door was even more distinctive.","“Complete the magic circle on the door.”","The problem itself was fairly basic...... even I recognized it as a fundamental magic circle exercise.","[......It seems the routes aren’t divided solely by difficulty. They’re also separated based on whether or not you can use magic, or at least understand magical theory to some extent.]","[So that means the puzzles ahead will probably involve magic?]","Hearing Cornelia-san’s remark, I gave it some thought as well. Presenting a basic magic circle problem really did seem less like a difficulty check and more like a test of whether you could use magic.","If that was the case, then the path ahead would probably contain challenges that couldn’t be solved without using magic.","“Cornelia-san, can you use magic?”","[Ah, yes. Noble children generally attend a magic academy for about a year after turning 10 to learn magic. So, aside from nobles living in remote regions where attending for a year would be difficult, most nobles have mastered the fundamentals of magic.]","Now that she mentioned it, Eris-san had used magic without any trouble, while Marie-san had said she couldn’t use it. If you had to travel to a city with a magic academy to study, it made sense that financial circumstances would prevent some people from learning.","“Then all of us here can use magic, so perhaps we should take the magical route. I’m interested to see what kind of challenges await us......”","Still, being able to use magic was incredibly convenient...... Maybe after getting Kuro’s permission, I could give Marie-san the beginner’s magic textbook Kuro had made once I finished reading it.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Strange, isn’t it? I mean, being able to use magic would definitely be useful, and from Marie’s perspective, she’d probably be grateful for it...... So why does this feel like yet another seed of stomachache being planted?]"]},{"number":2610,"title":"Chapter 2610 - Demon Realm Amusement Park 41","paragraphs":["The first room we entered after choosing the magic route was...... well, there was nothing there. I mean, it was labeled “Rest Area”, with benches and the like.","It really did seem to be a room for taking a break, and when I looked at the wall, there was something that looked like a map, or rather, a route chart.","[This looks like a route chart. It doesn’t go into detail, but we’re here right now...... and if this is the goal, then there are about five rooms left.]","[It seems there’s only one route split ahead.]","The route chart in the rest area didn’t provide any details, but it did show the overall layout, such as the number of rooms and which rooms contained route branches.","It looked like the paths branched quite a bit. Even two rooms ahead, the route appeared to split into two different directions.","[You know, I was just thinking...... We’ve come down the route meant for people who can use magic, but just how much ability are they expecting? That last problem was as basic as it gets, but in reality, people have different levels of proficiency, right? I was wondering if there might be problems that stop you from progressing if you’re not skilled enough......]","[That’s true. It’d be scary if you chose a high-difficulty route and ended up completely stuck.]","[......Well, considering this is just an attraction at an amusement facility, I think they’ve probably kept the difficulty reasonable. I doubt it’d involve advanced magical theory...... Ah, I see now. The important thing is probably whether you can coat yourself in magic power. That last problem wasn’t really about magic itself, it was about whether you could consciously wrap your body in magic power...... Which means there are probably mechanisms ahead that only activate when you touch them while cloaked in magic power.]","It was true that simply being able to use magic covered a huge range of skill levels, and everyone had different amounts of magic power, so there was no way the challenges would require participants to cast spell after spell.","With that in mind, Fate-san’s reasoning seemed to hit the mark. The previous magic circle puzzle had required coating your hand in magic power to correct it. If you could clear that, then you were capable of wrapping your body in magic power, and simply doing that wasn’t something greatly affected by differences in proficiency.","[Fate-san, when it comes down to it, you’re actually really smart and pretty sharp, aren’t you?]","[I told you, didn’t I? I can do it if I try...... I just don’t.]","That was an undeniable fact. When all was said and done, Fate-san was incredibly quick-witted, with an excellent grasp of situations and remarkable adaptability. She had a knack for instantly seeing through to the heart of things, but just as she always said, she simply lacked the motivation. She’d understand what was going on but stay silent, or she’d be able to figure it out if she bothered thinking about it, but couldn’t be bothered to devote the effort.","Another good thing about her was that, while she was undeniably lazy, once she decided to do something, she rarely complained after getting started.","This attraction was the same. Alice had asked her to participate, and she’d only agreed on the condition that she’d be going around with me, but once she’d decided to take part, she actually participated properly. Of course, when choosing routes and the like, she’d still aim for whichever path looked the easiest and quickest to finish, but......","“That aside, this facility is very well thought out. The focus on puzzles is likely because the intent is to emphasize flexible thinking and flashes of inspiration rather than physical ability or knowledge. That way, even people with vastly different levels of strength can still enjoy themselves after being separated into different groups......”","[That’s just like Shall-tan, isn’t it? They said the goal was the throne, right? Assuming the other girls who were randomly split off are following similar branching routes...... does that mean the final room on this chart is the throne room?]","[That’s the most straightforward assumption, but there may be some sort of trick involved.]","Hearing Lillywood-san, Fate-san, and Cornelia-san’s comments, something about it began to bother me. It was related to what Fate-san had mentioned earlier about “what would happen if someone got stuck”...... As far as I remembered, there hadn’t been any rule saying “you weren’t allowed to go back to a previous room”.","If that was the case, then if you got stuck, couldn’t you simply return to the previous room and take a different route? Wouldn’t that mean you could eventually clear every room? ......No, but surely allowing players to clear every room would take far too much time. There was probably some kind of restriction or penalty in place.","And if Alice had been involved in designing it, then just as Cornelia-san said, there was probably some sort of unusual gimmick waiting......","[.....................]","[Unn? Kai-chan, what’s wrong?]","[No, um...... what do you think this upward-pointing arrow beneath the route chart means?]","[Isn’t it just indicating that this is the route chart?]","[......That’s what I thought at first too, but the arrow feels awfully small for that......]","What caught my attention was the tiny upward-pointing arrow beneath the route chart. Something about it felt off...... or rather, it kept nagging at me.","With that in mind, I casually reached out to touch the route chart, but...... it seemed to be an image created through Illusion Magic, and my hand passed right through it.","I thought there might be some kind of mechanism built into the chart, but apparently not......","————There are probably mechanisms ahead that only activate when you touch them while cloaked in magic power.","Suddenly, I remembered what Fate-san had said a little while ago. I wrapped my hand in magic power and reached out again...... This time, I felt as though I’d touched something.","It was probably an incredibly advanced magic formula...... one that only became tangible while the user was cloaked in magic power. But simply touching it didn’t do anything...... An upward-pointing arrow...... As if operating a tablet, I slid my hand upward.","Thereupon, the route chart slid upward, and words appeared.","“Extinguish every light”","......Could this be a hidden route?","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Alice does seem like the type who’d love putting in hidden routes like this, so it wouldn’t be surprising if she snuck one in.]"]},{"number":2611,"title":"Chapter 2611 - Demon Realm Amusement Park 42","paragraphs":["What appeared after sliding the route map in the rest room was what seemed to be a challenge leading to a hidden route.","[Kai-chan, what’s this?]","[I think it’s probably a hidden route that isn’t on the route map.]","[Ah~~ That totally seems like something Shall-tan would do~~]","Alice definitely struck me as the type who liked adding little bonus features, hidden extras and things like that.","Honestly, stuff like this is exciting, and I personally love it too. On top of that, this route requires you to be able to use magic, check the route map in the rest room, and notice that tiny little arrow, so I imagine it’s a pretty difficult secret to discover.","If I had to guess, there are probably several hidden routes like this, and this is just one of them.","Anyway, first things first, the challenge. Along with the words “Extinguish every light”, the screen displayed a number of circular lights arranged in a fairly regular pattern.","So the objective was to turn them all off? I tried touching one while enveloped in magic power, and...... the light I touched and the one immediately to its right went out, while the circle on the left, which had originally been dark, lit up.","[......Ah, I think I get it. This is probably one of those puzzles where touching a spot toggles that light and the ones on either side on and off. You have to switch the lights on and off until you manage to turn every single one off.]","I remembered seeing a similar gimmick in a game I’d played years ago. It had actually been a pretty difficult puzzle, and personally, this was the kind of brain teaser I wasn’t very good at.","There were quite a lot of lights on this screen too, so this looked like it would be a challenge.","[Hehh...... Hey, Kai-chan. Mind if I give it a try?]","[Yeah, of course.]","[Thanks~~ So pressing one changes it and the ones next to it, right? Then if I want to turn them all off...... like this, then this...... turn this one on once...... and...... there.]","[That fast!?]","Since Fate-san wanted to try, I let her have a go. After hearing the rules from me, she stared at the screen for only a moment before tapping it several times without the slightest hesitation, and in no time at all, every light was out.","It really made me feel the difference in our basic abilities. Once again, I was reminded that Fate-san wasn’t just powerful, she was incredibly smart too.","[It’s simple, but it’s a really well-designed puzzle~~ That should clear it, right?]","[Yeah, I think something should happen now...... Oh?]","Just as I thought something was about to happen, a deep rumbling echoed through the room. The wall where the route map had been split apart from the center, opening to either side, revealing what looked like a staircase leading underground.","[This seems to be the hidden route...... Though, is everyone okay with taking this path?]","[I’m good with it~~]","“I have no objections either.”","[Likewise. I have no objections.]","I’d been talking as though we’d already decided to take the hidden route, so I checked with everyone just to be sure. Since all three of them were perfectly fine with it, we headed down the stairs.","Even though they were stairs, they were broad and the steps were shallow, probably designed with larger people in mind. We continued downward, and eventually...... we arrived in a spacious chamber.","Mirrors mounted on pedestals fitted with magic crystals had been placed all around the room, and it looked like we’d be using them somehow. Right near the entrance stood a signboard explaining the room’s challenge.","“Guide the light to the deepest point”","Reading that, I looked around the room and noticed an Illumination Magic Tool embedded in the wall at the far edge, shining a beam of light straight ahead.","“The light we’re meant to guide must be that Illumination Magic Tool. Since it’s fixed to the wall, I assume we’re not supposed to remove it...... Rather, are we meant to reflect its light with the mirrors until it reaches the far end?”","[I think that’s probably it. The pedestals are likely fixed in place, and only the mirrors themselves can be rotated.]","[Yes, just as Kaito-sama said, the pedestals are fixed. However, touching the magic crystal rotates the mirror 45 degrees clockwise.]","As I answered Lilywood-san’s question, Cornelia-san, who had been examining one of the pedestals, offered some additional information. It seemed the objective was exactly what I’d expected: rotate the mirrors to reflect the beam of light until it reached the door at the very back of the room.","It took a bit of thinking, but it wasn’t especially difficult. After discussing it with the three of them while adjusting the mirrors around the room, we soon succeeded in reflecting the light all the way to the far end, and the door at the back opened.","[I wonder how many rooms this hidden route has?]","[Hmmm...... If we’re thinking normally, I’d guess five rooms, just like the other routes. There wouldn’t really be any reason to make only this one longer or shorter...... Though, if the rest room counts as the first room, then there might only be three rooms left.]","I gave Cornelia-san’s question some thought before answering. It’s possible this hidden route exists to obtain some special item, in which case it could be shorter because you’d return to the main route afterward. Still, I thought it was more likely that the total number of rooms to the goal was the same as the other routes.","Since we had solved a puzzle in the rest room as well, counting that as one room would make the underground section a total of four rooms, with the last one being the goal.","Thinking that, we stepped into the next room. In the center stood an ornate pedestal, and resting atop it...... was a Rubik’s Cube.","“Complete all six faces as quickly as possible. Time measurement begins the moment you pick up the cube. The slower you are, the higher the difficulty of the next room’s challenge. Maximum difficulty is reached after 5 minutes.”","I see. All six faces in five minutes huh...... For someone attempting it for the first time, even 5 minutes would be fairly challenging. This hidden route was probably intended to be considerably more difficult than the others.","......Well, no problem. Let’s finish it in under 30 seconds.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Just as always, the protagonist’s pulling off that overpowered-main-character vibe in the weirdest moments......]"]},{"number":2612,"title":"Chapter 2612 - Demon Realm Amusement Park 43","paragraphs":["The challenge waiting in the room they reached was a Rubik’s Cube. Moreover, it was the type where the difficulty of the next room changed depending on how quickly you cleared it...... Solving a Rubik’s Cube happened to be one of my few special skills, so clearing this should be no problem.","[Hmmm, looks like Body Reinforcement, Thought Acceleration, and even Space-Time Magic are disabled in this room huh?]","“That appears to be the case. It is likely a measure to ensure the challenge is carried out under conditions as equal as possible.”","Apparently, this room was designed to nullify what could be called Buff-type Magic. Well, that was only to be expected.","For example, if you could manipulate time with Space-Time Magic, you could clear it instantly. And being able to use Thought Acceleration would create far too much of a gap between those who could and those who couldn’t.","[Well, if it were me or the World King, we could ignore restrictions on the level of something that’s constantly deployed throughout a room...... But wasn’t solving Rubik’s Cubes your specialty, Kai-chan?]","[Yes. So leave this one to me.]","[Ooh, Kai-chan’s looking unusually confident today. Pretty cool~~ Alright then, we’re counting on you~~]","When I had my match with Megiddo-san before, Fate-san had been doing live commentary alongside Alice, so she apparently remembered that I was good at solving Rubik’s Cubes.","Of course, I had intended to handle this challenge from the beginning, so I simply nodded at Fate-san, who entrusted it to me with a smile, and stepped in front of the pedestal.","The timer started the moment you picked it up, so while I couldn’t see the pattern on the bottom face, as long as I could see the other faces, it was easy enough to deduce what the remaining side looked like.","Actually, seeing just two or three faces was usually enough to figure out almost the entire solution. This arrangement...... this combination...... It’ll probably take a few more moves than usual, so around 18 seconds, maybe? If I can move my middle fingers quickly and precisely enough, I might even make it into the 10-second range...... Alright.","After spending about 20 seconds working out the solution and memorizing the sequence of moves in my head, I took a deep breath and picked up the cube. I seemed to be in perfect condition today, my hands moved astonishingly smoothly without the slightest hesitation as I solved the Rubik’s Cube...... Ah, this...... I might actually set a new personal best......","I solved it so smoothly that I was convinced of it. After placing the completed cube back onto the pedestal, I looked at what appeared to be the timer, and it displayed “9.53”.","Y- Yes! I finally did it! My first sub-ten-second solve! I’d always dreamed of pulling it off someday...... but to think it’d happen here......","[O- Ohhh......]","[That was truly splendid. It was easy to see just how refined your skill is, Kaito-sama.]","“Indeed. I had no idea Kaito-san possessed such a talent.”","If I’d been alone, I would’ve shouted in triumph. As it was, I held it in and settled for a fist pump with one hand.","Sub-ten seconds. The dream of breaking 10 seconds...... This feels incredible. Sure, the very best solvers back in my old world were operating on the level of three-second solves, so I wasn’t anywhere near that, but if I’d managed to break ten seconds, then even if I couldn’t call myself one of the absolute best in the world, I think it was fair to say my skill had reached a world-class level.","[Ooh~~ Amazing, Kai-chan. Weren’t you faster than when you did it against the War King before?]","[Yeah. I was in incredible form this time and set a new personal best. It’s my first time ever breaking 10 seconds.]","[Hehh, that’s great. Congrats~~]","[Thanks. With a time like this, I think the next room’s difficulty should’ve dropped all the way to the lowest setting.]","I thanked Fate-san with a smile as bright as hers and replied. There was no way the conditions would be something absurd like needing to solve it in under five seconds, or only lowering the difficulty to the minimum if you achieved a world-record-level time.","Even if this was a hidden route that was supposed to be more difficult, there was no way it’d demand top-tier ability in a specialized field like that. I’d guess the threshold was probably around 30 seconds...... no, more likely anything under a minute would be enough to reduce it to the lowest difficulty.","[I handled the previous challenge, and Kai-chan handled this one...... So how about Konekone or the World King takes the next one?]","“That sounds reasonable. If the next room’s difficulty has indeed been lowered, perhaps it would be best to let Cornelia-san give it a try.”","[Yes. If everyone is alright with it, I’d like to take on the next challenge.]","[Then let’s have Cornelia-san do the next one, and Lillywood-san the one after that. Of course, if it looks too difficult to solve alone, we’ll work together......]","Among the members of our group, Fate-san was by far the most exceptional in terms of raw ability, followed by Lillywood-san, then there was a considerable gap before Cornelia-san and me.","I had no idea how skilled Cornelia-san was at puzzles, but she seemed quite intelligent, so she might even be better than me. Solving Rubik’s Cubes just happened to be one of my specialties......","When we entered the next room...... There were puzzles mounted on three of the walls. They were the kind where you slid the pieces around to rearrange the image, and they were fairly large. Ah, no, there was one on the wall we entered through as well, and looking up, there was another on the ceiling, making five in total......","There was what looked like a magic tool in front of each puzzle, so I guessed you were supposed to operate it to complete the large sliding puzzles.","“Complete the puzzles within five minutes. ※ Because the previous room was cleared in under one minute, all puzzles except the one you select will be completed automatically.”","So it really was a challenge to complete sliding puzzles. At maximum difficulty, you’d have to finish all five within five minutes, which sounded incredibly difficult.","This time, however, thanks to our score from the previous room, every puzzle except one would be completed automatically. That meant we only had to finish a single puzzle within five minutes, making the challenge significantly easier.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Maybe she could tell Kaito was absolutely thrilled on the inside, so Fate celebrated with him in her usual way. I guess that’s what you’d expect from his girlfriend...... Well, Kaito’s the type whose emotions show all over his face, so he was probably obviously overjoyed anyway......]"]},{"number":2613,"title":"Chapter 2613 - Demon Realm Amusement Park 44","paragraphs":["Standing quietly before the magic tool used to operate the sliding puzzle, Cornelia’s mind was now clearer than it had ever been before. At present, Cornelia was in a sort of invincible state, where her consciousness automatically diverted itself away from anything that might lead to stomach pain.","Unlike Marie, Cornelia didn’t think she was dreaming or anything of the sort. She was simply in a state where she wasn’t thinking about unnecessary things...... if it had to be described, she was in a kind of zone.","Having eliminated every unnecessary thought, she was able to focus on the task before her to the absolute limit, and she could feel herself sharper than ever before.","Yes, without even realizing it, she had become comfortable enough to chat naturally with Fate and Lillywood. She had even made a casual promise with Kaito to attend a soirée together if the opportunity arose. Beyond that...... from an outside perspective, she had been talking with Kaito so intimately that it would be difficult to deny being mistaken for his lover...... Once she came to her senses afterward, it was all but guaranteed that she’d foam at the mouth and faint from the accumulated burden of future stomachache, but at this very moment, her mind was at its absolute sharpest.","(The completed picture, the current positions of the four corner pieces...... the sequence of moves...... How strange. Even without thinking deeply about it, I know exactly how I should move them. It sounds like I’m praising myself, but perhaps it’s more accurate to say that my field of vision has become remarkably broad. I’m naturally solving the puzzle while viewing it as a whole from above. I must be concentrating exceptionally well.)","In a sense, because all the mental resources that would normally be spent worrying about the future, including her inevitable stomachache, were instead focused entirely on the present, Cornelia completed the sliding puzzle in what was nearly the shortest possible sequence of moves.","As soon as she did, the remaining sliding puzzles began moving automatically until they, too, were completed, and the door at the back opened.","[That was amazing, Cornelia-san. That puzzle looked pretty large and difficult, but you solved it so smoothly without getting stuck at all.]","[I believe I was able to concentrate very well myself. It’s thanks to Kaito-sama lowering the difficulty in the previous room. I managed this one, but if there had been five of them, it certainly would’ve been quite difficult......]","[Seeing how you handled that, it feels like you would’ve breezed through the others too. Are you especially good at puzzles?]","[No, not particularly. I just happened to do well this time. As for that three-dimensional puzzle in the previous room, it was my first time ever seeing one...... I certainly don’t have the confidence to solve something like that within 5 minutes. Kaito-sama solving it in under 10 seconds was truly astonishing.]","As could be seen from Megiddo’s reaction the first time she encountered one, the Rubik’s Cube wasn’t common in this world...... or rather, it hadn’t even existed before.","It only began being sold after the first Six Kings Festival, so while it was now available for general purchase, its recognition was still quite low, making it perfectly understandable that Cornelia had never seen one before.","[Ahh, that’s called a Rubik’s Cube. It’s one of the toys from the world I came from...... I just happened to be really good at it. There are standard solving methods and sequences of moves, so once you understand the basics, it’s actually pretty easy to solve.]","[I see, so it’s a toy from the otherworld. Even so, solving it that quickly is quite extraordinary...... If you wouldn’t mind, would you teach me sometime?]","[The Rubik’s Cube?]","[Yes. Part of it is simple curiosity, I would like to experience games from the otherworld...... but if I put it that way, I thought it would make for a good excuse to spend time with Kaito-sama. Come to think of it, we’ve been gradually getting to know each other, the tea party hosted by Eris-sama, then you showing me around the merchant company, and this chance encounter today. I do think we’ve built up quite a few opportunities to interact, but I’d also like to spend time together in a more relaxed setting.]","As she said that, Cornelia smiled cheerfully. If her usual self had heard those words, she would have rushed over and stopped herself with everything she had, even if it meant punching herself first. She was charging headfirst into a minefield of her own making. Unfortunately, the invincible-state Cornelia had no way of realizing that.","[You are older than I am, Kaito-sama, but the age difference isn’t all that great. Of course, relationships befitting a noble lady are important, but I’d like to set all of that aside for a while and simply spend time together as friends. That’s...... what I want.]","[Ahaha, honestly, I’d prefer that too. It means I don’t have to be so formal. Speaking of games from the otherworld, Eris-san played one at my birthday party too. They’re called video games, and they’re really fun. We should definitely play together sometime.]","[Yes. I’ll look forward to it.]","Deep within her heart, the part of Cornelia’s consciousness that had been sealed away was screaming as she continued piling up advance reservations for her own march into certain doom...... but the Cornelia of this moment remained blissfully unaware, happily chatting with Kaito as they headed toward the next room.","Completely unaware that this entire exchange had significantly increased Kaito’s affection for her......","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [She practically just reserved a plot in the graveyard for her stomach, but an invitation like “I just want to get to know you better as ordinary friends” is about as perfect an approach to Kaito as you can get. Yeah...... there’s no future where she escapes the stomachaches anymore.]"]},{"number":2614,"title":"Chapter 2614 - Demon Realm Amusement Park 45","paragraphs":["Now then, we’d been making excellent progress through the Forest Castle, and by our estimate, either the next room or the one after it would be the last.","A total of 10 rooms just felt like the right balance. I had been wondering whether the challenge in the rest area counted as one of the post-branch challenges...... but I was leaning toward no. Or rather, to be more precise, I thought the rest area itself counted as one room, but its challenge did not.","The reason being that the other routes all had four rooms after the rest area, so I figured this route would probably be the same. The rest area’s challenge was likely just there to unlock the hidden route, while every route totaled ten rooms including the rest area.","[......This is probably the hardest route, isn’t it?]","[I think so. Kai-chan solved it so quickly, but that Rubik’s Cube, was it? Clearing one of those within five minutes on your first try, without using magic like Thought Acceleration, would be pretty difficult.]","[The slide puzzles I did also gave plenty of time if there was only one. But with five of them, you only have one minute for each, so I think that’s quite challenging.]","“Indeed. If the target audience is ordinary visitors coming to enjoy the amusement park, the difficulty may be rather high.”","I suppose so. I just happened to be good at Rubik’s Cubes, and because of that, the slide puzzle’s difficulty had effectively been lowered...... but even the very first puzzle Fate-san solved had already been significantly harder compared to everything up to that point.","Which meant the challenges ahead would probably be even more difficult...... Thinking that, we entered the next room...... and there were several board games laid out, resembling chess.","Ah, if I’d come here alone, this might’ve been where my run ended......","“Win on every board ※Detailed rules are written on the sign”","Was it something like a chess puzzle? Thinking that, I walked over to the sign and read the rules. The board game itself looked similar to chess, but the piece movements were more complicated, and the pieces themselves were different, so it appeared to be an entirely different game.","Maybe it was an original board game. For now, the sign explained how each piece moved and the rules for clearing the challenge. Touching the magic crystal on each board would automatically generate a puzzle, which had to be solved within five minutes. There were five boards in total, and clearing all of them completed the challenge...... If you failed, however, that board would reset and generate a brand-new puzzle.","......Eh? That’s brutal...... In other words, if you ran out of time or failed, the puzzle would be completely replaced, so you couldn’t learn from your mistakes and clear it on the next attempt.","It didn’t seem like there was any penalty for failing itself, you could challenge it as many times as you wanted, but the piece movements were extremely complicated, and it looked incredibly difficult.","“......I understand the rules, but I suppose I won’t know how difficult it is until I actually try.”","[Lillywood-san, do you play board games?]","“No, I’ve had very little experience with this sort of entertainment. That said, this is essentially just a puzzle where you decipher the correct sequence of moves, so I don’t believe it will pose any problem.”","[I see. I’m sure you’ll be fine, Lillywood-san, but don’t push yourself too hard. Good luck.]","“Yes. Thank you.”","According to Fate-san, magic such as Thought Acceleration was generally unusable on this hidden route. Someone of Lillywood-san’s caliber could apparently ignore that restriction if she wished...... but knowing her personality, she wouldn’t.","As for me, I’m absolutely hopeless when it comes to board games, so I couldn’t be of any help at all. The only thing I could do was cheer them on.","After smiling at my words, Lillywood-san reached out and touched the magic crystal. The pieces on the board began moving on their own, generating the puzzle.","I still hadn’t even memorized how the pieces moved, so I had no idea what was going on. Lillywood-san, however...... without even seeming to think, picked up the pieces and made about ten moves.","Then, accompanied by a chime that sounded like a “correct answer” notification, the board she had just played on vanished. Apparently, she’d cleared it. If she repeated that four more times, we’d clear this room, right?","[......Lillywood-san, you solved that incredibly easily just now.]","“Yes. A problem of that level...... the pieces’ movements are fairly straightforward, so I wouldn’t say it’s a particularly difficult game. Perhaps this room is easier than the others.”","No, it looked incredibly complicated...... There were around 20 different kinds of pieces...... I’m pretty sure it was much harder than chess or shogi......","Lillywood-san proceeded to clear the other four boards just as effortlessly, barely pausing to think. She genuinely seemed to believe it was a simple game.","[......Cornelia-san, did you understand what was going on?]","[If I took my time, I think I could probably solve it, but my impression is that it’s extremely complicated and difficult. The last puzzle, in particular, took around 30 moves...... To solve something like that within five minutes, I think you’d need not only quick thinking, but also insight and a bit of luck.]","Thank goodness. Apparently, I wasn’t the only one who thought it was difficult. It wasn’t that the challenge was easy, it was simply that Lillywood-san was extraordinary.","Lillywood-san herself wore a quietly satisfied smile...... She was probably enjoying the novelty of experiencing what she considered “ordinary people’s entertainment”.","......This route really is incredibly difficult. Having Lillywood-san and Fate-san with us meant we’d be fine, but...... what kind of challenge could the final room possibly have waiting for us?","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [So Lillywood really does have ridiculously high specs......]","? ? ? : [Just like how Kuro-san once said she’d only ever seen six other people with talent comparable to Lilia-san’s, Lillywood-san is genuinely a genius on the same level as Lilia-san. She can grasp the rules at a glance, and even on her first try, she’ll breeze right through the challenges.]"]},{"number":2615,"title":"Chapter 2615 - Demon Realm Amusement Park 46","paragraphs":["The room we arrived at, which I expected would be the last one if my guess was right, was...... clearly different from all the others.","[......A chapel, perhaps?]","Yes, it looked like a large chapel. The walls were lined with enormous stained-glass windows, each depicting a different symbolic scene.","And beneath each stained-glass window was a door...... A quick count revealed nine stained-glass windows and nine corresponding doors. In the center of the chapel stood a sign.","“Proceed along the right path ※Once you pass through a door, you cannot return”","I see. So the final challenge was a puzzle...... Out of the nine doors, only one was the correct choice, and we were supposed to determine which one it was using the clues hidden throughout the chapel. The images on the stained-glass windows were probably the key.","[I have a feeling...... no matter which door you choose, you’ll still reach the goal in the end. It’s just that only the correct door leads to the special hidden-route ending.]","[So we must deduce the answer from the clues within the chapel.]","Cornelia-san nodded at my conclusion and slowly looked around the chapel. The figures depicted in the stained glass looked vaguely human, but what significance did they have?","As I was wondering that, Fate-san muttered with an awkward expression.","[Ugh...... that’s me......]","[Eh? Ah, now that you mention it, it really does look like Fate-san. And that stained glass over there looks like Chronois-san, while that one resembles Life-san.]","After Fate-san pointed it out, I took another look. She was right, it really did resemble Fate-san...... There were also figures that looked like Chronois-san, Life-san...... Sky-san, Gaia-san, Shea-san, and Fortune-san.","“Perhaps these stained-glass windows are based on the Creation Story.”","[Ahh~~ yeah, that does seem likely. Me, God of Time and Space, God of Life and the two direct subordinate gods serving each of us.]","[The Creation Story is something almost everyone knows. It certainly makes for a fitting theme for a puzzle.]","The Creation Story was best known as the tale reenacted by Gods during events like the Hero Festival, but as Cornelia-san said, it was fundamentally one of those classic stories that nearly everyone in the world knew.","The closest equivalent in Japan would probably be Momotaro. Parents told it to their children, people heard it during worship, at school, and at blessings. Living an ordinary life in Trinia without ever encountering the Creation Story would be extraordinarily rare.","Of course, few people knew every detail or all of its deeper meanings, but even I knew the general outline.","“The great God of Creation created the world, and first brought forth the Goddess of Fate. Through the Goddess of Fate, the world’s laws came into being. Next, the God of Creation created the Goddess of Life, and through the Goddess of Life, life was born into the world. Then the God of Creation created the Goddess of Time, and the flow of time began. Fate fashioned the scales of calamity and fortune. Life established the earth and the heavens. Time raced forth like a flash of light, nurturing the thoughts of all living beings......”","That’s how the story went, a myth describing how the present world came into existence, beginning with Shiro-san. The full tale was much longer, but this opening portion was by far the most famous. It featured Fate-san, Life-san, Chronois-san, Shea-san, Fortune-san, Gaia-san, Sky-san, God of Flash-san, and God of Thoughts-san, perfectly matching the figures depicted in the chapel’s stained-glass windows.","[......Well, the Creation Story is really just a fabricated tale. More of a piece of propaganda constructed to spread awareness of Gods.]","[Eh? I- Is that true?]","[Unn. Kai-chan and World King already know this, but in reality, everything was created by Shallow Vernal-sama. She created the world, the laws of nature, life, everything. We Gods were created afterward by Shallow Vernal-sama and granted the necessary powers...... our Authorities, to manage and oversee the world she had made., so it wasn’t that fate came into existence because I was born. It’s actually the other way around. I was created in order to govern the concepts of laws and fate.]","Judging by the obvious look of surprise on Cornelia-san’s face, it seemed that the Creation Story was generally accepted as historical fact by the public.","[......You said it was constructed...... Does that mean the Creation Story was actually written by Gods?]","[Unn. More specifically, it was a story God of Life, God of Time and Space, and I came up with together. Well, God of Time and Space did most of the writing. God of Life and I only chimed in with suggestions every now and then......]","[Ah~~ was that Shiro-san’s idea?]","[Of course it was. If it hadn’t been Shallow Vernal-sama’s command, there’s no way we’d have made up a story claiming that things Shallow Vernal-sama did were actually our own accomplishments.]","[Yeah, that makes sense.]","I’d already suspected that the Creation Story had been written at Shiro-san’s instruction. After all, otherwise I couldn’t imagine Gods allowing such a story to exist.","[Apparently the original proposal came from Kurorin. After the Treaty of Friendship was signed, she thought it would be good to have a story like that to help people become familiar with the God Realm...... I think that’s also why Shallow Vernal-sama instructed us to write it so that we were the ones who created fate, life, and time. If the story was just “Shallow Vernal-sama created everything, and we were put in charge of managing it”, then it wouldn’t make for much of a story.]","[Well...... that’s certainly true. But if the Creation Story is the basis for this...... then which door is supposed to be the “right path”?]","[......That’s the problem.]","Right, we’d figured out the theme, and having Fate-san here had let us hear some fascinating behind-the-scenes details...... But that was beside the point. Now that we knew the motif was the Creation Story, the real question was which of the doors was the correct one. With that, all of us tilted our heads in thought.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Well, considering Shiro and her thoughts only that of “maintaining the Treaty of Friendship”, I can’t really imagine her coming up with something so thoughtful on her own, so it makes sense that Kuro was the one who proposed it. Honestly, I bet Kuro came up with almost everything, and Shiro just passed Kuro’s instructions along to the Supreme Gods as if they were her own.]"]},{"number":2616,"title":"Chapter 2616 - Demon Realm Amusement Park 47","paragraphs":["A chapel presumably modeled after the Creation Story. I figured out the motif, but as for which door is the correct one, I have no idea.","The Gods represented by the doors preside over fate, life, space-time, calamity, fortune, sky, earth, flash, thoughts...... Just knowing that doesn’t tell us anything.","[After all, it feels like there’s a hint somewhere in the Creation Story, doesn’t it?]","“Given how clearly it’s based on it, that would be the natural assumption, but...... I don’t remember anything in particular that would indicate the correct door.”","[Hmm~~ Maybe it’s about making associations?]","I don’t remember the Creation Story in that much detail, but since neither Lilywood-san nor Fate-san could think of anything in particular either, it seemed there wasn’t any direct hint.","At that moment, Cornelia-san, who had been wearing a thoughtful expression, opened her mouth.","[......This might be a bit of a stretch, but in the latter half of the Creation Story, in the section concerning the Treaty of Friendship, there was a line about light shining upon the dawn of a new era, wasn’t there?]","[There was. I see, the Treaty of Friendship was a major turning point for this world, and if we associate “dawn” with opening a door......]","“Then, based on the phrase about light shining through, the stained-glass door depicting the God of Flash is the correct one?”","It did seem to form a reasonable association, and if none of the three of them could think of anything else that fit, then there probably wasn’t anything else.","In that case, the stained-glass door depicting God of Flash-san was the correct one...... or at least, thinking that way did feel a little forced, just as Cornelia-san had initially said.","That said, we couldn’t think of any other candidates, and we couldn’t spend forever here, so even though none of us were entirely convinced, we were about to head toward the door in question.","It was then that I happened to look at the signboard with the instructions written on it...... and was struck by an intense sense of wrongness.","[......Wait a second. I just thought of something. This signboard...... The warning says that once we pass through a door, we can’t come back, but the actual challenge says “Proceed along the right path”...... It doesn’t say “door”, does it?]","[......You’re right. There are nine doors laid out here as conspicuously as possible, but maybe they’re actually all wrong...... That does sound like something Shall-tan would do.]","That’s right. The challenge deliberately says to proceed along the right path, rather than to proceed through the right door.","[On top of that, something occurred to me...... Even though this is based on the Creation Story, there isn’t a stained-glass window of Shiro-san in this chapel......]","[Indeed, as Kaito-sama says, it would be unnatural for a chapel this intricately constructed to lack only a stained-glass window modeled after Shallow Vernal-sama, the god of the world.]","That’s right, the absence of a stained-glass window depicting Shiro-san was unnatural too. No matter how I looked at it, she was the most important existence among the gods, and she should also have been the very first one to appear in the Creation Story. It was strange that there was nothing here modeled after Shiro-san.","“Now that you mention it, I just realized something. Why is this place a chapel? If it’s just the doors and stained-glass windows, there was no reason it couldn’t have been a hall or something...... If there’s a reason it’s a chapel, then the key would be...... prayer, perhaps?”","[Come to think of it, the center is unusually spacious, isn’t it? I thought it was simply part of the design, but...... arehh, is that space for praying?]","Not a door, but a path. Shiro-san’s nonexistent stained-glass window. A chapel as the location. The spacious area in the center...... We looked at one another and nodded, then moved to the central space and assumed a posture of prayer.","I didn’t know whether this was the correct action, but there was no harm in trying...... And so, after about 10 seconds had passed with us in a posture of prayer...... a rumbling sound like an earthquake rang out, and a change occurred within the chapel.","It was probably an effect made possible precisely because it was created with Illusion Magic, but the stained-glass windows depicting the nine gods, including Fate-san, above the doors began to move...... And just when I thought they had broken apart like pieces of a puzzle during the movement, they assembled and merged together on the wall directly in front of us, transforming into a single enormous...... stained-glass window modeled after Shiro-san’s appearance from behind.","The enormous stained-glass window, which was so majestic that it almost felt divine, flashed several times as though sparkling before fading away like mist...... And in the place where the gigantic stained-glass window had been, a path leading straight ahead appeared.","[T- This is an incredibly elaborate and magnificent mechanism. I got goosebumps......]","[It was really impressive when our stained-glass windows merged together and became a stained-glass window of Shallow Vernal-sama. Also, we did it, Kai-chan! This is definitely the right path.]","“If Kaito-san hadn’t made that observation, I believe we would have proceeded through one of the doors despite sensing that something was off, so this was thanks to you, Kaito-san.”","[N- No, I just happened to find it strange. I’m just glad it was the correct answer.]","Surely there was no way that a path that had appeared with such an elaborate spectacle could be the wrong one. Feeling embarrassed by their praise, I lightly scratched my cheek as I looked at the path that had appeared.","A path that had appeared after fulfilling the special conditions for a hidden route...... At the very least, I assumed it would lead us somewhere different from the goal we’d originally been told about, but what kind of place would we find......?","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [......Well, Alice would certainly prepare a trap where all the choices are wrong.]","? ? ? : [It’s a hidden route, after all. Honestly, it’s more like a bonus factor. It was something I put in with the idea that someday, someone would find it and clear it~~ Though, the moment Kaito-san decided to go to Forest Castle, I figured he’d probably make it there......]"]},{"number":2617,"title":"Chapter 2617 - Demon Realm Amusement Park 48","paragraphs":["After walking along the path that had appeared and seemed to be the correct answer for a while, we arrived at what appeared to be the goal. It was, how should I say this...... a space that was so impressive I couldn’t help but be overwhelmed.","It was a space filled with colorful flowers, various trees, and vivid fruits, with what looked to be not merely dozens but hundreds of different kinds of flowers and trees blooming in abundance. Although it looked somewhat eclectic at first glance, the colors and such had been arranged in a way that made the whole thing look vivid and beautiful.","A straight path continued as though surrounded by beautiful flowers, and at the back of the room was a magnificent throne made of wood. It seemed there was no mistake that this was the goal.","[......This is incredible.]","“I see, must be precisely because they’re made with Illusion Magic huh. Under normal circumstances, plants that could not grow in the same environment are blooming together, and it has a flamboyance and grandeur befitting the throne room of the Forest Castle.”","[If World King really put their mind to it, couldn’t you actually create a space like this?]","“It would be possible, but even if I forcibly gathered them all into one place, the flowers and trees would feel cramped. Besides, this sort of flashy splendor isn’t something I particularly favor. No, they are pleasant to look at like this, but...... preparing something like this as a place for my use......”","Indeed, this space was worthy of being called the throne room of the Forest Castle...... the castle in the forest. Despite being almost entirely made up of plants, it had an appearance of extravagant splendor, and one could certainly call it the domain of a king who ruled over the forest.","Well, Lillywood-san, who could actually be called the king of the forest, doesn’t particularly care for that sort of extravagant splendor, so this could be considered a throne room belonging specifically to the attraction.","If anything, perhaps they may have deliberately made it different from Lillywood-san’s tastes in order to convey that this was merely an amusement park attraction and had nothing to do with Lillywood-san herself.","As I thought about that, I walked along the prepared path while admiring the beautiful flowers and neatly arranged trees. Just as we reached around the center of the room, glowing letters appeared in midair.","“Congratulations. You have reached the hidden true throne, which is not intended for audiences. To commemorate your achievement, we have prepared a small commemorative gift. Please touch the magic tool in front of the throne one person at a time, in order. You can return to the entrance through the magic circle behind the throne.”","So this really was the goal...... and more specifically, there was no doubt that this was the true goal at the end of the hidden route. Apparently, we were going to receive something like a clear reward.","I decided to represent everyone and touched the cylindrical magic tool in front of the throne first. After emitting a faint glow once, a single card appeared.","Metal? I wasn’t sure what it was made of, but the card had a texture that felt somewhat like iron. A picture of the Forest Castle was drawn on its front, while the back read “You are the first Explorer to reach the true throne”.","When Fate-san and the others touched it in turn, the numbering on the back changed to second, third, and so on. I see, so the clear reward for completing the hidden route was a special card with a serial number huh...... It was a nice keepsake that would serve as a memory of this attraction.","[However, even though we made pretty good progress, it took quite a while. I’m a little worried that the others might be waiting for us.]","[Ahh, I think we don’t have to worry about that. After we were teleported here, large-scale Space-Time Magic and a barrier were placed over the entire attraction, so it seems that the flow of time inside the attraction is being adjusted to some extent. Even if the groups were divided differently or took different routes, I think it’s probably arranged so that everyone can leave at roughly the same time.]","“It is quite a complicated and advanced barrier formula, so Kuromueina must have designed it. Rather than simply slowing the flow of time, it seems to accelerate it depending on each individual’s progress when necessary, adjusting things so that, in the end, only about fifteen minutes pass outside.”","[That’s quite something...... A barrier that is so complicated and advanced that, even if I heard the explanation, I wouldn’t even be able to imagine the formula.]","I had felt that each individual challenge took a fair amount of time, and that, aside from some of the higher-difficulty ones, they could be attempted as many times as we wanted, so I figured that struggling with them could make the whole thing take quite a while...... But apparently, a barrier that adjusted the flow of time had been placed so that every group could return about 15 minutes after entering.","Just like Cornelia-san, I couldn’t even begin to imagine the formula behind it, but I remembered Dr. Vier using magic that altered the flow of time within a barrier, so this was probably an even more complicated version of that.","Apparently, Kuro’s creative abilities had been improving by leaps and bounds lately, and I’d heard that she had become capable of doing things fairly similar to Shiro-san, so I supposed it wasn’t particularly strange that she could do something like this.","Well, regardless, if that was the case, then it was a relief to know that we wouldn’t have to worry about going outside and waiting for a long time, or conversely, making the others wait for us.","[Well~~ then, if everyone is okay, shall we head back......?]","[Yes. We can return by stepping onto the magic circle...... Judging by its size, it looks like we can only go one person at a time.]","[Then let’s head back in order, starting with Konekone~~]","Since the order in which we had touched the magic crystal in front of the throne had been me, Fate-san, Lillywood-san, and Cornelia-san, we had moved away after receiving our cards in that order. As a result, Cornelia-san was currently the closest to the throne, so leaving the room in the reverse order of how we had touched the magic crystal seemed like it would be the smoothest way to go.","Cornelia-san nodded at Fate-san’s words, stepped onto the magic circle, and disappeared. Next, Lillywood-san stepped onto the magic circle and teleported away.","Next was Fate-san...... or so I thought, but Fate-san turned around in front of the magic circle and beckoned me over.","[Hey, Kai-chan. Bring your face closer~~]","[Eh? Like this——— Mmph!?]","As I bent down to bring my face closer as Fate-san asked, she suddenly pressed her lips against mine and kissed me head-on, catching me completely off guard.","After a deep kiss in which our lips were firmly pressed together, yet one that lasted only the briefest instant, Fate-san pulled her lips away and smiled mischievously.","[Ehehe, I had so much fun going through it with you, Kai-chan! Thanks~~]","With that, she stepped onto the magic circle with a beaming smile and disappeared. I was so caught off guard by the completely unexpected surprise that I was left momentarily stunned, but I couldn’t help giving a wry smile at how utterly typical of Fate-san’s suddenness that was.","Then, savoring the pleasant sensation of happiness that faintly lingered on my lips, I stepped onto the magic circle as well.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [What the heck are you doing!? I thought having a large group meant we were safe, but don’t take things in that direction!!! Stop! What are you going to do if the whole flow changes!?]"]},{"number":2618,"title":"Chapter 2618 - Demon Realm Amusement Park 49","paragraphs":["Although the barrier within the attraction ensures that everyone can generally finish and come out at roughly the same time, there seemed to be some slight differences, and when we were teleported to the entrance, there was no one around except us.","However, that only lasted for a few dozen seconds, as another group soon appeared in the area that served as the exit...... and immediately afterward, I felt something cling to my back.","[Huh? Eh? ......Rosemary-san!?]","When I turned around, there was Rosemary-san, practically plastered against my back. She had her hands on both of my shoulders, hiding so completely behind me that she was almost invisible from the front, and was trembling slightly.","I barely had time to wonder what had happened before Eris-san, Caraway, and Theta were teleported in after Rosemary-san...... and the moment I saw the members, I pretty much understood what’s going on.","[K- Kaito-kun......h- hyel, help me......]","[A- Ahh~~ I see......That was an unfortunate grouping. Are you okay?]","[E- Eris-chan did her best, and we managed to clear it without any problems, but......I was too scared to talk at all, so I felt horribly awkward the whole time.]","[......Good work out there.]","For Rosemary-san, who has an extreme case of stranger anxiety and, even with someone she takes to quickly, needs anywhere from several hours to several days before she can get used to them, being assigned to a group consisting entirely of people she had barely ever spoken to could only be described as incredibly unlucky.","She probably remained silent the entire time with her expression frozen, while Eris-san and the others probably tried to be considerate by initiating conversation and talking to her. But Rosemary-san wouldn’t be able to respond and would only glare at them...... It must have created an atmosphere straight out of hell.","“......You’re the same as ever, aren’t you?”","[N- No, well, even so, compared to before, I’ve gotten to the point where I can talk to people I’m meeting for the first time for about two days less on average before I get used to them......B- But even so, people I’m not familiar with are scary.]","Rosemary-san replied in a small voice to Lillywood-san, who spoke with an exasperated smile. No, really, she looks quite flashy, but personality-wise she’s completely a timid little Chihuahua, so the gap is incredible...... Also, she’s pressed herself really tightly against my back, so I can feel...... Camellia-san, please come quickly.","[Eris-sama, good work. How are things on your side?]","[C- Cornelia-sama...... W- Were you really okay with that grouping......?]","[Eh? Yes, I had a very enjoyable time, and it was an honor to be able to speak at length with Fate-sama and Lillywood-sama.]","[When did you start calling them by name......I- I’m glad you were okay, though......Ah, but to return to the matter at hand, unfortunately, I was unable to demonstrate enough ability to earn Rosemary-sama’s recognition, and I wasn’t able to speak with her directly until the very end. She did cooperate with me during the challenges and such, so I suppose it’s not as though she didn’t evaluate me at all......but it made me realize that I still have a long way to go.]","After speaking with Cornelia-san, Eris-san, who had been wearing a puzzled...... or rather, concerned expression, seemed to pull herself together a little and continued talking.","Earn Rosemary-san’s recognition? A- Ahhh, come to think of it, I seem to remember that when we were dealing with the rose accessory case, she said that Rosemary-san was difficult to deal with and would only speak to people she acknowledged...... Is that how she’s generally perceived by society? It’s more like she’s afraid of strangers though......","As I was thinking that, the others gradually began returning as well, and perhaps relieved to see Camellia-san appear, Rosemary-san moved away from my back and started talking with her.","Lilia-san, who I had been worried about, had been grouped with Luna-san, Hina-chan, and Tir-san, which was about as safe a combination as you could ask for. Apparently, Hina-chan and Tir-san had happily taken the lead, while Lilia-san enjoyed watching them together with Luna-san and occasionally stepped in to help when necessary.","[Ehh~~ Kaito-senpai, you actually made it to the True Throne!?]","[Unn. We happened to take the right route by chance......Arehh? But Hina-chan knew about the True Throne too?]","[Errr, the one we reached was the normal throne, but when we got there, a message appeared in glowing letters that said something like “There is also a hidden True Throne separate from this one, so if you have the opportunity to visit again, please try looking for it.”]","[Ah~~ I see. Having something like that makes you want to try again, so it’s a pretty clever design.]","I had thought that finding the hidden route would be quite difficult, but if there was a hint when you reached the normal throne, then when you tried again, you’d know to look for something like that, which might make it easier to find. It would also simply encourage repeat visitors, so I thought it was a good idea with the official opening in mind.","As I was giving Hina-chan, who seemed interested, a brief explanation about the True Throne, Aoi-chan joined the conversation as well, and we ended up talking about the routes each of us had taken.","Apparently, Lilia-san and Luna-san had basically left everything to Hina-chan and Tir-san, only helping when they ran into trouble, so they made it to the goal by taking a relatively easy route.","According to them, many of the easier routes weren’t really puzzles so much as rooms where you had to search around for something, like the first room, and find a key.","Aoi-chan seemed to have taken a high-difficulty route, and as expected, there were many problems that required some serious thinking, with quite a few that were basically three-dimensional puzzles.","Still, even though they were on the difficult side, they were designed in a way that worked as attractions, and apparently there were hardly any elaborate gimmicks like the hidden route we took, or things involving restrictions or changing difficulty levels.","Well, regardless, taking everything into account, including our impressions after finishing it, I think it was a good attraction that a large group of people could enjoy together.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Lilia got a nice, peaceful grouping with no stomachaches involved, because Kaito had thought beforehand that he hoped things would turn out like that......]","? ? ? : [No doubt the luck correction kicked in there. Well, the only concern left is...... at what point Cornelia-san’s bomb would explode.]"]},{"number":2619,"title":"Chapter 2619 - Demon Realm Amusement Park 50","paragraphs":["Our visit to the Forest Castle attraction had come to an end, and naturally, we couldn’t continue going around in such a large group, so we split up.","Come to think of it, though, it really was quite amazing that this many people had happened to gather in one place.","[God of Fate-sama, how did you like the attraction?]","[Since Kai-chan was with me, I had fun. I was impressed by how much thought had gone into the content, too. Amusement parks really are pretty amazing......]","[I see. Would you be interested in going around some of the other attractions?]","[No, that’s too much of a hassle, so I’m going home. I’ll leave the rest to God of Fortune.]","This is very much like Fate-san. She spoke quite happily about how much she enjoyed the Forest Castle, and she was also interested in and impressed by the novelty of the amusement park and the ingenuity that had gone into its attractions.","But that was that; she still found going around too much of a hassle, so she’d completed the one attraction she was obligated to do and was going home.","[Fate-san, would you be willing to write a comment about your experience, or perhaps a short recommendation?]","[Shall-tan...... Do you really think I’d write something like that?]","[I don’t. I was just asking on the off-chance you actually would.]","[You can write it in a way that makes it sound like I wrote it.]","[......This God just outright told me to forge it......]","As for a short comment for promotional purposes...... well, I certainly can’t see Fate-san writing one. Still, it seemed like Fate-san was fine with her name being used, or rather, she basically had a “do whatever you want” attitude about it, so there probably wouldn’t be a problem with putting something like “God of Fate has experienced it herself” on promotional material for the Forest Castle.","[We’re planning to go get something to eat after this...... What are you guys going to do, Lillywood-san?]","“We intend to spend a little more time looking around the Forest Area. It is an area with a familiar atmosphere to us, and depending on what we find, there may even be things that could be put to use in Yggfresis.”","Lillywood-san and the Seven Princesses seemed to be planning to continue looking around the Forest Area. Lillywood-san seemed to have taken an interest in amusement-related facilities, which she hadn’t really shown much interest in until now, and she’d looked quite intrigued by Forest Castle as well, so perhaps someday something like an amusement facility might be built in Yggfresis under the direction of the World King’s subordinates.","Something like a large-scale athletic course making use of trees and such might even become a tourist attraction.","[I see...... What about Eris-san and Cornelia-san?]","[We have several things we need to report to our families, so we intend to move on after we finish contacting them. Cornelia-sama, is that all right with you as well?]","[Yes. It is a shame to interrupt such a pleasant atmosphere, but I do need to report that I met Fate-sama and Lillywood-sama, as well as the fact that I was granted the Provisional Blessing of Goddess of Fortune-sama.]","[......Um, Cornelia-sama? Are you really alright?]","[Eh? What do you mean?]","[......No, if you’re fine, then that’s all that matters......]","What was that about? I was a little concerned by the worried expression on Eris-san’s face as she looked at Cornelia-san. There didn’t seem to be anything strange about Cornelia-san in particular, and even through Sympathy Magic, I couldn’t sense any emotions suggesting that she was forcing herself, so I assumed she was fine.","If anything, perhaps she was just a little more energetic than usual? But then again, it was only natural to get somewhat excited when coming to an amusement park.","[......Shall-tan? What are you doing?]","[I’d feel too sorry for her to drink wine, but this is still pretty nerve-racking. It’s like I’m staring at an unexploded bomb.]","[What do you mean by that?]","[Literally what I said.]","It was a little concerning, but in any case, there were so many of us that we couldn’t stay and chat for too long. So, after briefly saying goodbye to Lillywood-san and the Seven Princesses, Fate-san and Fortune-san, and Eris-san and Cornelia-san, our group left the area.","<Afterword>"]},{"number":2620,"title":"Chapter 2620 - Intermission: The Stomachache Catches Up","paragraphs":["After parting ways with Kaito and the others, Eris and Cornelia were finally in a position to take a breather, but...... Eris was still concerned about Cornelia’s condition.","(At first glance, there doesn’t seem to be any problem. If anything, she seems quite at ease, but what is this inexplicable anxiety I feel......? It’s as though I’m looking at a thread that’s about to snap, or a balloon that’s been filled with too much air...... No, but I don’t have the words to properly describe that state, nor do I have anything resembling a basis for my concern.)","Eris felt an indescribable sense of unease regarding Cornelia’s current condition, but she found it difficult to put that feeling into words.","Cornelia was calm, and there was nothing strange about her behavior or appearance. If anything, she seemed even more relaxed than usual, but somehow...... it felt as though she was too relaxed.","[......Cornelia-sama, it must have been quite difficult being together with not only Kaito-sama, but also Goddess of Fate-sama and World King-sama, all such illustrious figures. Have you not accumulated any mental fatigue?]","[Yes, Fate-sama and Lillywood-sama are both extremely benevolent individuals, and they were kind enough to engage in conversation with me, so I feel that I was able to deepen our friendship to a reasonable extent.]","Even when Eris tried probing her with those words, Cornelia remained calm. She wasn’t excessively excited, nor did she appear to be escaping from reality.","Eris began to think that perhaps she had been overthinking things. Convinced herself that whatever had felt strange was simply her imagination, she gave a faint smile.","[I see. To think you became close enough to address both of them by name before I even realized it. I must say, I’m impressed by you, Cornelia-sama. I would be too intimidated myself; even if the other party gave me permission, I think it would take quite a bit of resolve for me to actually call them by name.]","[......Call them by name...... Resolve...... Arehh? Come to think of it, I...... when did I......]","[U- Um? Cornelia-sama?]","[......W- Why did I speak to the two of them with such familiarity......? N- Not only that, I was overly familiar with Kaito-sama as well...... Eh? Arehh? ......N- No, but......]","It was a small trigger, but one that would inevitably lead to a situation she could no longer escape. Eris’s words made a tiny hole in Cornelia’s thoughts, like pricking a tightly stretched balloon with a small needle...... and the things she had unconsciously been pushing aside began surfacing in Cornelia’s mind one after another.","(What on earth had I done? I casually called Goddess of Fate-sama and World King-sama by their names simply because they themselves didn’t reprimand me, and I was acting far too familiar with Kaito-sama as well...... No, I even had such casual conversations with them that they could almost be called shameless......)","The events from Forest Castle, which had taken place only moments ago, came flooding back into her mind like a series of flashbacks. Under normal circumstances, Cornelia would have considered it far too presumptuous even to speak with Fate and Lillywood, yet she had actively initiated conversations with them herself and spoken with them. It was something the usual Cornelia would never have done.","Moreover, although she was the first-born daughter, she was not the heir to the Sharon County, and because of her position, she also had to take the circumstances of the County into consideration. Her value had already risen far too much due to her association with Kaito, leaving her troubled over the situation as it was. And now, to voluntarily plunge herself into an even more extraordinary realm on top of that, it was an utterly foolish act.","No, even then, it would have been fine if that were all. Those interactions had taken place strictly within the attraction, and fortunately, none of the other nobles had witnessed them. Of course, Cornelia would still have to worry about how she should handle her relationship with Fate and Lillywood from now on, but as long as Cornelia kept it to herself, it was something that would not become public.","(......Even if it was only a verbal promise, I said that if Kaito-sama invited me to accompany him when he attended a soirée, I would go with him? If Kaito-sama were to attend a soirée, he would attract an incredible amount of attention, and if I were to accompany him, it would reach a level where there would be no possible excuse, and people would assume that I held Kaito-sama’s affection...... N- No, not just that, what did I say? Shamelessly, I even asked Kaito-sama to teach me how to use the amusements from the otherworld...... Abababa......)","Reality had caught up with her. The effect of her invincible mode, which had been maintained by unconsciously excluding anything that might cause her stomach to hurt, had worn off, and what came rushing in were all the sources of stomachache she had been accumulating...... The color drained from Cornelia’s face to such an extent that it was obvious even to anyone watching from the outside, and sweat began pouring down her body.","[C- Cornelia-sama!? What happened!? Please, pull yourself together......]","[A- Awawawa, I- I- I, what have I...... Ababababa......]","[Cornelia-sama!? Her complexion is extremely abnormal...... Someone, find a place where she can rest!]","Seeing Cornelia begin trembling with a face so white that it seemed as though even the blood had completely drained from it, Eris hurriedly gave instructions to the servants nearby to secure a place where she could rest.","But even that was too late. Cornelia’s mind, completely overwhelmed by the torrent of information rushing through it, reached its limit...... and, as though a thread had suddenly snapped, she lost consciousness...... and Cornelia fainted while foaming at the mouth.","[Cornelia-sama!? This is...... Ah, c- could it be!? Until just now, she had been unconsciously diverting her thoughts away from it? If that’s the case...... Quickly arrange somewhere for her to rest, and contact the Sharon County. Cornelia-sama will probably be unable to continue going around the attractions, so make preparations for her to return home once she wakes up......]","Having realized the true nature of the strange feeling she had sensed from Cornelia earlier, Eris continued issuing instructions while carrying the unconscious Cornelia in her arms...... sincerely pitying Cornelia, who would likely be troubled by stomachaches for quite some time even after she woke up......","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Poor thing...... Still, when you see a scene like this, even though she also suffers her own stomachaches, Eris really is strong in her own way...... It’s like she has a lot of endurance...... That’s probably why she gets thrown into the Gods’ Festival, though......]"]},{"number":2621,"title":"Chapter 2621 - Re: Demon Realm Amusement Park 1","paragraphs":["If we were going around in order, the next area would be the Ice Area, which was presumably modeled after Isis-san, with its fantastical snow and ice. However, we had agreed to have lunch after visiting two areas, so we decided to eat lunch before that.","As a general rule, there were snack stalls featuring specialties from each area scattered all over the place. The Aqua Area had shops selling things like seafood skewers, while the Forest Area had shops selling fruit sticks and drinks made with Seal Fruits, among other things.","[Looking at the pamphlet, it seems the restaurants are around the outer perimeter of the Central Area.]","[Yeah. We’re planning to visit the Central Area last, but shall we go to the restaurant area around the perimeter?]","However, those kinds of establishments were basically intended for things like eating while walking around, so if we wanted to have a proper lunch, it seemed that the outer perimeter of the Central Area, which was called Gourmet Street, would be more suitable.","After discussing it, we decided to head there, making our way from the Forest Area toward the Central Area. That said, there were paths leading to the main Central Area from each of the other areas, and since the Gourmet Street was located along its outer perimeter, we arrived there fairly quickly.","[There sure are quite a lot of establishments here.]","[......There are some well-known restaurants, too. Perhaps they’re branches?]","[With a facility of this scale, they could expect quite a lot of sales, so I suppose it wouldn’t be strange for them to open branches here.]","Just as Lilia-san, Luna-san, and Sieg-san were looking around with interest, there really were all kinds of establishments. Some even looked like high-end restaurants, while others were more like fast-food places.","They probably weren’t quite large enough to be called chain restaurants, but there seemed to be branches of famous establishments as well, so there appeared to be far more options than I had expected.","[Hina-chan, what should we do?]","[Hmm~~ It’s hard to choose. But since we’ve come all this way, we’d want to go to a restaurant that’s unique to this amusement park, right?]","At present, Hina-chan was the one deciding the course of action for our group, and when Aoi-chan asked her...... Hina-chan folded her arms and looked quite troubled as she pondered the choice.","Indeed, there were a lot of options, and considering the Central Area’s outer perimeter covered quite a considerable distance, there must have been a substantial number of establishments.","However, considering that we still had other areas to visit, we didn’t have time to spend too long deciding. I wanted to make the decision as quickly as possible, but given Hina-chan’s current level of enthusiasm, there was also a possibility that she’d want to make a complete circuit of the outer perimeter before deciding.","[Hina-chan, apparently...... that restaurant over there has a park-exclusive parfait.]","[An exclusive parfait!? That’s the one! Let’s go there!!!]","Thus, I decided to play one of my cards specifically for dealing with Hina-chan. Hina-chan loved parfaits, and if it was an exclusive parfait that could only be eaten here, there was no way she’d pass it up.","And so, when I happened to spot the words “Park-Exclusive Parfait” at a stylish-looking restaurant in my line of sight and suggested it, the decision was made without a second thought.","None of the others seemed to have any objections either, so we headed toward the restaurant with the exclusive parfait. The interior had a somewhat fancy feel to it, but when you were told it was an amusement park restaurant, it certainly felt appropriate.","[Oh, the menu has pictures! Ah, this one is cute.]","Naturally, there wasn’t a table large enough for all of us to sit together, so, as usual, we split up and took our seats in groups: me, Aoi-chan, and Hina-chan; Lilia-san, Luna-san, and Sieg-san; and Anima, Caraway, Eta, and Theta.","Just as Hina-chan said, the menu at this restaurant used photographs, which were still quite expensive and far from commonplace since the magic tools hadn’t yet become widely available, making it very easy to look through.","They even had things like lunch plates modeled after the amusement park’s characters, making it practically a hundred out of a hundred as an amusement park restaurant...... No, it’s almost too perfect...... This might be a restaurant that Alice or Kuro is involved in running.","Kuro has her hand in trading companies, and Alice also has restaurants in various places. I’ve even gone on dates with them to some of them, so it wouldn’t be surprising if she had given them some advice.","[I think I’ll go with this chicken-based plate.]","[I’ll have this pasta...... What about you, Hina-chan?]","[I’ll have the amusement park plate with the limited-edition parfait!]","What I chose was a lunch plate centered around what looked like herb-roasted chicken, while Aoi-chan ordered cream and mushroom pasta. Hina-chan ordered a cute amusement park plate shaped like the mascot characters, along with the limited-edition parfait.","[I’m looking forward to it! I’ll give you a bite of the parfait too, Kaito-senpai and Aoi-senpai!]","[Unn? You’re okay with that?]","[Yes! After all, it’s more fun when you share delicious things with everyone! So let me have a bite of your chicken too, Kaito-senpai!]","[Ahaha, I see. Sure.]","[Thank you!]","She really was having a great time, or rather, seeing how happy Hina-chan was made me feel happy too. There was something childlike about her, but her cheerful and adorable demeanor was also strongly reminiscent of a small animal.","That said, well, when she moved around by bouncing up and down like that, her large breasts would sway quite a bit, so I do think it would be better if she didn’t move quite so vigorously up and down.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [This guy, he’s got the gall to have such a wholesome, fun time! There’s a certain count’s daughter whose stomach is being obliterated at this very moment, you know!?]"]},{"number":2622,"title":"Chapter 2622 - Re: Demon Realm Amusement Park 2","paragraphs":["When you think of a restaurant at an amusement park, the image that comes to mind is usually one that looks stylish and has high prices, but while the food at this restaurant was indeed a little more expensive than at ordinary restaurants, considering it was an amusement park restaurant, the prices were quite reasonable.","The food that came out was also quite high quality, and the plate I ordered was extremely delicious. Aoi-chan and I didn’t order dessert, but of course, Hina-chan ordered a parfait.","[Wooooah, this is amazing! It’s so colorful and looks delicious!]","[Since it has seven colors, or rather, seven layers, I guess it’s meant to represent the different areas of the amusement park?]","[The colors certainly make it look that way.]","As we watched Hina-chan’s eyes light up at the sight of the rather large parfait, Aoi-chan and I voiced our impressions of it. It was a stylish parfait divided into several layers, with colors that seemed to represent the different areas of the amusement park.","However, that aside...... it was huge. It was a size that I could hardly believe was meant for one person. Was she really going to be okay? At the very least, I had absolutely no confidence that I could finish this by myself.","[......Hina-chan, isn’t this thing ridiculously big?]","[It’s a big-size parfait! When something has a big visual impact like this, it really gets you excited just looking at it, doesn’t it?!]","[N- No, Hina-chan? Can you actually finish this?]","[It’ll be fine! I’ve eaten something even bigger than this all by myself before...... Ah, well, I’m definitely not gonna be fine calorie-wise, but I’ll make up for that by running a whole lot later.]","As I muttered, overwhelmed by its sheer size, Hina-chan actually responded as though she was delighted. Aoi-chan, who presumably had a similar reaction to mine, asked her worriedly, but Hina-chan replied with a bright smile that there was no problem.","She didn’t look like she was forcing herself and genuinely seemed to have no trouble with it, so...... when it came to parfaits, I decided to assume that Hina-chan had a separate stomach from her normal one.","[Mmm~~ It’s delicious! The whipped cream is incredibly fine and the texture is amazing!]","Hina-chan immediately started eating her parfait, and after taking a bite, she seemed to really like it, making an expression that showed just how delicious she found it.","As I watched her fondly, after eating several bites, Hina-chan turned her gaze toward me and cheerfully held out her spoon.","[Kaito-senpai, you should try some too! It’s delicious!]","[Eh? Ah, errr......]","[Come on, don’t be shy! Have some!]","Well, I didn’t mind getting some of her parfait, but...... there was only one spoon, and the spoon Hina-chan was currently scooping the parfait with and holding out to me was the very same spoon she’d been eating with until just now.","Wouldn’t that make it an indirect kiss? Hina-chan didn’t seem to care about that at all though, and was actually urging me to hurry up. It felt like her excitement had gone completely off the charts from having two things she loved, amusement parks and parfaits, come together.","Well, if Hina-chan didn’t have a problem with it, then I figured it was fine, so I let her feed me some of the parfait sitting on the spoon she held out.","[Unn. It really does have a nice texture, or rather, it’s delicious in a way that almost makes it melt right in your mouth.]","[Right?! It’s really high quality! Ah, Aoi-senpai, you should have some too!]","[Thank you. I have a teaspoon, so I’ll use this to have some.]","Aoi-chan and I hadn’t ordered dessert, but we’d each ordered tea and coffee after the meal. Since Aoi-chan had ordered tea, she had a teaspoon, which she used to eat some of the parfait.","Since I’d ordered black coffee because it was after the meal, I didn’t have anything like a teaspoon.","[Ehehe, I’ll give you some again when I get to the next layer!]","[Ahaha, thanks. But Hina-chan, don’t rush and just take your time eating.]","[Okay! But it’s so delicious that I just can’t help picking up the pace.]","With her cheeks slightly flushed, perhaps because she was so excited, Hina-chan wore a huge smile, looking as adorable as ever in that small-animal sort of way.","Even through Sympathy Magic, I could feel her emotions screaming that she was having the time of her life, so there was something about her that made me want to pat her on the head. Well, patting her head while she was eating a parfait would probably just get in the way, so I managed to restrain myself......","[Oh, this layer has ramune-flavored jelly. Here, here, Kaito-senpai, you should try some too! Here you go.]","[Hm? Ah, thanks.]","I accepted another helping of parfait that she held out to me. Since it was already the second time, I felt like I naturally let her feed it to me.","Her excitement really was at MAX, and as I wondered if this was what it would be like to have a little sister, I watched Hina-chan happily and fondly, occasionally letting her feed me another helping of parfait.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Ghaak...... W- What?! No, no, that’s not it, Kaito! She’s probably aware of it and conscious of it too!!! She’s shamelessly going for the “Aaah~~” because she sees this as the perfect opportunity...... Hina, what a terrifying girl......]"]},{"number":2623,"title":"Chapter 2623 - Re: Demon Realm Amusement Park 3","paragraphs":["To my eyes, it was quite a large parfait, but Hina-chan happily ate the entire thing from start to finish, reminding me once again of the saying that there is always room for dessert.","Well, even so, after finishing it all, she said “But it was a little big”, which made me think she still had plenty of cuteness left in her.","At the very least, compared to Alice’s strong-arm style of pushing the restaurant’s inventory to its limits, she seemed completely normal.","In any case, we finished our meal at the restaurant and once again made our way to the Ice Area. This was, well, completely in line with what one would imagine, a snow and ice area, with buildings and paths that looked as though they were made of ice, snow piled up here and there, and scenery that was easy to picture from its name, yet still had a rather fantastical and dreamlike atmosphere.","The buildings looked like ice, but they weren’t actually made of ice; they merely had that sort of appearance.","[They sure have made quite the effort into every area.]","[Indeed. Just looking around gets me excited...... So, Hina-chan, which attraction should we go to here?]","[Hmm, I think this Ice Mirror Labyrinth would be good. It’s easy to imagine what it’s like, isn’t it?]","[Ah, yeah. Judging by the name, it sounds like a maze lined with mirrors, and it seems like it’d be fun.]","Rather than simply being easy to imagine, it was the sort of attraction that seemed like it would be found at an amusement park...... Though the amusement parks I went to as a child didn’t have anything like a mirror maze.","Still, the idea of a mirror labyrinth inside an ice-like building fit the fantastical atmosphere of the Ice Area quite well and seemed like it would be fun.","I checked with everyone else as well, but no one seemed to have any objections, so we decided to go to the Ice Mirror Labyrinth first.","When we arrived, it was a fairly large building, and if the maze was actually that large, it might be pretty difficult...... Ah, no, there was also the possibility that it was simply large because, like Forest Castle, multiple groups could progress through it simultaneously.","When we went inside, there was a beautiful reception area that looked like a hotel lobby, and...... I wonder what that is? I noticed a lot of what looked like portraits hanging along the walls.","[......What are those paintings?]","[They have kind of an eerie atmosphere to them.]","Aoi-chan tilted her head as she looked at the portraits, while Hina-chan murmured that the paintings were creepy. Now that she mentioned it, they did seem somewhat eerie...... They were definitely portraits, but there was something about their coloring that was somewhat dark.","There was no consistency among the people depicted. There were men and women, people who looked like Humans and people who looked like Demons, all sorts of different people.","Wondering about them, we went to the reception desk and learned that this attraction was structured like a maze where participants had to reach the goal in pairs of two. As expected, multiple pairs could start simultaneously.","The pairs could either be decided beforehand, or they could be randomly assigned during teleportation, like in Forest Castle. Since there were ten of us, we would be divided into five pairs, so we decided to have the pairs assigned randomly and all stepped onto the magic circle.","We were enveloped in a dazzling light and teleported to what appeared to be the starting room...... and I immediately spotted Hina-chan nearby.","[Ah, Kaito-senpai! We’re positioned together!]","[Looks like it. Let’s do our best.]","[Yes! Let’s do our best together!]","It seems I’ve ended up paired with Hina-chan, meaning the two of us would be taking on the mirror labyrinth together...... At the starting point, this room had something that looked like a magic tool in the center, with the words “Please touch this first” written on it, and beyond that was a large door and...... a single stylish lantern.","[......Are we supposed to touch it?]","[Probably the rules and such will be explained.]","[I see, then I’ll touch it!]","When Hina-chan touched the thing that looked like a magic tool...... some rather ominous music began to play, followed by an eerie voice.","“......This is a labyrinth inhabited by a terrifying mirror monster. So far, 43 souls have been dragged into the mirrors, and even now, those souls continue to wander within them. The portraits at the entrance to this labyrinth belonged to the victims of the past. I was tasked with exterminating the mirror monster...... but if someone is listening to this recording I have left behind, then I must have become its 44 victim as well. You have been deceived by the mirror monster and brought here. So that whoever is listening to this does not become its next victim, I shall leave behind all the information I know...... Please, those of you listening to this, escape the mirror labyrinth safely.”","Hmm~~ Arehh? This introduction is kind of different from what I expected...... No, I imagined we’d be tackling a maze, but the atmosphere is different, or rather......","[U- Umm, K- Kaito-senpai...... I- Is this, perhaps...... one of those scary ones......?]","[Unn. It feels like...... some kind of panic horror attraction, where we have to escape while avoiding this mirror monster......]","The introduction was completely that of a horror attraction, and there was no doubt that this was the type it was going to be. Sure, when I first saw the area divisions, I’d predicted that the Dark Area would have haunted houses and things like that, but each area was huge, so it wasn’t strange for there to be horror attractions in other areas as well.","Maybe I should have suspected something when the entrance already had such an eerie atmosphere...... In any case, this seemed to be an attraction quite different from what I’d imagined, but I wondered what it would actually be like......","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [S- So, if it’s a horror-type attraction, then there’s at least a slight possibility of it being serious......]","? ? ? : [Of course it’s serious.]","Serious-senpai : [Eh? C- Can I really expect a serious development this time?]","? ? ? : [Yes, by all means, expect a lot. You can have seconds of plot development, too.]","Serious-senpai : [O- Oh......]","? ? ? : [Don’t hold back. Let’s expect everything that we’ve been missing out on until now, too!]","Serious-senpai : [Fortune has come from such an unexpected place...... At long last, my time has come......]","? ? ? : [....................]","Serious-senpai : [I thought being alone with the timid kouhai in a horror attraction was going to be the setup for a lovey-dovey event, but the heck, it’s that classic pattern where everything takes an unexpected turn!]","? ? ? : [.......................................]","Serious-senpai : [I wholeheartedly welcome this kind of surprise! Now, let’s get this torrent of serious developments underway!]","? ? ? : [From this moment onward, the lovey-dovey event shall begin!!!]","Serious-senpai : [I knew it! Godd*mmit!!!]"]},{"number":2624,"title":"Chapter 2624 - Re: Demon Realm Amusement Park 4","paragraphs":["The Ice Mirror Labyrinth that I had chosen, thinking it would be an attraction like a mirror maze, was more or less what I had expected, though it seemed to have had horror elements added to it.","It didn’t seem like the kind of attraction where we simply made our way through the maze and called it a day, so for now, I decided to listen to the explanation.","“The mirror monster captures its prey and drags them into the mirror. Once that happens, there is no means of escape, but while the mirror monster possesses tremendous power inside mirrors, it cannot wield much power outside of them. Therefore, it cannot drag its prey into a mirror unless it touches its prey three times.”","This was probably an explanation of the number of lives we had. In other words, if we failed to deal with some action from the mirror monster three times, it would be game over.","Conversely, that meant it was okay to fail twice...... Once again, it seemed like the objective wasn’t simply to run away, but to actually do something.","“The mirror monster approaches from within the mirrors. At times it will conceal its form, and at times it will change its appearance...... Find the abnormalities within the mirrors. And once you find the mirror monster, point the Holy Lantern toward the mirror in which the mirror monster is hiding and press the Holy Stone on the handle. Doing so will cause holy light to be emitted from the lantern, driving away the mirror monster. But be careful...... Once the Holy Lantern’s light is used, it cannot be used again for 20 seconds. Be certain to point it toward the mirror in which the monster is hiding. We wish you the best of luck.”","I see, so the lantern placed beside that door was the equipment we were supposed to use to clear the attraction...... I could more or less picture how it worked. It was probably structured like a mirror maze, with mirrors in every direction. As we proceeded, some kind of abnormality, some behavior that would be impossible for an ordinary mirror, would occur somewhere among them, and we would have to identify it and drive it away with the lantern as we continued onward.","There was a 20-second interval so that we couldn’t just shine the light at mirrors indiscriminately...... In that case, was it possible that later on there would be things like feints?","For example, perhaps the monster would immediately move from the mirror where we first noticed something strange to another mirror, and we would ultimately have to shine the light on the mirror it had moved to. Something like that seemed possible.","[......D- Do you think this is the kind where something scary suddenly appears in the mirrors?]","[I feel like it would be more like there’s something there meant to startle us.]","[Uuuuugh, I- I’ll tell you this because you’re Kaito-senpai, but...... I- I’m actually pretty bad with scary things......]","She said it as though she were confessing some hidden secret, but I already knew, or rather, had realized that Hina-chan wasn’t good with scary things.","That said, in Hina-chan’s case, it wasn’t that she absolutely hated scary things and didn’t even want them in her field of vision. I think she was the type who was bad with scary things, but...... if there happened to be a haunted house, she’d still go inside at least once anyway.","[I’m not particularly good with them either, but it’s fortunate that there are two of us instead of just one.]","[T- That’s true. If I were alone, I might have given up...... I wonder if we’re even allowed to give up?]","[I wonder? I’m pretty sure we can if we really want to, but...... Oh?]","There were probably people who were genuinely terrible with scary things, so I figured it should be possible to give up. As I approached the lantern, however...... I noticed something resembling a notice posted on the door.","“Caution: Horror elements are present beyond this point. Those with weak hearts or who are extremely uncomfortable with horror may place the lantern on the table in the center to exit the attraction. Additionally, if you wish to retire while challenging the attraction, turn the handle on the bottom of the lantern clockwise twice. The lantern’s light will go out, and you will be returned to the reception desk.”","Ahh, so there really is a means of escape, or rather, a way to retire partway through. I think she’ll be fine, but if Hina-chan seems to be reaching her limit, we’ll consider retiring. I’m neither particularly good nor particularly bad with horror, so I don’t think I’ll have a problem.","[Looks like we can leave partway through, so if it gets too scary to handle, we’ll just retire.]","[O- Okay. I’ll do my best for as long as I can...... Ah, K- Kaito-senpai...... c- can I hold your hand?]","[Sure. Then let’s hold hands and go together.]","[Yes!]","For now, I decided to carry the lantern myself, and held out my free hand toward the frightened Hina-chan and took her hand. From the feeling of her hand in mine, I could tell that she was pretty tense, or rather, trembling with fear.","......I’m still fine with the scary stuff, but if they try to startle us with something like a sudden loud noise, even I might jump...... If possible, I don’t want to show my cute kouhai such an embarrassing side of myself, but who knows how it’ll turn out......","[Okay, let’s go.]","[Y- Yes.]","When we opened the door and stepped outside the room...... it was indeed a maze made of mirrors, but since it was a horror attraction, it was rather dim.","That said, it wasn’t so dark that we couldn’t see our surroundings. If I had to compare it to something, it was about as dark as being in the shade during the daytime, so there was absolutely no problem seeing the path and such.","[Eek!? K- K- K- Kaito-senpai! T- The mirror in front......]","[Hm? Ah, I see, so this is how it works......]","Responding to Hina-chan’s frightened voice, I looked ahead and saw something resembling a purple haze behind the reflections of me and Hina-chan in the mirror directly in front of us.","Thinking about it from a meta perspective, this was probably something like a tutorial. The proof was that it was so blatantly obvious.","For now, I raised the lantern toward the mirror in front of us and pressed the stone on the handle...... the switch. The lantern shone brilliantly, and the purple haze vanished with an eerie scream.","[D- Did you beat it?]","[They said it would drive it away, so I don’t think we actually defeated it. It’ll probably show up again further ahead, so we’ll have to keep an eye on the mirrors around us.]","[Uuuuugh, p- please make it only mildly scary.]","I smiled reassuringly at Hina-chan as she squeezed my hand tightly and pressed herself against me, apparently out of fear, then took a step toward the mirror maze.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [T- The flag for her getting scared and clinging to him is standing loud and clear......]"]},{"number":2625,"title":"Chapter 2625 - Re: Demon Realm Amusement Park 5","paragraphs":["The basic premise of this attraction is to make your way through the maze while fending off attacks from mirror monsters, but I think the first one, which was obviously easy to spot, was basically a tutorial, so I get the impression that the difficulty is going to start increasing from here.","[They said something about not overlooking anything out of place during the initial explanation, right?]","[Y- Yeah. I guess that means something strange is going to show up in the mirrors, even if it’s not as blatantly obvious as the one before?]","[That’s probably it, but I think it’d be too harsh if a tiny discrepancy meant you were immediately out just because you missed it once, so maybe they approach in several stages...... Ah, but on the other hand, if there’s a major discrepancy, maybe missing it means you’re immediately out for one attempt.]","This is, after all, just an amusement park attraction, and it’s not some sort of hidden route in Forest Castle, so the difficulty should basically be set at a level where you can clear it if you just play normally.","So, for example, it shouldn’t be so difficult that there’s an incredibly tiny discrepancy in the mirror that you can only notice if you look carefully, and missing it means you’re out for one attempt.","However, considering that you’re out after three mistakes...... and that you’re safe even if you miss something twice, I think it probably focuses mainly on easy-to-spot discrepancies, with some slightly more difficult ones mixed in from time to time.","For the time being though, Hina-chan is pretty scared, so it’ll probably be difficult for her to calmly spot anything out of place. If possible, I want to do my best here and make sure I’m the one who notices them.","With that in mind, I took another look around the mirror maze...... Basically, the parts that were mirrors were the sections corresponding to the walls. The floor wasn’t mirrored, and the ceiling was too dim to see, but at least it didn’t seem to be a mirror either.","In that case, unless we were at a corner or a dead end, the things we needed to pay attention to were the mirrors on both sides as we moved forward.","[......Hina-chan, it’s been about 20 seconds since the first one, so something could happen at any moment. Watch out.]","[Y- Yes......]","The Holy Lantern’s interval is 20 seconds, so now that it’s available for use again, an attack from a mirror monster could happen at any moment.","However, there was no point in stopping and waiting, so we cautiously continued through the maze. Even without constantly turning my head to look, the mirrors on either side were within the edges of my vision, so if there was any major discrepancy, I should be able to notice it......","Just as I was thinking that, I caught a glimpse out of the corner of my eye of my face reflected in the mirror on our right suddenly swiveling around to look directly at us.","[Hyaaaah!?]","[ ! ? ]","As I felt Hina-chan leap onto my arm with a scream, I pointed the lantern at the mirror on the right and used it. A scream just like the one from before rang out, and black mist emerged from my body reflected in the mirror before fleeing into the depths of the mirror.","T- That startled me...... Having the me inside the mirror suddenly move differently from the me on this side really was exactly what you’d expect from a horror attraction. But I see, so they can also disguise themselves as our reflections in the mirrors......","[Hina-chan, are you okay?]","[T- T- T- That was scary...... C- Coming at me all of a sudden like that, isn’t that cheating!?]","[That surprised me too. It really caught me completely off guard......]","Hina-chan was trembling slightly and her voice was somewhat tearful, so it was clear that she must have been pretty scared, and I could understand how she felt since that startled me quite a bit too.","However, the way she was tightly clinging to my arm was somewhat problematic, or rather...... My arm was currently sandwiched between Hina-chan’s ample breasts, making it difficult for me to stay calm.","Of course, from Hina-chan’s perspective, she was desperately clinging to my arm because it was the arm of someone she felt close to, trying to escape the fear of the horror attraction she was bad with, so I couldn’t really blame her.","That said, I was having a hard time keeping calm myself, or rather, considering how tightly she was hugging me, we were pressed together so closely that it was practically impossible for me not to be conscious of it.","However, that didn’t mean I could tell a frightened Hina-chan to move away from me, and besides...... it didn’t look like she was going to let go anytime soon.","But if things continued like this, I was going to be far too conscious of the sensation I’m feeling from my arm...... S- So, for now, I’ll just casually suggest it......","[......Hina-chan. Um, I don’t think there’ll be another attack for another 20 seconds, and I think it’ll be difficult for both of us to walk like this, so for now, maybe we should......]","[I- I- I- Is staying like this...... no good? I- I’ll be careful so that Kaito-senpai can walk properly...... I- It’s just...... I’m scared right now, so I don’t really want to let go......]","[U- Unn. If you’re okay with it, Hina-chan, then it’s fine.]","......No good. If she pleaded with me with eyes that teary, there was no way I could tell her to let go of my arm. Considering Hina-chan’s state of mind, I suppose it would be best to continue like this, with her clinging to my arm......","For now, all I had to do was stop thinking about anything weird and focus properly on keeping an eye on our surroundings. I’d just have to consider the concentration I was losing because of the softness and warmth I could feel against my arm as the price I had to pay to make Hina-chan feel safe.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Guh...... I knew this was coming, but the damage...... Unlike when Lilia once clung to his arm, there’s none of that gag-like element where it felt like she was about to crush the bones in his arm, so this feels way more lovey-dovey......]"]},{"number":2626,"title":"Chapter 2626 - Re: Demon Realm Amusement Park 6","paragraphs":["This place was quite elaborate. I mean, there was more of an unexpected scariness to it than I had anticipated, and Hina-chan, who was bad with scary things, was completely frightened, to the point that she was clinging to my arm.","Even so, she never said anything like “Let’s give up” or “I can’t go any further”. If anything, even when she was frightened, she seemed to be enjoying herself.","[Are you okay, Hina-chan?]","[It’s scary...... B- But, I’m also curious about what it’s going to be like further ahead.]","[Well, yeah. It does seem pretty elaborate, so I am curious about how it’s going to attack us next.]","[Yes...... I’d prefer it if they kept the startling stuff to a minimum though......]","Despite repeatedly saying how scary it was, she’s got the same state of mind as those watching a horror movie all the way to the end or making it through a haunted house while screaming...... There was no doubt that she was scared, but she seemed to have accepted even things like being startled from unexpected places as part of the appeal of horror attractions.","Even though Hina-chan was trembling with fear while clinging to my arm, she would move along with me whenever I moved, so we continued through the maze together...... And, as expected, after walking for a little while, we reached a fork in the path.","[......A fork in the path.]","[This place doesn’t have a time limit, and it’s not like we absolutely have to choose the right path...... but I feel like there might be an attack if we reach a dead end.]","[R- Right. Since they come from inside the mirrors, I don’t think they’d come from behind us, but if it’s a dead end, there would be three mirrors, one in front and one on either side.]","[Unn. But well, there’s no point in thinking about it too much. Which way do you want to go? You can choose, Hina-chan.]","If I chose randomly, I would probably end up taking the correct path, and that would cut the fun of the maze in half. In that case, I decided to let Hina-chan choose the path.","After looking thoughtful for a moment, Hina-chan pointed toward the path on the right, so we proceeded that way.","[It feels like there’s been a bit of a gap since the last one appeared.]","[......I- I wonder when it’ll come? M- Maybe something has already happened without us noticing......]","That certainly wasn’t impossible. The previous one had been an obvious anomaly, but there was a possibility that a smaller anomaly had appeared.","For example, the mirror monster we could see in the depths of the mirror, about the size of a tiny bean, might be gradually getting closer as we progressed, or something like that could also appear...... Just as I had that thought, I held the lantern up to the mirror on the left and pushed a stone in. Immediately afterward, we heard the mirror monster let out a scream.","[Eh? W- Was it there just now?]","[Unn. I don’t know how long it had been there, but...... the color of the clothes on my reflection in the left mirror had started looking kind of blue.]","[I- I didn’t notice it at all.]","[Maybe it has been changing gradually? It might have started turning a little bluer from black, and then once it had completely changed to blue, it would attack us.]","Just as Hina-chan hadn’t noticed, this one had been quite difficult, or rather...... I didn’t even know at what point the color had changed.","However, when I looked at the mirror on the left, my clothes somehow looked more indigo than black, so I treated that as an anomaly and used the lantern.","[Come to think of it, are most of them cases where there’s some kind of change in what’s reflected in the mirrors?]","[It’s easier to notice when something other than us is reflected in the mirror, so I feel like there have been a lot of cases like that. K- Kaito-senpai, I’m counting on you! I’m too scared to really look closely at the mirrors...... I- It’d be scary if the faces in the mirror suddenly turned my way or something......S- So, please don’t expect too much from me as far as being useful.]","[It’s okay. It’s more than enough if you tell me whenever you happen to notice something. I’ll keep a close eye on things, so I’ll do my best to protect you properly, Hina-chan.]","I knew Hina-chan was absolutely terrified, so even though she said not to expect her to be useful in combat, I was grateful that she still paid some attention to the mirrors and cooperated.","I was fairly fine with the scary stuff, aside from the sudden-jump-scare type...... and while part of me wanted to look good in front of my cute kouhai who was relying on me, I answered as reassuringly and dependably as I could.","[K- Kaito-senpai...... One hundred points. That was a perfect response. You really are quite the lady-killer.]","[......I can’t tell whether you’re complimenting me or insulting me...... But in a situation like this, saying “I’ll definitely protect you” would be worth a hundred points, wouldn’t it?]","[Hmmm, I wonder? Personally, rather than someone confidently saying something without any basis to back it up, I prefer it when they say something like they’ll do their best within the limits of what they can actually accomplish. Ah, but I guess it also depends on how much you trust the other person, doesn’t it? If Kaito-senpai said you’d definitely protect me, I could honestly believe you...... I guess that’s what they call trust and track record? Kaito-senpai protected me when I was attacked by a Black Bear too......]","[Ahaha, though in reality, I couldn’t do anything and just got beaten up.]","[......But Kaito-senpai back then...... to me, you were the coolest person in the world.]","Perhaps Hina-chan’s bashful smile was dazzling, or perhaps I was simply embarrassed, but I gave an awkward chuckle while turning my face slightly away.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Oi, mirror monster! What are you doing? Attack these two while they’re flirting!!!]","? ? ? : [Wouldn’t that just make them flirt even more?]","Serious-senpai : [......So either way, it’s an out huh...... D*mn it! Actually, now that I think about it, including everything up to this point, Hina’s opinion of Kaito ever since the Rigforeshia incident has basically been consistently “reliable and cool”...... I knew that already, but this kouhai really does have a pretty high level of affection for him......]"]},{"number":2627,"title":"Chapter 2627 - Re: Demon Realm Amusement Park 7","paragraphs":["Hina-chan’s chosen path continued for a while, but unfortunately, we ended up reaching a dead end.","[Ah, it’s a dead end. I’m sorry.]","[No, no, it’d be stranger to get through a maze without reaching a single dead end, so it’s not something you need to apologize for, Hina-chan. Just be careful...... it’s probably coming.]","[Y- Yeah. It’s coming, right?]","Reaching a dead end wasn’t a problem. There was no particular penalty, and when entering a maze for the first time, it was practically inevitable that we’d run into a few dead ends.","However, considering the concept of this attraction, I couldn’t imagine the mirror monster not appearing at this particular moment. No, conversely, maybe they’d anticipate participants thinking that it would appear here and try to outwit them by going one level beyond that...... No, I don’t think they’d make it that complicated. In places where you’d probably think it was going to appear, I think it’d just appear normally.","With that thought in mind, I kept an eye on the mirror directly in front of us at the dead end, as well as the mirrors to our left and right...... When I thought I saw a black haze reflected in the mirror directly ahead for just an instant, the mirror monster appeared.","[Hyaaahhh!?]","This time, the mirror monster’s appearance was clearly visible. With bulging eyes, disheveled hair, exposed sharp fangs, and an overall aura reminiscent of a yamauba, it looked quite terrifying, and Hina-chan screamed and leaped at me.","I was slightly startled by the soft sensation, but I immediately held up the lantern toward the front and tried to press the stone in...... However, the mirror monster moved to the mirror on the left even faster.","[Eh? It moved?]","I hurriedly pointed the lantern toward the mirror on the left, only for it to return to the mirror directly ahead...... So it was going for feints...... If I fell for it and used the lantern, there’d be a cooldown before I could use it again, and it would attack during that opening......","The mirror monster moved swiftly between the mirrors in front, to the left, and to the right, and even if I reacted after seeing it, by the time I pointed the lantern at it, it had already moved to another mirror.","......No, but considering that this is an attraction, there must be a way to repel it...... Panicking would mean losing here. I need to carefully observe its movements.","Though I was being toyed with by its rapid movements, I remained on high alert. After moving several times, the mirror monster that had moved to the mirror directly ahead suddenly stopped, so I quickly held up the lantern and pressed the stone in. With a scream, the mirror monster disappeared.","I see. After moving around for a certain amount of time, it stops for a fixed period, so if you’re overwhelmed by the impact of it suddenly appearing right at the start and use the lantern immediately, you’d end up failing.","[Hina-chan, it’s okay now.]","[I- I- I- I was so scared! It had such a scary face......]","[Yeah, it did have a pretty startling appearance, especially if it suddenly came right up close to you.]","It certainly had an imposing appearance, kind of like a yamauba, but if we were talking about sheer scariness, I felt that the dimensional beasts from Gluttony-san’s place were probably scarier.","Well, anyway, we’d managed to repel it, so there was no problem.","[......Hina-chan, errr, it’s about time you......]","[Eh? Ah, s- sorry!]","[No, you were startled because it came at you so suddenly, so it’s understandable.]","Since Hina-chan was currently clinging to me from the side, I gently pointed it out, and Hina-chan hurriedly pulled away from me, her cheeks turning red with embarrassment. However, perhaps because she was still scared, after separating from me once, she hugged my arm again, wrapping both arms around it.","Of course, I don’t dislike being hugged itself. I’m a man too, and if a beautiful girl like Hina-chan were to hug me, I’d actually be happy about it. Given the circumstances, I suppose you could even call it a fortunate turn of events.","However, if possible, I don’t want to make a sloppy-looking face. Right now, well, how should I put it...... unless I’m being conceited, I think she sees me as a kind, dependable senpai, so there’s a part of me that wants to keep up that good image and doesn’t want to ruin it.","That said, acting all cool isn’t really my character, so I’d like to behave as naturally as possible, without consciously thinking about it.","No, it’s impossible not to be conscious of it at all when she’s already hugging my arm...... but I’d like to maintain the image of a cool senpai as much as I can.","[Anyway, once we get past this attack, it doesn’t look like there’ll be another one until we return to the fork in the path, so shall we head back?]","[Yes. That said, I didn’t expect it to use feints like that.]","[It actually has quite a variety of tricks, doesn’t it? I thought disguising itself as me or you was probably its main gimmick, but I didn’t expect it to actually show itself and then throw us off with its speed......]","[Do you think we could have defeated it without letting it move if we’d immediately used Body Reinforcement or something to quickly point the lantern at it and press the stone?]","[Hmmm, no matter how quickly you point it or press it, there’s still a slight delay between pressing the stone and the lantern lighting up, so putting it in meta terms, if it was designed to move in response to the action of pressing the stone, then it might not have been possible.]","The mirror monster’s movements just now were ultimately an attraction gimmick, so I couldn’t imagine that it had been designed to be overcome simply by brute-forcing it with physical abilities. Or rather, with Alice supervising it, she’d obviously have taken measures to prevent something like that.","That’s why, I think the mirror monster was designed to stop after moving several times...... Even if you pressed the stone on the lantern somewhere other than the intended point for defeating it, it would probably move to another mirror before the lantern could emit its light.","[......You could at least be a little more conscious of them though......]","[Unn? Hina-chan, what did you just say?]","[Ah, errr, it’s nothing! Let’s go back!!!]","[Eh? U- Unn.]","Hina-chan had muttered something in a quiet voice, but I couldn’t make out what she’d said, so I tried asking her about it, but she just smiled and said it was nothing before tightly hugging my arm.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Guaaahhh, t- this is...... It’s not something she’s doing as part of some strategy, but an impulsive hug because she was genuinely scared and it just happened by chance. And yet, at the same time, there’s this maiden’s heart that feels a little dissatisfied that he’s not conscious of her at all...... Guh!?]","? ? ? : [......Are you some kind of love expert?]"]},{"number":2628,"title":"Chapter 2628 - Re: Demon Realm Amusement Park 8","paragraphs":["As we continued through the Mirror Labyrinth, we managed to fend off several attacks from the mirror monsters and have been making fairly good progress. It is an attraction with horror elements, but rather than horror being the main focus like in a haunted house, it has more of the atmosphere of an attraction that happens to include horror-themed effects.","In fact, even the attacks by the mirror monsters have quite a wide variety to them: some are meant to startle you, some are eerie or frightening, some use feints to confuse you, and others are more like quizzes, such as the color of their clothes slowly changing. Overall, it doesn’t feel like it’s entirely focused on horror.","[B- But we’ve made quite a bit of progress, right? A- Are we still far from the goal?]","Though Hina-chan has been progressing perfectly well while being scared of absolutely everything, or rather, her reactions are big every time, and she seems to be enjoying the attraction with all her heart.","Incidentally, the previous attack involved the face of a mirror monster suddenly appearing in an extreme close-up on the mirror the instant you turned around, so she is currently hugging my arm tightly and seems to be on high alert.","[Hmm, I don’t think it’s probably that big of a maze. I mean, if a huge number of people could progress through it simultaneously like in Forest Castle, then sure, but this attraction is designed for two people at a time...... Since we were able to go together, even if 10 people can go through at once, it’s still being operated as a theme park attraction. And since the maze itself isn’t the main focus of the attraction, I don’t think it’s all that large.]","[......That’s true. There were several forks in the path, but whenever we took a wrong turn, we reached a dead end pretty quickly, so they were fairly easy to understand.]","[Unn. The attacks from the mirror monsters are also, in the end, pretty easy to figure out, so they shouldn’t have designed this as a high-difficulty attraction...... When you think about it that way, I feel like we should be reaching the goal soon.]","To put it bluntly, this attraction isn’t very difficult. Part of that may be because the previous attraction was Forest Castle, but what you have to do here is simple, and most of the abnormalities with the mirror monsters are easy to notice, so there aren’t many things that are particularly easy to overlook.","The feints where they move between mirrors can be a little tricky, but even those leave themselves exposed in an obvious opening after moving a few times...... so I think it was designed to be clearable even by relatively young children.","Naturally, that means the maze itself shouldn’t be all that difficult either, and we’ve already made a fair amount of progress...... We’ve also driven off the mirror monsters around 10 times by now, so I don’t think it would be strange for us to reach the goal soon.","As we continued moving while talking about that, Hina-chan suddenly came to a stop.","[......Hina-chan?]","[It’s almost about to end huh...... Kaito-senpai! W- What do you think? Don’t you think this would be a good time to do that capable-man move where you put your arm around the shoulder of your frightened kouhai and reassure her?]","[......U- Unn?]","She had suddenly started saying something strange, but judging from her expression and tone...... it seemed like she had decided to take some sort of plunge because the attraction was almost over.","Maybe it was one of those situations she’d always dreamed of and had naturally hoped would happen by now, but since it hadn’t, she had given up waiting and was directly asking for it...... Well, whatever the case......","[I mean...... putting aside all the other reasons, if I want to put my arm around the shoulder of Hina-chan while you’re clinging to my right arm, I’d need about one more right arm to make that work......]","[Huh!? T- There’s that’s the blind spot!? N- No wonder it never turned into that kind of situation......]","That’s right. Regardless of whether I’d actually been trying to make it happen or not, in order to create that situation where I put my arm around Hina-chan’s shoulders and reassure her...... it would be impossible unless Hina-chan, who had been clinging to my right arm practically since the beginning, let go at least once.","There was no way I could put my left arm around Hina-chan’s shoulder while she was clinging to my right arm...... in the first place, I was holding a lantern in my left hand.","[......Errr, would you rather we did it that way?]","[Honestly, I’ve always kind of dreamed about doing something like that...... so if you’re okay with it, Kaito-senpai, I’d like to try it at least once......]","[I’m fine with it, but are you sure you’re okay with it, Hina-chan?]","[Kaito-senpai can be incredibly dense at certain key moments, so I’ll say this just in case...... I wouldn’t be clinging to the arm of a member of the opposite sex that I didn’t have any feelings for in the first place, you know?]","The line was far more straightforward than I had expected, and I couldn’t help but feel my heart skip a beat. However, if there was one thing I had to argue against...... I thought Hina-chan was actually pretty dense herself.","I could somehow tell from her behavior up until now, as well as the emotions conveyed through Sympathy Magic, but I got the impression that Hina-chan was being affectionate towards me as more like my little sister, not really being conscious of me as a member of the opposite sex...... But it wasn’t as though I didn’t see Hina-chan, who was cute and quite physically affectionate, as a member of the opposite sex at all. If anything, I sometimes had to consciously keep my expression under control so that my face wouldn’t slacken when she clung to my arm.","W- Well, regardless. Since this was a request from Hina-chan herself, I might as well grant her wish......","“Ahahahaha.”","[Hyiih!?]","At the sudden sound of laughter, Hina-chan let out a shriek and clung to me. I hurriedly checked the mirrors around us, but...... there was nothing particularly strange about them. However, the laughter continued to reach our ears.","[K- Kaito-senpai, what do you think that is......?]","[There’s nothing reflected in the mirrors...... It feels like we’re only hearing the voice? For now, let’s proceed while staying alert.]","[Y- Yes!]","Keeping an eye on the surrounding mirrors in case something suddenly changed, we continued forward, and with every step we took, the laughter grew louder and louder.","This was probably...... no, almost certainly the laughter of the mirror monster...... but what was going to happen?","As I continued forward while wondering about that, we eventually arrived in an unusually spacious room. It was circular, and naturally, every wall was covered in mirrors...... Square mirrors were arranged in a circle, and there must have been several dozen of them.","[......There’s no exit?]","[It...... really doesn’t feel like a dead end though? Something’s going to happen——— Ah!?]","As we cautiously entered the room, the path we had just come through was blocked by a mirror that rose up from the ground.","“Ahahahahahahahahahaha!”","Based on what I had expected, we should have been nearing the goal. A room surrounded by a huge number of mirrors, the laughter of the mirror monster, our retreat cut off...... Arehh? Is this, perhaps...... the start of some kind of boss battle?","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [W- Well done, Mirror Monster! You actually stopped the lovey-dovey development!! You’re my only ally!!!]","Mirror Monster : [No, that situation isn’t good. It’s too sudden, and it would be more of a case of being swept along by the circumstances...... I do think that’s another valid form of it, and there are situations where that kind of thing can be delicious. But if we’re talking about truly intense lovey-dovey romance, I want drama and a beautiful finish. Here, I’d like to set up a situation where the two of them have to face a difficult challenge together, deepen their bond, and then, after overcoming it, embrace each other in a surge of emotion! Then, after getting embarrassed and pulling apart, they can revisit that suggestion from earlier that was interrupted, where he’d put an arm around her shoulders, and the two of them walk toward the brightly lit goal together...... That’s the plan I’d like to go with.]","Serious Senpai : [......This guy turned out to be one hell of an enemy......]"]},{"number":2629,"title":"Chapter 2629 - Re: Demon Realm Amusement Park 9","paragraphs":["A room surrounded by mirrors, with no apparent exit and an atmosphere that clearly suggested there was going to be a boss battle. As I wondered what we should do, the pedestal where the Holy Lantern had been placed in the first room appeared in the center of the room.","When I approached it, glowing letters appeared in the air.","“A mirror monster approaches. If you place the Holy Lantern on this pedestal once and then take it back, you will be able to concentrate the holy light into a single point and fire it. Use the red guiding light to aim, and if you strike the mirror monster with the concentrated light three times, the fearsome monster will return to the heavens.”","I see, so this is basically the rules for the boss battle. Judging from the explanation, it looks like we’ll be able to fire something like a laser beam.","As for “use the red guiding light to aim”...... Does that mean something like a laser pointer will appear, and we’ll use it to aim at the target mirror among all the mirrors in this room, then fire the laser? If we hit it three times, we win?","“However, concentrating the holy light is a double-edged sword...... Once it is used, it cannot be used again until the lantern is filled with light once more. Be careful not to miss your target.”","It was an abstract warning, but I could imagine what it meant. Since we’re supposed to hit it three times, there were probably multiple phases. And I guessed that the lantern’s laser could probably only be used once per phase.","The first lantern had specified its cooldown in seconds, whereas this one described it abstractly as “until the light is filled again”, along with the warning not to miss...... If we missed, I was guessing that we’d definitely get hit by the mirror monster once.","“The blessing of light is abundant. At present, even the mirror monster’s attacks can be nullified up to three times. However, you will not be able to withstand a fourth attack.”","Our margin for error was also three times...... No, saying that we’re safe up to three times meant we’d be out if we got attacked four times.","[......This really does seem like an actual battle.]","[R- Right. So, I guess placing the lantern on the pedestal and picking it up again is what starts it, right?]","Hina-chan nodded with a slightly tense expression while nervously looking around the room. The laughter that had been audible ever since we entered the room had disappeared, leaving us enveloped in an eerie silence that felt like the calm before a storm, so she was probably feeling scared.","That aside...... There sure are a lot of mirrors. There must be nearly 50 of them, right? Covering all of them is going to be pretty difficult.","Hina-chan was scared, so I wanted us to somehow get through this smoothly. Just as I was thinking that, I felt Hina-chan release the arm she had been clinging to. When I turned toward her, I saw Hina-chan trembling slightly, but both of her hands were clenched tightly into fists.","[Hina-chan?]","[K- Kaito-senpai! I’ll watch the right half! Kaito-senpai, please watch the mirrors on the left half.]","[That would be a big help, but are you sure you’ll be okay?]","[Yes! I’m scared, I really am...... but I’ve been relying on Kaito-senpai this whole time, so I’ll help too! ......Ah, but please keep holding my hand...... I’m scared.]","Seeing Hina-chan muster up her courage and offer to help, I smiled lightly. Hina-chan was frightened enough that even she was aware of how scared she was, but even so, she declared that since this was the last part of the attraction, she would do her best to be useful.","This really was a huge help. There was a world of difference between keeping watch over nearly 50 mirrors by myself and splitting them between the two of us.","[Alright, then let’s work together and clear this.]","[Yes!]","I placed the lantern on the pedestal once, then lightly patted Hina-chan’s head with my now-free hand. Then, with one hand still holding Hina-chan’s, we looked at each other and nodded.","[......Alright, I’ll pick up the lantern.]","[J- Just bring it on!]","She was definitely scared, but judging from Hina-chan’s words, she somehow seemed like she would be alright. As I picked up the lantern again...... just as expected, a red laser pointer appeared on the mirror directly in front of us.","It seemed like the targeting beam was extending straight ahead. The red light was quite distinct, so aiming didn’t look like it would be difficult.","“Ahahahahahaha!”","And, as expected, picking up the enhanced lantern seemed to have started the battle with the mirror monster, as an especially loud burst of laughter echoed throughout the room.","Then, the very next moment, our reflections appeared in the countless mirrors, each wearing an eerie smile.","[Hyiih...... I- It’s fine. This much is nothing.]","The figures clearly weren’t reflections of how we looked right now. The versions of us in the mirrors weren’t holding hands, and every single mirror showed us facing straight ahead.","However, since we appeared identically in every mirror, we still couldn’t tell which one contained the mirror monster.","[Hina-chan! I think from this point, one of our reflections is probably going to change somehow.]","[I- I understand. So we just have to find it, right?]","The battle had probably already started. The versions of us in the mirrors were merely grinning eerily, but there should be some kind of change in the mirror where the mirror monster was hiding.","[Ah, Kaito-senpai! That senpai in that mirror looks kind of bigger than the others!!!]","[......There!]","I looked at the mirror Hina-chan was pointing toward, and sure enough, the versions of Hina-chan and me were slightly larger compared to the mirrors on either side...... No, they were probably gradually getting closer toward us, which was why they looked larger than the others.","“Aaaaaaaaaaah!?”","I aimed squarely at that mirror and pressed the stone. A dazzling light was released, immediately followed by the anguished scream of the mirror monster, and all of our reflections in the mirrors disappeared.","Looks like we got it right. Two more hits and we win...... We’ve made it this far, so if possible, I’d like to win without taking a single hit, but we’ll see......","<Afterword>","Mirror Monster : [That’s right...... If you put it another way, Hina has made it this far with Kaito protecting her. She was probably afraid and not good with this sort of thing, but she also wanted to be useful herself. However, Kaito was the one holding the lantern, and Kaito was usually the first to notice anything out of place. But in this boss room, there were clearly too many mirrors for one person to cover by themselves, and combined with the fact that this was undoubtedly the final part of the attraction, it was easy to imagine her summoning up her courage and trying to cooperate.]","Serious-senpai : [N- No way...... Are you saying this was all calculated......?]","Mirror Monster : [There is something sweet about accomplishing something together. Hina in particular gets hyped up easily, and she’s also quite proactive when it comes to physical affection toward Kaito. And by appearing on Hina’s side at the very beginning and letting her be the one to discover me, I give her a sense of accomplishment from having been useful. If that causes her to become overwhelmed with emotion after the boss battle and impulsively do something...... You catch my drift, right?]","Serious Senpai : [......At this point, you’re basically a romance monster......]"]},{"number":2630,"title":"Chapter 2630 - Re: Demon Realm Amusement Park 10","paragraphs":["The first attack succeeded, leaving only two more...... I didn’t think it would come at us with the same pattern as before, but as I wondered what would happen next...... this time, frames and things resembling portraits began appearing in all the mirrors.","[Kaito-senpai, what is this......?]","[Unn. They’re probably the portraits we saw at the entrance...... Ah, but there are two over there that only have frames...... Maybe they’re planning to put us in there?]","[Hyiih......]","The slightly creepy portraits we had seen at the entrance...... Considering the voice in the first room, if the 43 victims and the person who left that voice had all lost to the mirror monster, that would make 44...... And then there were two empty frames with no pictures drawn in them. Surely, these two were some kind of theatrical metaphor, implying that if we lost to the mirror monster, we would become the 45th and 46th victims.","I checked the lantern and found that it was filled with light, so it seemed like we could use it again. But just as I wondered what kind of attack it would use this time...... I saw one of the portraits in the frames open its mouth and laugh.","“Ahahaha!”","I immediately pointed the laser pointer’s light at it, but at that instant, the picture returned to normal...... and this time, laughter came from a different picture.","[The pattern where it moves around huh......]","[Does it move when you point the red light at it......? Ah, next, over there!]","[Tsk...... As expected, it moves immediately...... Judging by how things have gone along the way, there should be a chance to attack...... Ah, maybe...... Hina-chan, since the mirror monster keeps moving from one picture to another, tell me when you find the picture it entered.]","[O- Okay!]","If I thought of this as something like a boss battle in a game, there should definitely be opportunities for us to attack...... And when I pointed the red light at it, the mirror monster immediately moved to another picture. I had a feeling that this movement was probably random.","This was just a prediction, but if the mirror monster remained inside the same picture for a certain amount of time, we would lose and it would attack us. To prevent that, we would keep pointing the red light at the pictures the mirror monster entered, forcing it to move from one to another...... And the randomly moving mirror monster would eventually......","” ! ? “","That’s right, it moved into one of the frames without a picture, leaving the mirror monster’s form completely exposed instead of a portrait. As if surprised, the mirror monster began looking at its own body, staring at its hands and such as though checking its own appearance, and its movements stopped.","Taking advantage of that opening, I pointed the lantern at it and fired a laser of light......","“Aaaaaaaaah!?”","The second scream...... I guess that meant we had cleared the second phase. Now there was only one more left, but what on earth would happen next......? Just as I was thinking that, I heard a clunking sound, and then more and more new mirrors appeared above the mirrors that had been surrounding us in a circle.","[Eh? Eeeeeeh!? There are so many more mirrors now!?]","[......Since this would be the final phase, I guess things are really getting serious......]","The mirrors formed something resembling a dome, leaving us in a state where 180 degrees around us was filled with countless mirrors. There were simply far too many of them; finding the mirror monster among all these mirrors looked like it would be quite difficult.","What’s more, unlike before, there were no changes such as something appearing in the mirrors or laughter being heard......","[Hina-chan, I think this time we’re supposed to find the mirror monster approaching us from somewhere.]","[I- I see, so they’re going with the most basic form for the final phase.]","Exactly. Although the scale had grown much larger, the final phase was the same as what we had encountered along the way: find something strange appearing in one of the mirrors and attack it.","[S- Since it’s the last one, I thought they’d make it tricky and difficult, but it’s actually pretty simple.]","[......Tricky......]","As I carefully watched the dome-shaped mirrors, the word Hina-chan muttered gave me an intense sense of wrongness. The mirror monster was supposed to be a cunning monster. In fact, it had already launched attacks against us in all sorts of different ways along the way.","And now, the final phase was simply this? Rather, what if the point of making it into this dome shape was precisely to make us inevitably direct our gazes upward......?","[! There!]","Thinking that, I lowered my gaze and saw that the pedestal where I had first placed the lantern had turned into a mirror, and the approaching mirror monster was visible there.","I quickly pointed the lantern at it and released its light......","“Gyaaaaaaaaaah!?”","An especially loud scream rang out, and something resembling black mist poured out from the pedestal...... only to disappear when it came into contact with the lantern’s light.","At the same time, the dome-shaped mirrors returned to their original formation, and immediately afterward, the mirrors disappeared, revealing a path forward.","[......D- Did we do it?]","[I- I think we cleared it.]","[ ~ ~ ~ ! ? Senpai!!!]","[Whoa! Hina-chan!?]","Perhaps overwhelmed with emotion at having successfully defeated the mirror monster, Hina-chan happily jumped at me. She ended up hugging me tightly, and while I was startled, Hina-chan lifted her head and happily opened her mouth.","[We did it! A complete victory!]","[Yeah, somehow or other, even with all that happened, I’m glad we managed to clear it without taking any damage.]","[Yes! It’s all thanks to Kaito-senpai...... Ah...... Awawawa, I- I’m sorry!?]","Hina-chan had been excitedly celebrating, but perhaps she realized that she was hugging me from the front, her face turned red, and she hurriedly pulled herself away.","[I- I just acted on impulse...... I- I’m sorry.]","[Ah, no, I understand how you feel, so it’s fine.]","[Uuuu~~ H- How embarrassing.]","There was no doubt that Hina-chan had done remarkably well, considering how bad she was with scary things, and it seemed that the joy and sense of accomplishment from finally being released from all that fear and tension had caused her excitement to go completely overboard.","But, well, that was that. Seeing her blush and fidget shyly was cute, yet at the same time, it was making me feel strange too, creating an awkwardly embarrassing atmosphere that was hard to describe.","[W- Well, anyway, let’s pull ourselves together and head for the exit......]","[R- R- R- Right! If we go out through there, we’ve cleared it, right!?]","The newly appeared path was filled with light, making it obviously feel like the goal, so there was no doubt that we would clear it once we went through there.","I was about to head straight for the exit when I suddenly remembered. One way or another, our conversation from before coming into this room had been interrupted by the mirror monster’s laughter...... What should I do? Things were a little awkward between us right now, so I felt like I might become overly conscious of it...... But she had said something about dreaming of doing it, and if I missed this opportunity, I probably wouldn’t get another chance......","[Ah~~ errr, Hina-chan.]","[Yes?]","[Well, the exit is right there, and I don’t think the mirror monster is going to show up anymore...... So, errr, even though it’s only for a short distance, do you want to try what you said earlier, about putting my arm around your shoulder?]","[Uehh!? Ah, e- errr, umm...... I- I...... would like to...... try it. I- I mean, I’ve always admired it......]","At my suggestion, Hina-chan was clearly flustered, her face bright red as she fumbled for words...... but eventually, as though squeezing the words out, she replied in a tiny voice that she wanted to try it.","[T- Then, excuse me for a moment.]","[Y- Yesh......]","Honestly, it really did feel like we were both getting strangely nervous, but I slipped my arm around Hina-chan’s shoulder and gently pulled her closer. The sensation of her small, rather delicate shoulder beneath my hand, and Hina-chan’s warmth as she lightly leaned against me...... Perhaps because the atmosphere had made me overly conscious of everything, my heart seemed to be beating unusually fast.","Hina-chan’s face was bright red as well, but she didn’t seem to dislike it...... and the emotions I could sense through Sympathy Magic were also ones of happiness.","And so, while feeling an atmosphere that was somehow a little sweet and bittersweet, I started walking toward the path filled with light, keeping my arm around Hina-chan’s shoulder.","<Afterword>","Mirror Monster : [......This is where the fact that we were interrupted at that exact moment pays off. Even though things were interrupted and left hanging, Kaito had heard Hina talking about the kind of situation she had always dreamed of, so he wanted to somehow make it come true for her. Then, see? Rather than having Kaito simply get swept along by Hina’s request from back then, Kaito is the one who suggests it and puts his arm around her shoulder, making the two of them conscious of each other and their hearts start pounding...... That’s what you call lovey-dovey development that also serves as groundwork for what comes next.]","Serious-senpai : [Guaaaaaaaaaah...... Just get lost already, seriously...... You’re way too d*mn troublesome......]"]},{"number":2631,"title":"Chapter 2631 - Re: Demon Realm Amusement Park 11","paragraphs":["Having reached the exit of the labyrinth, Hina-chan pulled away in embarrassment, and while I felt an oddly ticklish sort of atmosphere, we continued toward the exit.","Several groups had already arrived, and once we joined up, the remaining people soon came as well.","After hearing what had happened, it seemed that their experiences had been pretty much the same. Apparently, there were a few people who had been hit once or twice, but it seemed everyone had managed to clear it safely.","As expected, or rather, just as I had predicted, when the mirror monster used a feint and moved between mirrors, no matter how quickly you pointed the lantern at it, until it reached a specific state where it became vulnerable to attack, it would apparently move to another mirror during the time lag between pressing the stone and the light actually coming out. That seemed to be the point where it was easiest to fail.","Also, even if you took damage along the way, the upgraded lantern would restore all the damage you had taken for the final battle, which was a thoughtful design intended to make it easier to clear.","In fact, the phases of the mirror monster during the final battle also seemed to be based around noticing the sense of wrongness as it approached, waiting for an opportunity without being fooled by its feints, and being caught off guard from outside your awareness, along with the attacks encountered along the way. It seemed that the phase wouldn’t change when you failed, so all things considered, the difficulty really did seem to be designed on the assumption that you would clear it.","[But even though it was pretty unexpected, it was fun!]","[......Hina-chan, why does your face seem a little red?]","[It was scary after all! So scary I even cried a little...... A- Anyway, let’s move on to the next one!]","Hina-chan hurriedly tried to cover it up when Aoi-chan pointed out the lingering redness from when I’d put my arm around her shoulders earlier. However, Aoi-chan naturally already knew that Hina-chan wasn’t good with scary things, so she simply nodded without thinking much of it.","[Hina-chan, where are we going next?]","[Next, let’s just go with something that actually has “coaster” in the name. I’d rather not have another horror attraction suddenly ambush us......]","[I don’t think we’ll keep running into horror attractions that often...... How about this snow-and-ice coaster then?]","As I watched Aoi-chan and Hina-chan talking while we moved along, someone suddenly gave me a light pat on the shoulder. When I turned around, I found Luna-san there, wearing an amused, rather mischievous grin.","Hmmm, Luna-san can be pretty perceptive, so she probably figured out something was going on between Hina-chan and me and came over to tease me about it.","[It seems that, for Miyama-sama, this was an attraction where you could experience emotions other than fear. Even while out with such a large group, the way you boldly seized every opportunity to make your move as though you were deliberately waiting for an opening...... This humble Lunamaria cannot help but feel a profound sense of awe.]","[You’re as lively as a fish in water. Were you okay with the horror attractions, Luna-san?]","[I had no particular problem with them. Rather, what I was worried about was places like the Forest Area......]","[Ah, I see...... Though, I don’t think there’s probably anything like what you’re worried about, Luna-san......]","What Luna-san wasn’t good with was insects, and while the Forest Area certainly seemed like the place in this amusement park where something like that might appear...... Unless they were cute, exaggerated, cartoon-like insects, I didn’t think there were any attractions featuring realistic caterpillars or anything else that would scare Luna-san.","Well, if I carelessly went along with the topic, she’d probably tease me about it endlessly, so it was important to skillfully steer the conversation elsewhere.","[......So? What exactly happened? You can tell me secretly, just between the two of us, you know? After all, you and I are so close, aren’t we, Miyama-sama......]","[No comment.]","[Mmph, you’re keeping your guard up. Well, very well. We still have plenty of time after all, so from here on, I’ll continue to enjoy watching the prowess of Peerless Love Warrior Miyama-sama. So, who will you be setting your sights on next?]","She looked like she was having fun. She looked like she was having a lot of fun. If anything, she seemed to be enjoying herself more than at any point since we’d arrived at this amusement park. Luna-san also had a side to her that liked gossip, so perhaps she enjoyed talking about romance-related matters as well.","Even now, while she was honestly teasing me to some extent, she also seemed genuinely fascinated by anything related to romance...... Come to think of it, her tastes and interests really were quite feminine.","[......Then, I suppose I’ll set my sights on Luna-san next.]","[Oh my, whatever shall I do? At long last, I too have fallen prey to Miyama-sama’s fangs.]","[.................]","[......Eh? A- Are you actually serious?]","When I stared back at Luna-san with a straight face after her playful response, she began to panic, her expression clearly showing that she was shaken.","In that respect, she was rather similar to Alice. She liked to stick her nose into this sort of thing of her own accord, stirring things up and asking all sorts of questions, yet the moment the tables were turned on her, she became extremely vulnerable. They were remarkably alike in that regard.","[Well, who knows?]","[L- Let’s calm down, Miyama-sama...... You yourself said it before, didn’t you? That if you put your mind to it, you could probably seize the initiative in an instant...... Considering the difference in our actual experience, there is no way I could possibly stand a chance if Miyama-sama seriously came after me. Don’t you think bullying the weak is rather shameful? I believe the strong should possess a generous heart.]","[......Then, for now, whenever we come across an attraction where we have to split into pairs, let’s go together.]","[Miyama-sama, I apologize for getting carried away, so please have mercy...... Miyama-sama occasionally shows an S side toward Alice-sama and me, so I have nothing but apprehension about this.]","[..................]","[Please stop smiling silently like that...... It’s frightening, you see.]","Truth be told, the fact that she teased me about romantic matters was practically like shaking hands with me, or rather, it was as though she had challenged me to a battle by bringing up the very subject that was her own weakness.","Even now, my previous impression hasn’t changed. If anything...... compared to when I’d talked with her during the Six Kings Festival, I’d gained more experience myself. More importantly, the countermeasures I’d developed for dealing with Alice applied here as well, so when it came to this sort of topic, I felt I could seize the initiative as easily as taking candy from a baby.","<Afterword>","? ? ? : [Yeah, that’s true. Kaito-san sometimes gets a little more S-like toward people who like to tease him, like me...... Alice-chan and Luna-san, so it’s kind of troublesome.]","Serious-senpai : [I feel like it’s also proof that he feels comfortable around you guys. It’s a different sort of relationship, but he also speaks sharply to people like Tre......]"]},{"number":2632,"title":"Chapter 2632 - Re: Demon Realm Amusement Park 12","paragraphs":["The coaster we stopped by as the second attraction in the Ice Area was pretty much what I had expected, but riding a coaster along a course with a fantastical atmosphere was enjoyable in a different way from the one in the Aqua Area.","The scenery of snow and ice had a unique atmosphere to begin with, which was nice, and the effects created through illusion magic were also incredibly elaborate. I’d thought this several times since coming to this amusement park, but the amount of attention to detail put into each and every attraction was incredible.","[Every single one of these attractions is amazing and so much fun, isn’t it?!]","[Hmmm, but if they pack in this much amazing magic like Illusion Magic, wouldn’t the operating costs be pretty high......?]","As we made our way toward the next area, the Flame Area, I could see Aoi-chan tilting her head as she replied to Hina-chan, who was speaking excitedly.","It was true that every attraction had incredible effects, and they certainly seemed to have a lot of money invested in them. On top of that, considering how many effects were created through magic, I thought it was only natural to wonder just how many magic crystals the entire amusement park would need to have prepared in order to supply all that magic power.","But, though this was nothing more than a guess...... I think the energy-related operating costs of this amusement park are probably almost zero. The reason is simple: this is an amusement park made by Shiro-san at the center, and I remember Alice saying something before about how “the energy is generated internally, so it can operate infinitely” or something along those lines.","And since that amusement park has been placed in the central area, they’re probably supplying the other areas with the infinite power energy created by Shiro-san for that amusement park. Since there’s no need to worry about energy...... or rather, magic power, they can probably afford to incorporate abundant magical effects into every attraction.","Well, this is all just speculation, and...... for example, if Kuro were to put her mind to it, she could probably easily ask Tre-san and the others for their cooperation and secure as many high-purity magic crystals as necessary for operation, so I can’t say that I’m certain.","While I was thinking about that, we arrived at the next area, the Flame Area, but...... this area was incredible in an entirely different sense from everything we had seen so far.","At the center of the area stood a gigantic mountain with huge amounts of magma seemingly glowing brilliantly as they poured out of it, while lava flowed through the entire area like rivers, and even the paths had the appearance of black volcanic rock...... It was a scene that gave me the impression of something like a burning hell.","[This is something else......]","[It certainly is a sight befitting the name Flame Area...... but the place isn’t hot. The lava and such are merely made to look that way, so I suppose it isn’t actually real lava.]","At my mutter, Lilia-san murmured with an impressed expression. Indeed, the area looked incredibly hot, but I couldn’t feel any heat at all.","It wasn’t because I had received Shiro-san’s blessing; just like in the Ice Area earlier, the flames and lava were probably merely part of the effects.","[Coming here from the Ice Area, the change between ice and fire really makes the difference feel incredible.]","[Indeed. It makes me want to see the boundary between the areas from somewhere high up...... So, Hina-chan, which attraction are we going to here?]","[Hmmm...... For now, why don’t we go to that huge mountain? It stands out so much, and that’s definitely the main attraction of this area!]","When Aoi-chan asked Hina-chan which attraction we should go to, the first thing Hina-chan pointed out was the gigantic volcano visible in the center.","Every so often, it spewed fire from its summit as though it were erupting, and its visual impact was certainly the greatest in this area.","[Let’s see, according to the pamphlet, the attraction located there is...... Flame River Racing...... Racing?]","[“Flame River” probably refers to the lava flowing down that mountain, right? And if it’s a race...... maybe we’ll be doing something like whitewater rafting?]","[Whitewater rafting down a mountain that high sounds like it would be incredible......]","After checking the attraction located at the volcano’s position in the pamphlet and telling the others, both Hina-chan and Aoi-chan had expressions that showed they couldn’t quite figure out what to expect either.","Indeed, it was difficult to imagine what it would be like from the name Flame River Racing alone. Like Hina-chan said, it might involve some kind of competition, or perhaps the whole thing was simply part of the attraction’s setting and effects.","[When you say racing, is it something like the games Master has?]","[I think the meaning is similar, but it would be difficult to make it like that game...... Ah, but that game was also made available to the general public during the Six Kings Festival, so technically, I suppose it isn’t impossible......]","Hearing Anima’s murmur, I realized that it could indeed be a race conducted by transferring us into a special space, similar to the VR game races at the Six Kings Festival.","That VR game was also made by Alice, after all...... Well, I suppose we’ll find out once we go there.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Going by the name, it probably isn’t Lunamaria’s turn...... The suspicious ones are the Magic Area or Dark Area...... Considering how the Ice Area was wrapped up, there’s also a possibility that the attractions in each area will be simplified to about one each...... Is there a possibility that a third party will show up? No, but Lilia, Sieg, and Anima, who are all his lovers, are here too, and I also feel like Hina has been the main focus throughout the whole thing...... No, but considering that the lovers will have some onsen time later, maybe they’ll keep things more subdued here...... I- I got no clue.]"]},{"number":2633,"title":"Chapter 2633 - Re: Demon Realm Amusement Park 13","paragraphs":["With the enormous volcano in the center serving as an easy-to-identify landmark, Flame River Racing, which I expected to be the main attraction, had a rather spacious reception area at the foot of the volcano as well.","I could see a few people who appeared to be other invitees here and there, but it didn’t feel particularly crowded, and we were able to reach the reception desk right away and receive an explanation of the attraction.","As the name suggested, this attraction was apparently a race, and up to 10 people could participate simultaneously, which was a perfect fit for our group.","As for the attraction itself, it was something like an individual race. Each participant would board a small boat capable of traveling up a river of lava...... a canoe-like boat in appearance, and proceed toward the summit while traveling through the lava. The first person to reach the summit would be the winner...... In other words, it was quite literally a race.","The boats were easy to operate. We couldn’t accelerate or decelerate them ourselves; instead, the boats would automatically proceed toward the summit. Apparently, all we could do was move them left and right.","The lava paths leading toward the summit branched off in various directions, and apparently, which course you chose to follow would make a difference in the outcome.","[Also, along the way, there are three factors that will affect the outcome of the race. The first is the volcanic rocks that randomly fall from the summit. Of course, since they are illusions created by Illusion Magic, you won’t be injured or anything, but if one hits you, your boat will stop for one second, so please carefully judge the timing and avoid them.]","Since this was a race where we couldn’t control our acceleration or deceleration ourselves, it was only natural for there to be components like these traps. Otherwise, the outcome would be determined purely by luck in choosing a course we’d never seen before.","[The second is these balls of wind displayed here. If you come into contact with one, your boat’s speed will increase significantly for three seconds. This is a useful ability, but please be careful when controlling your boat.]","And next was an acceleration gimmick...... This was another important factor that would affect the outcome, but a boat traveling at higher speed would presumably be harder to control, increasing the possibility of hitting obstacles. There might also be some placed in locations that were difficult to reach, places where forcing your way over to collect one might actually result in a loss of time.","[The third is obstacles. These come in various forms, such as rocks, walls, and monsters, but please be careful, as coming into contact with one will reduce your boat’s speed for three seconds. If you come into contact with obstacles consecutively, the duration of the speed reduction will reset with each contact, so please understand it as lasting for three seconds from the most recent contact. Also, contact between boats will be treated the same as contact with an obstacle.]","Finally, there were the obstacles. Unlike the volcanic rocks, they wouldn’t bring us to a complete stop, but would instead reduce our speed...... From what I’d heard, the race itself was fairly simple: avoid the volcanic rocks and obstacles while collecting the balls of wind to accelerate and make your way forward.","[......I- I’m relieved it’s a simple system.]","[......Eta’s bad at the racing games Master has after all.]","[Apparently, I find it difficult to compete while thinking about several different things at once, and I end up hesitating at crucial moments.]","[You just suck at thinking about multiple things at once...... Eta, you’re so one-track-minded.]","[What did you say? You’re not exactly very good at it either......]","[I’m better than Eta.]","[......You said it. In that case, I’ll challenge you to a race!]","[......Bring it on.]","It seemed like Eta and Theta were glaring sparks at each other, but this was more or less just the usual...... If anything, the fact that they were trying to settle things through an attraction made them seem perfectly rational, so there didn’t seem to be any problem.","Maybe because both of them had once served under the War King, but whenever they had a disagreement, they tended to settle it by competing against each other right away. So while they often got into arguments, once they had competed and reached a conclusion, neither of them would complain about the result, meaning it didn’t lead to any lingering resentment afterward...... It was probably better to just let them have this level of confrontation.","In fact, Anima and Caraway seemed to share my way of thinking, as neither of them showed any intention of stopping the two.","[This is exciting! But when it comes to racing...... Lilia-san is probably really strong, right?]","[Hmmm, unlike that racing game, individual technique doesn’t seem to matter all that much, so I don’t think there’ll be that much of a difference.]","Just as Hina-chan said, when it came to VR racing games, Lilia-san was overwhelmingly the strongest among this group. Her technique in particular was incredible; her cornering and other movements were on the level of a top-tier player at the highest level, so Hina-chan and I wouldn’t even stand a chance against her without being given a significant handicap.","However, with this attraction, I had a feeling that those kinds of technical skills wouldn’t create much of a difference...... The volcanic rocks fell randomly, after all, and it seemed like there were quite a few factors that depended on luck...... So if anything, I wondered if that might actually put Lilia-san at a disadvantage.","I don’t know...... Hopefully, it’s just my imagination, but...... I had this strange feeling that volcanic rocks were going to rain down on Lilia-san’s boat in particular, one after another.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Ahh, so she’s insanely strong when there are hardly any random factors and it’s purely a contest of technique, but she’s bad at ones involving gimmicks because she ends up black-holing all the annoying gimmicks...... Even in the game they played on Kaito’s birthday, didn’t she say annoying gimmicks kept spawning right at her feet......?]","? ? ? : [It’s not that Lilia-san herself is necessarily unlucky, but she’s the type who somehow draws bad luck her way. Well, that’s just the kind of person she is......]"]},{"number":2634,"title":"Chapter 2634 - Re: Demon Realm Amusement Park 14","paragraphs":["I had gotten a general understanding of the rules for Flame River Racing, and before long, I found myself participating. When I stood on top of the teleportation magic circle and the attendant activated the magic tool, the next moment I was on a racing boat.","We were already above a river of lava, but the area was like a somewhat spacious cave, with words floating in the air.","< You will be moved to the starting point in one minute. Until then, you may check the boat’s controls. >","Ah, I see. So I could check how quickly it moved from side to side and things like that...... It seemed that all I had to do to move left and right was shift my weight in the respective direction. By putting more weight into it, I could move farther, while putting less weight into it resulted in a smaller movement, so it seemed I could adjust the distance I moved left or right to some extent.","However, the speed wasn’t particularly fast. If I wanted to avoid obstacles and such, it seemed I’d have to start moving left or right somewhat early. This was probably intentionally designed to make lateral movement gradual so that differences in reflexes wouldn’t have as much of an impact.","It seemed the controls had been adjusted so that movement would generally be somewhat broad, making it difficult to use incredible technique to dodge obstacles with only the minimum necessary movement.","Depending on when I noticed something, there might be times when I wouldn’t be able to avoid a volcanic projectile or obstacle even if I knew it was coming, so I’d have to be careful about that.","Well, since movement was really only left and right, there wasn’t anything difficult about it. I finished checking the controls quickly, and while I was waiting, once the minute had passed, the boat started moving, exited the cave, and came to a temporary stop.","Looking around, I could see everyone else riding similar small boats, and a large countdown began in front of us.","It seemed to be a ten-count, and when the number reached zero, all the boats started simultaneously...... and I saw Lilia-san’s boat get hit by a volcanic projectile that happened to come down at precisely the spot right after the start, causing her to come to a temporary stop...... It was random, so I suppose something like that happening immediately after the start was possible too, but I couldn’t help feeling terribly sorry for her.","That said, I couldn’t afford to worry about it. The race had already started, so I needed to pay attention to the direction I was going...... The lava river was reasonably wide, and even with ten boats, it didn’t feel cramped.","It was probably also because we were still right after the start, but I had a good view ahead, making it easy to judge the situation.","Just as I was thinking that...... the path ahead suddenly split into three. More precisely, the middle path sloped upward, while the paths on either side sloped downward, and I could see a wind orb on the middle path.","......This seemed really suspicious. Considering that this was a race where we had to climb all the way to the summit, the middle path seemed advantageous even without taking the wind orb into account, but...... it was so blatantly obvious that it felt like a trap.","But it was also possible that they were making us think that, only to turn the tables on us and make the center route genuinely advantageous...... Yep, I have no idea.","For now, my current position was closer to the right-hand path, so I was worried that trying to force a change in course here would cause a collision with another boat...... Unn? Thinking about it, there hadn’t been any acceleration items so far, so if all the boats were moving at the same speed, we should have been lined up side by side, but why were we slightly staggered forward and backward? Ah, could it be that moving left and right causes the speed to drop slightly......? If that’s the case, moving left and right too much would be a bad move, too...... Then I’ll just stay on this course and take the right-hand path.","Looking at the others, I still couldn’t tell which path Lilia-san, who was slightly behind, would choose, but everyone else seemed to be adjusting their positions to choose their respective paths, just like me.","Hina-chan, Eta, and Anima seemed to have simply decided that the center was faster and were positioning themselves to head there...... Luna-san also seemed to be adjusting toward the center, so perhaps she was trying to read the situation one step further and choose the center after all.","Aoi-chan, Theta, and Caraway were coming toward the same right-hand path as me, while the rest seemed to be heading down the left-hand path. I was thinking that we’d already become pretty spread out right from the start when I saw several volcanic projectiles coming down.","Ah, this might be pretty troublesome. If I focused too much on the course ahead, I might fail to notice volcanic projectiles falling from above, while if I paid too much attention to the volcanic projectiles, my decisions would be delayed.","And that’s not all. The volcanic projectiles could also alter the course. This time, Aoi-chan made a fairly large movement to avoid a volcanic projectile coming down, which caused her to drift toward the center path, and she hurriedly moved back after dodging the volcanic projectile, but if it had been just a little closer, she might have been forced to switch to the center path.","It seemed like a simple race, but there was surprisingly quite a lot to think about. Since I was doing this, I’d like to aim for the top, but now then......","As I was thinking that, I reached the fork and entered the right-hand path as planned, which led downhill, but...... there was a cave in the direction I was heading, and the path split into three again.","Could there really be this many forks......? I can’t see what’s inside the cave either...... Hmm, I’ll just go left for now.","<Afterword>","Singularity : [Hmm, I’ll just “go pick out randomly” and turn left here.]","Countless Blessings : [I’ve been waiting for this moment!]","Abnormal Luck : [You want to aim for the top? Leave it to me!]","Overwhelming Power of Fate : [Don’t think. Feel......]","Serious-senpai : [......Ah.]"]},{"number":2635,"title":"Chapter 2635 - Re: Demon Realm Amusement Park 15","paragraphs":["The cave-like path I chose in Flame River Racing was fairly easy to navigate, thanks to the lava river itself giving off enough light to illuminate the area, as well as the path being considerably wider than I had expected.","There were also several wind balls placed in easy-to-reach positions, and there weren’t many obstacles. I can’t say for certain since I have nothing to compare it to, but wouldn’t this be a pretty good route?","As I was thinking that, I continued on for a while, eventually passing through the cave and coming back outside. Judging by the location, we’re probably around the middle of the mountain. I feel like I’ve made pretty good progress.","And when I looked down slightly, I was able to see part of the other courses...... and right where I happened to move my gaze was Lilia-san’s boat.","Her path was fairly wide but seemed to have a moderate number of obstacles, and within the range I could see, Lilia-san was skillfully maneuvering her boat around the obstacles with elegant control.","Even though this isn’t an attraction where technique has that much of an impact, I couldn’t help thinking that her piloting skills were truly impressive...... when directly below Lilia-san’s boat as she was progressing along the course, a pitfall suddenly appeared...... or rather, there was an effect that made it look like the road itself was collapsing, and Lilia-san fell while making a face that looked like “Eh? Seriously!?”.","L- Lilia-saaaaaaan!? W- Was that some kind of course selection? So there are also trap-like gimmicks, or rather, factors that change the course......?","What’s more, judging by the position of that pitfall, it was set up so that you’d get caught if you tried to take the wind ball by the shortest possible route. That’s a pretty terrifying trap.","Feeling sorry for Lilia-san’s incredible luck at encountering it so precisely, I turned my gaze back, only to find that the path had split into several routes again.","I couldn’t see any other boats behind me, so it seems like everyone has gotten pretty spread out across the different routes.","But this time there are four...... Hmm, I have almost no information to base my decision on, so I don’t know. For now, I’ll take the second path from the left.","Following my intuition and choosing that path...... Whoa, this route has a lot of obstacles. There are several enormous rocks, and it looks like it’ll be difficult unless I move the boat quite a bit from side to side......","[Whoa!? That was close———- ah, shoot!]","At that moment, I saw a volcanic rock falling down and hurriedly moved to avoid it. While I was traveling through the cave-like path, no volcanic rocks had fallen at all, presumably because that’s how that section was designed, so I’d let my guard down. As a result, my reaction was a little slow, and I moved in the wrong direction to avoid it.","Judging by the positions of the huge rocks, I needed to dodge to the right here. If I went left, there was a huge rock directly in front of me, and by the time I realized I’d made a mistake, I was already too close to avoid it.","Well, a collision penalty would only slow me down, not result in a game over, but I’d really let my guard down. Even knowing it’s just a video, crashing straight into a huge rock is terrifying———– Unn? Eh? Arehh?","My boat charged straight into the huge rock, but instead of the expected slowdown...... it just passed straight through as though the rock didn’t even exist.","[......Could this be a hidden route?]","After passing through the huge rock, I found myself entering a cave-like course, and the boat continued onward. I never would have imagined that there would be a hidden course inside an obstacle.","But normally, a hidden course like this would be something akin to a shortcut, so wouldn’t it be reasonable to get my hopes up?","The path was somewhat narrow, but it was almost entirely straight, so there wasn’t much need to maneuver...... Then, after progressing for a while, I reached a zone where about 10 wind balls were lined up in a straight line, and I raced along the straight path at tremendous speed as I accelerated.","And once I made it all the way down that straight stretch, there was an exit from the cave, and when I emerged outside again...... I was at a height where I could see the volcano’s crater——— in other words, I was near the summit.","I continued along the path, and partway through, there was a section where several courses seemed to merge together. Before long, I could see a large gate ahead with the word “GOAL” written on it.","There was no one ahead of me...... and when I looked back, I couldn’t see anyone else’s boat either. If that’s the case, then this means......","With anticipation welling up inside me, I passed through the goal, and a fanfare rang out as glowing letters reading “1st Place” appeared in front of my boat.","Nice! I finished in first place. I had wondered if entering the hidden course might give me a chance, but I’m simply happy that I actually came in first.","As I was thinking that, the glowing letters changed, and this time something resembling the clear times from several races was displayed, while “Course Time Ranking” appeared overhead.","Quite a bit of time had already passed since the amusement park opened, and since this was clearly the main attraction of the Flame Area, I imagine quite a lot of people had played it.","At the very least, the time ranking was displayed starting from 50th place, so at least fifty people had played. And rankings of this sort probably only display from a certain point near the top, so there were likely even more people who had played.","Then, what appeared to be my time began flashing, and it was a far reaching first place, more than two minutes ahead of second place.","<Afterword>","Abnormal Luck : [Now’s the time!]","Volcanic Bomb : [Leave it to me! Right hereeeee!]","Serious-senpai : [The difference between Lilia getting taken out by the gimmicks and Kaito having even the gimmicks go all-out to support him......]"]},{"number":2636,"title":"Chapter 2636 - Re: Demon Realm Amusement Park 16","paragraphs":["There was no sign that we would be teleported immediately after reaching the goal. The boat came to a stop once it reached the open area beyond the goal. Then, after a little while, something resembling a large monitor appeared before me, displaying the progress of the other people’s races.","Ah, could it be that we have to wait until everyone reaches the goal? And while we’re waiting, we can watch the other people’s races......","Eh? But this is some amazing technology. Aren’t recorder magic tools still supposed to be relatively underdeveloped? Had they really advanced to the point where they could do things like floating monitors and nine-way split-screen displays?","[No, it’s not quite that simple.]","[Alice?]","[Congratulations on winning. Cutting straight through the theoretically fastest course is just like you, Kaito-san. Well, the others will probably take another two minutes or so, so this Transcendental Beauty who can keep Kaito-san from getting bored will answer your questions.]","I heard a voice from behind me and turned around, only to see Alice sitting on the edge of the boat, having appeared there at some point. There was no need to ask how she knew what I was wondering about. Knowing Alice, it would be easy for her to look at the floating monitor and predict what questions I would have.","[Fumu...... When you say it’s not that simple, you’re talking about the recorder magic tool, right?]","[Yep. At a glance, what Kaito-san sees right now might make you think it’s developed into some super-advanced, sci-fi-like technology, but they’ve installed several thousand magic crystals throughout this volcano just to make this possible.]","[Several thousand!?]","[Once you get into displaying images in real time, the spell formulas become way too complicated. This is one area where magic falls far behind the machines in Kaito-san’s world. Magic power isn’t particularly good at transmitting or projecting information. See, even hummingbird is pretty lousy when you compare it to email, and the character limit can be affected by the individual’s skill, so there are a lot of inconvenient aspects to it, right?]","[That’s true. Functionally speaking, smartphones are vastly superior.]","[It’s not that it’s impossible, but the cost-performance just doesn’t add up. Even a magic tool used solely for communication takes several magic crystals and a few minutes to operate, so radio waves are much more efficient for that sort of thing.]","Indeed, while the magic tools of this world had some capabilities that far surpassed those of certain machines, they were extremely poor at things like communication and recording.","For example, magic tools for recording music, equivalent to what we would call CDs in our world, were also quite expensive, making them difficult for ordinary households to purchase.","As a result, inexpensive music boxes were the norm, and there were places resembling concert halls in various cities, so there were many areas where they were clearly inferior to mechanical products.","Conversely, when it came to storage and transportation, magic could perhaps be said to have an overwhelming advantage. Magic Boxes and teleportation magic tools were the most obvious examples of that.","[Well, it’s only natural that magic and machines would have different strengths and weaknesses.]","[Suppose we make use of Alice-chan’s transcendental intellect, I could make things that solve those problems, and if I really wanted to, I could even create something like a mechanical civilization that’s different from Kaito-san’s world...... But if you develop this and that too rapidly, all sorts of cracks inevitably start to show, so we have to be careful and take things slowly.]","[Hmm...... that’s rough. Anyway, you’re saying that continuously broadcasting footage like this, almost like a live broadcast, requires quite a lot of preparation and expensive equipment, right?]","[Exactly. This amusement park is also partly being used to experiment with technologies like that, so some of them have been implemented without regard for cost. And the system in the attractions you’ve played so far, where the same tool randomly determines your teleportation destination, is also a new technology.]","[......Now that you mention it, I don’t think we’ve ever had anything like that before.]","Thinking about it, the random destination teleports in places like the Forest Castle and the Mirror Labyrinth seemed like they could be useful in all sorts of attractions, but I had never seen anything like them before.","[But I see...... So it’s not simply about making a profit. It’s also serving to regulate the development of technology throughout the world and test out new technologies...... You’ve really thought this through.]","[Ah, no...... I mean, actually...... this is for Kuro-san.]","[Unn? Kuro?]","[......Recently, she seems to be happy about being able to use various things with her creation-type power, and she started making things that had never existed before. If we just left her to do as she pleased, this place was going to turn into a completely absurd amusement park full of overtechnology, so after discussing it among ourselves, we made some adjustments.]","[......Good work.]","Come to think of it, Kuro had happily mentioned before that she had recently become able to do things like that...... So she had apparently started messing around with all sorts of things using the creation-type power she had gained access to, even making things with effects that normally shouldn’t be possible, which was probably why Alice stepped in to keep things under control.","[That’s right, Alice-chan is working really hard. So I think Kaito-san should spoil me more.]","[......But you’ll run away if I do.]","[No, well, I’d like you to adjust the pampering to just the right level where I don’t run away or get too embarrassed, while sometimes taking me by surprise depending on the situation, with little unexpected incidents here and there, yet striking such a perfect balance that even though I’m bewildered, my happiness outweighs it all, and if possible, make it pretty romantic......]","[T- That’s way too many requests......]","In short, her request amounted to “Please spoil me while somehow taking all the appropriate considerations into account”, but considering Alice’s request...... and considering just how hopeless she herself was at romance, to the point that she could confidently declare it herself...... fulfilling it seemed like it would require some truly delicate adjustments...... The difficulty level felt insanely high.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [No, that girl...... Once Kaito gets into a position where he’s going to push things through, she’ll go along with absolutely anything...... Rather than being difficult, she’s so hopelessly weak that anything you do would be a critical hit.]","? ? ? : [That’s not it. Alice-chan just wants him to be much more creatively sophisticated about it, with consideration, kindness, and affection, and adjust things so perfectly that the happiness outweighs the bewilderment.]","Serious-senpai : [.......................]"]},{"number":2637,"title":"Chapter 2637 - Re: Demon Realm Amusement Park 17","paragraphs":["As for the results of Flame River Racing, according to Alice, I came in first by taking the theoretically shortest course, followed by Caraway, Sieg-san, Theta, Aoi-chan, Anima, Hina-chan, Luna-san, and Eta, with Lilia-san unfortunately coming in last.","From what I could tell by watching on the monitors, there was almost no difference in skill or control ability, and it seemed that the people who happened to get good routes or collect more wind orbs ended up higher in the rankings. It felt like the rankings could change completely if we did it again.","However, Lilia-san was truly unlucky, or rather...... the randomly generated volcanic rocks were falling on her at about two to three times the rate they were for everyone else, which really left an impression.","There was even one scene where Lilia-san sensed a volcanic rock and dodged it, only for another volcanic rock to immediately fall where she dodged to, forcing her to dodge again. Then, in a three-stage attack with no opening whatsoever, another volcanic rock came down, which she barely dodged...... only for three volcanic rocks to fall side by side and hit her directly. I was left dumbfounded by the sight.","Was that really random? The volcanic rocks seemed to have an absurdly strong killing intent toward Lilia-san in particular. They would sometimes come down several at once, sometimes fall in ways that blocked off her escape route, and finally there was even a situation where three came down side by side, making them impossible to dodge. It was just too tragic.","[It was fun, though Lilia-san seemed to have quite a hard time.]","[It was rather difficult. There were many situations where I was able to react myself, but the ship’s movement speed wasn’t enough to get out of the way in time...... However, what surprised me the most wasn’t the volcanic rocks, but the pitfall.]","As we left the attraction and walked along the path, I made some light conversation with Lilia-san.","[Ahh, I happened to be watching from the upper section, but that really did come out of nowhere.]","[I’d already been hit by volcanic rocks so many times that I was paying far too much attention to what was above me when that happened...... Well, I only fell into the cave course, which had a lot of obstacles, and since the volcanic rocks don’t fall there, it was actually easier in that respect......]","Ahhh, I see. For Lilia-san, whose luck with volcanic rocks was so atrocious, being inside a cave where volcanic rocks didn’t fall was easier even if there were lots of obstacles...... In fact, she was good at controlling the ship, and she’d even managed to dodge three volcanic rocks in succession, so her technique was impressive too. Thinking about it that way, Lilia-san might have had the best raw control skills...... putting her luck aside.","[But I think troubles like that occurring during an attraction are actually part of what makes them fun. Personally, as long as nothing happens that makes my stomach hurt, I really don’t mind......]","[Oh! If it isn’t Kaito and Lilia! What a coincidence running into you here!!]","[...............]","[N- No, don’t glare at me......]","Lilia-san had been looking rather carefree, saying that there was no problem as long as she didn’t have to suffer any more stomachaches, but the moment she heard the loud voice coming from nearby, she turned a resentful gaze toward me.","I didn’t know whether this was my fault or not, but I already knew who we’d encountered without even having to check...... When I turned around, I saw Megiddo-san in her male form, along with the members of the War King’s Five Generals.","[Hello, Megiddo-san. It really is quite a coincidence.]","[Hello, Megiddo-sama.]","[Ou! I’m lucky to run into you by chance! Looks like you’ve got everyone from Lilia’s group here, so you’re all going around together? It’s nice and lively!]","Megiddo-san spoke cheerfully without seeming to care that her loud voice was attracting attention from everyone around us. In her current appearance, she probably wouldn’t fit the atmosphere of an ordinary amusement park very well, but considering this Flame Area was modeled after Megiddo-san, I felt like she fit in ridiculously well here.","[Megiddo-san too, you’re with the Five Generals as well.]","[Yeah. I would’ve been fine with splitting up, but apparently there are attractions meant for multiple people, so we’ve ended up sticking together anyway.]","[Well, you know, Boss...... If we’re randomly assigned and end up with another guest, and that guy happens to be someone you don’t like, you’ll kill them, right?]","[Ahh? I wouldn’t kill them right away. I’d warn them to disappear first. If they don’t disappear after that, then I’ll kill them.]","[That’s exactly why we’re accompanying you......]","Hearing Ozma-san say that with an indescribable expression on his face, I found myself completely agreeing with him. Megiddo-san is an utterly merciless person, but she’s not the sort who would immediately kill someone she happened to see in town for no particular reason.","Her stance is more along the lines of leaving someone she doesn’t like alone as long as they don’t involve themselves with her, and only killing them if they happen to catch her attention.","So there wouldn’t be a problem in an ordinary town, but as Ozma-san said, if they were randomly assigned and ended up having to spend time together regardless of whether they wanted to or not...... if Megiddo-san didn’t like that person, she really would kill them without mercy. If something like that happened during the pre-opening, it would be a serious problem, so I think having people accompany her as a precaution was a good countermeasure.","Well, even if Megiddo-san says she’ll mercilessly kill people she doesn’t like...... there aren’t actually that many people she dislikes to that extent. Unless they had some seriously problematic personality or something, she wouldn’t go out of her way to kill someone just because they irritated her a little.","Still, even if the possibility was low, they couldn’t afford to let their guard down...... and perhaps Alice or Kuro had subtly suggested that Ozma-san and the others accompany her for that very reason.","[Oh, right! I heard about it, Lilia! You’re apparently going to be contributing a comment about your impressions!]","[Eh? Yes, I was asked to do something like that, but......]","[You’re popular even in the Demon Realm after all! Oh, that’s right! I recently built a new facility in one of my cities too. I’ll invite you there, so give me a comment for that one as well! As expected, you’d have to hear the opinions of those that are strong, right?!]","[Yeksh! Ah, y- yes...... Ah, but if you’re going to invite me...... then perhaps Kaito-san could come along as well......]","......Am I being dragged into this somehow!? Lilia-san has certainly grown after everything she’s been through...... Well, I think I’m responsible for about 80 percent...... no, 90 percent of the reason, so I have no objection to accompanying her. But what kind of facility did Megiddo-san recently build? Was it for singing competitions? Or perhaps something like the fighting game she’d been interested in back at my birthday?","[Oh, that’s great! Then, Bacchus. Send an invitation to Kaito and Lilia later.]","[Understood. Lilia Albert and Miyama Kaito, please contact me later with dates that would be convenient for you.]","And, well, as usual, Bacchus-san was the one left to handle all the details of this sort of thing. He calmly told us to contact him with dates that would be convenient for us, as though he were accustomed to it, and after chatting with us for a little while longer, he left together with the cheerful Megiddo-san.","As usual, she was like a storm.","<Afterword>","Young Lady : [Eugh! Don’t bully Lilia!]","Serious-senpai : [She got volcanic rocks drawn to her nonstop, and then casually got hit with a follow-up stomachache...... This is the Strongest Stomachache Warrior......]"]},{"number":2638,"title":"Chapter 2638 - Re: Demon Realm Amusement Park 18","paragraphs":["After riding another attraction in the Flame Area, the next place we’re heading to is the Magic Area...... I’m guessing it’s probably an area modeled after Kuro, the creator of the magic tools.","However, it’s difficult to imagine what kind of place it is just from the area’s name. My impression is that it would have a strong fantasy feel to it, but magic is something commonplace in this world, so I wonder what it’ll actually be like......","[Once we get to the fifth area, it really feels like we’re entering the final stretch! But I wish we could’ve explored more of the areas we’ve been through so far too.]","[I understand how you feel, Hina-chan, but every single area is so large that it could practically function as its own theme park, so if we started exploring them without any restrictions, we’d never finish.]","[Even with the two attractions per area that we decided on at the beginning, it’s already taken quite a while, and I think that’s probably the best way to see all the areas...... But every area really is huge, and each attraction is so elaborate that there’s no way we could see everything in one day.]","Aoi-chan agreed with Hina-chan, who looked like she was having fun, and I joined the conversation based on my experience of exploring the park so far. In fact, every area really did have an incredible amount of content, and if we were talking about conquering every attraction, it was on a scale where I wondered just how many days it would take.","Actually, it was making me appreciate all over again just how incredible Kuro and Alice were for managing to build a theme park of this scale in less than a year.","We continued walking while talking like that and eventually arrived at the Magic Area, but...... it was once again an absolutely astonishing sight.","[Eh? Ehhhhh...... We’re in the sky?]","[N- No, but...... We came here normally without feeling like we were climbing to a high altitude or anything......]","I could understand why Hina-chan and Aoi-chan were staring in amazement. After all, when we arrived at the Magic Area from the Flame Area...... we found ourselves on what appeared to be a large floating platform, with similar platforms floating all around us, and clouds visible far below...... If I had to put it into words, it was as though numerous facilities, platforms, or pedestals were floating in the sky, creating what could only be described as a floating city in the heavens.","[This is...... The entire ground beneath our feet is probably Illusion Magic. It only looks this way, and in reality, I think there’s ordinary ground here.]","[However, this is...... amazing. It’s so intricately crafted that you can’t immediately realize it’s an illusion, and they’re able to keep Illusion Magic of this caliber active at all times?]","Luna-san and Sieg-san were also looking around in amazement, and even from the perspective of these two who were among the very best in the Human Realm, the Illusion Magic in this area seemed to be extraordinary.","The others appeared to be equally astonished, and Lilia-san murmured as she moved her gaze around with interest.","[......I see. A permanent Barrier Magic has been deployed throughout this entire area. In principle, I think it’s similar to the VR games Kaito-san possesses. Those use a method of sending one’s mind into a special barrier, whereas this appears to be projecting the scenery of a special barrier throughout the entire area. It’s a highly sophisticated permanent Barrier Magic, to the point that I would call it beautiful, so I imagine either Kuromu-sama or Alice-sama placed it here personally.]","I see, so the entire Magic Area is essentially one enormous Barrier Magic...... And that’s what makes it possible to create such an incredible spectacle......","[The reason why someone like me, who has high resistance, and Kaito-san are able to perceive the Illusion Magic as though it were reality is because it uses the same mechanism as the attractions we’ve encountered so far, with consent being established within the magic formula...... Most likely, the admission process at the entrance is being treated as consent.]","[Ahh, so it treats the act of voluntarily going through the admission process and entering as consent.]","I nodded in understanding at Lilia-san’s explanation. Just as Lilia-san said, although the format is different, the mechanism is probably similar to the VR game. In that game, voluntarily putting on the mascot costume is considered consent, while in this amusement park, they’re probably treating the admission procedure as consent within the magic formula so that people like me and Lilia-san can’t simply nullify it.","The notice at the entrance warning that Illusion Magic and other such things are used in the attractions might also be related to that consent.","[Anyway, I understand that this is an area where some incredible magic has been used...... But, how are we supposed to get around here?]","[If it only looks like this and there’s actually ground beneath us...... But when it looks this realistic, I have to admit I’m still hesitant.]","[But we can’t get anywhere unless we walk——— whoa!?]","Hina-chan and Aoi-chan muttered anxiously, and although I agreed with them, I figured we had to find some way to move around, so I approached the edge of the floating platform in the direction I wanted to go...... and a rainbow-colored bridge appeared in front of me.","[......Ah, I see. So when you approach while trying to head toward another platform, a path appears like this......]","[That’s amazing! So we walk across the rainbow to get to the next place!]","Once she understood how we were supposed to move around, Hina-chan’s excitement shot up, and her previously anxious expression instantly transformed into an excited smile.","Now that we knew how to get around, we immediately started walking across the rainbow bridge toward a relatively large floating platform nearby.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [It’s just an assumption, but does the Magic Area seem to have even more attractions and facilities that make use of various magic formulas than the other areas?]"]},{"number":2639,"title":"Chapter 2639 - Re: Demon Realm Amusement Park 19","paragraphs":["The Magic Area had an atmosphere that could only be described as a mysterious magical city. We had been moving along a rainbow bridge, and just as we reached a somewhat large, plaza-like area, something caught my eye.","There were several color-coded circular areas there, along with a sign that read “Warp Portal”.","Arehh? Could this be...... Previously, during the birthday party, I had seen Kuro really getting into a game, so I invited her to play another game together, and we had played it together. At the time, a facility with the same name had appeared in the game.","It was essentially a fast-travel feature, allowing you to instantly move to predetermined locations, and I remembered that Kuro had seemed quite interested in it.","[......Isn’t that different from a teleportation magic tool?]","[H- Hmm, I’ve never seen anything like that either. Judging by the map, I suppose you can move to locations corresponding to each color? But what about the cooldown......?]","Lilia-san tilted her head slightly as she answered Aoi-chan. It looked similar to a teleportation magic tool, but perhaps it would be more accurate to say that it was something different from the teleportation magic tools we had seen until now......","[This is just a guess, but considering what I think was the inspiration that Kuro was interested in...... I don’t know how it actually works, but I think it’s something like having Teleportation Magic constantly active while restricting the possible destinations, so you can move simply by stepping onto it...... Shall we give it a try?]","Saying that, I stepped into the red circular area among the several Warp Portals, and I was instantly transported somewhere else. Unlike a teleportation magic tool, there was no delay from selecting a destination or having a magic circle appear. It really was instantaneous.","I looked around for a little while, then stepped outside the red circle before stepping back into it, and I returned to where Lilia-san and the others were.","[......This is incredible! It could revolutionize distribution. I imagine the locations would have to be fixed, but if you could use it without having to wait for a cooldown......]","[Hmm, but I think this probably means long-distance travel isn’t possible, or even if it is, the construction costs would be far too high.]","In response to Luna-san, who spoke as though she were genuinely astonished, I told her what I had felt after actually using it. It certainly was incredible technology, and as Luna-san said, if it could be used for logistics, it would indeed revolutionize the industry.","However, if that were possible, there would be no reason for it not to have already been implemented by one of the trading companies Kuro owned, and Kuro was hardly reluctant to make that sort of technology available.","The fact that this hadn’t been done meant there had to be some kind of limitation, whether technical or energy-related...... As I was thinking about that, Alice suddenly appeared with a wry smile and gave us a brief explanation.","[Ah~~ Kaito-san, you’re right. Kuro-san and I made it as an experiment, but it’s basically a cheating piece of equipment. In theory, it works by keeping Teleportation Magic constantly active, but...... the magic crystals currently in existence couldn’t possibly provide enough power. If we tried to make up the difference, we’d need something like a magic crystal the size of a mountain, and even that wouldn’t be enough.]","[Ah~~ errr, so what you’re saying is......]","[Yep, just as Kaito-san imagined, the reason this can actually operate is because of that thing in the central area that Shallow Vernal-sama created, the infinite power source thing that’s practically picking a fight with the very concept of “energy”. Without that, we currently have no prospects of installing these anywhere outside the amusement park. That might change if we discover something capable of storing vastly more magic power than magic crystals, or some other source of energy though. For now though, it’s just a convenient facility exclusive to the amusement park.]","[I see. Thanks for the explanation.]","[Not at all~~ Well then, if you’ll excuse me~~]","To sum it up, for the time being, this was simply a convenient means of transportation that could only be used within the amusement park. The reason it was only in the Magic Area and nowhere else was probably because it was something unfamiliar even to the people of this world, so rather than introducing it everywhere at once, they had decided to implement it experimentally in only a few areas.","But certainly, if something like this...... a teleportation magic tool that could be described as a constantly active type could be implemented, it would drastically change the way goods were distributed. However, for that to become possible, they would need something capable of adapting to magic power and magic formulas with performance far beyond that of magic crystals, or perhaps some completely unknown form of energy...... Speaking of pipe dreams, then it certainly could be considered one.","However, the possibility of discovering some unknown energy or mineral in the future was not zero, and there was also the possibility that someone with a special ability like Tre-san’s, which allowed them to alter magic crystals themselves, might be born and give rise to something new, so perhaps there was a possibility that this dream could become reality someday.","Alternatively, technology brought over from the otherworld could potentially lead to rapid development, so there was no telling what the future might bring.","......Yes, certainly...... that was what I thought.","......At the time, I was merely letting my thoughts wander with a light sense of anticipation for the future.","......I never dreamed that, shortly afterward, an item brought to another world by a god would become the catalyst for discovering a way to evolve the properties of magic crystals.","<Afterword>","? ? ? : [......Can you not? Don’t give me an early spoiler for some huge Subject K that’s guaranteed to make Alice-chan overwork herself...... I’m already getting chills just thinking about it......]"]},{"number":2640,"title":"Chapter 2640 - Re: Demon Realm Amusement Park 20","paragraphs":["Now then, just as we did before, we had to decide which attraction to go to in the Magic Area, when Hina-chan came up with a suggestion.","[We’ve been deciding on one place first and then going there up until now, right? I think that’s fine too, but I think it’d also be fun to end up at an unexpected attraction. And fortunately, there are those short-distance Warp Portals here, so how about we intuitively warp through a few of them and then go to whichever attraction we happen to arrive at?]","[Ahh, I see...... Well, in a theme park like this, pretty much any attraction looks like it’d be fun, so that might be nice too. If we just pick something by looking through the pamphlet, there might be attractions we’d never choose otherwise......]","Hina-chan’s suggestion of moving around randomly several times using the color-coded Warp Portals and then playing at whatever attraction we ended up at was quite interesting. Since none of the others seemed to have any objections either, we decided to go with that format.","It seemed that we would also take turns choosing, so Hina-chan randomly chose first, followed by Aoi-chan, and we continued moving from one Warp Portal to another.","Then, at the point when we had moved so many times that we no longer had any idea where we were, Hina-chan announced:","[Okay, let’s make the attraction at wherever Kaito-senpai chooses next our destination!]","[Whoa, so I’m last huh...... Don’t blame me if we end up with something weird. Okay then...... Blue.]","The attraction closest to where I ended up after choosing the Warp Portal and moving for the final time...... There was a building a little way away from the point where we warped, so I guess that was it? The fact that it wasn’t a particularly large building probably meant it wasn’t a large-scale attraction.","Thinking that, I moved toward the attraction’s building...... and there, written in large letters, was “Shooting Gallery”.","[A shooting gallery!? No, surely shooting galleries are far too dangerous?]","[It’s an activity where you could suffer serious injuries depending on the circumstances, so perhaps we should really go to a different attraction......]","[......However, considering the concept of this amusement facility, I don’t think there should be a shooting gallery here......]","Somehow, I had managed to pick something completely outrageous. This was the shooting-gallery activity known as Super Space-Time Sniping Action, one of the competitions that had been incorrectly ported over to Trinia...... I’d had the opportunity to play a simplified version at the Founding Festival of the Hydra Kingdom, but was this the normal version? Judging from Lilia-san, Sieg-san, and Luna-san’s expressions of astonishment, I could tell just how dangerous it was...... But just as Luna-san said, would they really put an attraction like that in an amusement park?","Besides, this place was also intended for children, and even the attractions we had played so far had shown consideration in various places for children and people who couldn’t use magic, so it was hard to imagine that they would actually install an attraction where there was a possibility of someone suffering serious injuries.","[Ah, wait a moment. There’s a large sign in front of the building.]","Upon closer inspection, there was a gigantic sign set up in front of the building, and on it......","“New-Era Super Space-Time Sniping Action! An exciting sport that anyone can enjoy! Come and enjoy the super-evolved attraction, Shooting Gallery II!”","“※There is no need to worry about injuries with this attraction. Those who cannot use magic and children can enjoy it as well.”","......Could you not? I haven’t even managed to fully process the existing version yet...... Please don’t go and introduce some sort of advanced version.","B- But, anyway...... I guess this is something like a shooting gallery that’s been adapted into an amusement park attraction? Is it something like the one at the Founding Festival of the Hydra Kingdom? No, but that was fun as a minigame at a festival, yet it seemed a little too lackluster to be an amusement park attraction, and considering they went so far as to label it with II, I suppose it’s something different.","[......At any rate, it seems there’s no need to worry about injuries.]","[So they did take that into consideration...... However, if that’s the case, I can’t even imagine what kind of attraction it is.]","[......As for us, we can’t really imagine the shooting gallery Lilia-san and the others are talking about either......]","In response to Lilia-san, who muttered that with a thoughtful expression at my words, Aoi-chan gave a retort with which she wholeheartedly agreed.","I only had a vague understanding of it myself, or rather, all I knew was that it was a dangerous sport involving aerial combat.","Thereupon, Luna-san gave us a simple explanation to answer our questions.","[To put it in an extremely simplistic way, it is a sport where participants shoot magical projectiles at one another in the air. However, I heard that it originally came from the otherworld...... Since you said there is no magic in your world, do you shoot at one another using those things you call mashins?]","[......No, to begin with, the shooting gallery we’re familiar with isn’t something where you shoot at each other.]","[Conversely, how in the world did they turn it into a sport where people shoot magical projectiles at each other in the air......?]","Since we had my two kouhais who had also come from the otherworld with us this time, it was mentally reassuring not to feel like I was the only one who couldn’t keep up with the common sense of this world.","As for how it had been transmitted, which Hina-chan had wondered about, I knew that it had happened because Shiro-san had given fragmented pieces of information and Kuro had tried to recreate it based on those fragments...... So, well, there was really only one possible culprit: Shiro-san.","(Doya.)","And I had no idea why she herself looked so proud at that. Well, if this Shooting Gallery II turned out to be an incredibly fun attraction, then tracing its origins back might lead to Shiro-san...... right?","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [I see, during the Six Kings Festival and when they went to see RINGTOSS, there weren’t any other people from the otherworld around...... During the Maid Olympia, Akane was there, so they could relate to each other. I suppose being able to share the same common sense really is important...... Putting that aside, just what exactly is Shooting Gallery II......?]"]},{"number":2641,"title":"Chapter 2641 - Re: Demon Realm Amusement Park 21","paragraphs":["I don’t know exactly what kind of evolution it underwent, but for now, since it explicitly stated that there was no need to worry about injuries or anything like that, we figured it should be fine and entered the reception area for the Shooting Gallery II attraction.","And as soon as we entered the building, I felt like I understood why there was no need to worry about injuries.","[......I see, so that’s how it works.]","[It is something we’re pretty familiar with, but basically...... that’s what this means, right?]","Aoi-chan murmured in understanding at my words. The reason was that as soon as we entered the building, we could see a long row of mascot suits lined up farther inside.","Those mascot suits were similar to the ones used for the VR game I had received, which meant that Shooting Gallery II was apparently a competition held in that pseudo-VR space.","That certainly meant there was no need to worry about injuries, and if it was like a racing game, adjustments would presumably be made to things like our natural physical abilities as well, so we should be able to have a reasonably fair competition.","However, if I remember correctly, creating that VR space required a considerable amount of resources, and it had only been possible for the Six Kings Festival because they had unlimited access to materials...... But I suppose that aspect was also being solved by the Central Amusement Park’s mysterious power source?","Actually, now that I think about it...... Maybe the concept behind the Magic Area was to use the Central Amusement Park’s ridiculous power source to create attractions and facilities that would normally be difficult to realize with ordinary magical tools.","Well, I had only seen the Warp Portal and this Shooting Gallery II so far, so I could be wrong......","As I thought about that, we received an explanation of the attraction at the reception desk. There was also something resembling a small booklet, and it contained detailed information about the rules, making them easy to check.","And the impression I got after hearing the explanation was...... that it was something like an FPS game played in a VR space.","The basic rule was that it was a battle resembling a battle royale, with each player fighting using three types of special magic staves...... They looked like guns, so I’ll just call them guns, but anyhow, there were three types of guns to choose from.","When entering the VR space, each person would first be transported to a small room that served as their base. From there, they could choose whichever of the three guns they liked before heading out onto the field to fight.","Each player had a magical barrier, and taking attacks would reduce its durability...... This was essentially an HP-like mechanic. When an opponent’s attack reduces their durability to zero, the player would be forcibly returned to their base, where the magical barrier’s durability would be restored to maximum...... In other words, they would get taken out and respawn at their base.","They could also switch guns at their base, prepare themselves, and head back out onto the field...... Apparently, the attraction involved repeating that process and competing for rankings based on the number of opponents they defeated.","[......When you think of it as an FPS, I feel like it’s easier to picture.]","[Hmm, I’ve never played an FPS game before though.]","[......Is it different from those gun games at arcades?]","I had barely played any myself, but Aoi-chan also seemed to have no experience playing FPS games, while Hina-chan didn’t really understand what an FPS was in the first place and seemed to be imagining one of those arcade shooting games.","Still, if that was the case, it might be nice since we’d all be able to compete under fairly equal terms.","Having decided to participate in the Shooting Gallery II attraction, we went to the mascot suit area set up farther inside and climbed into whichever mascot suit we wanted...... and were immediately transferred into the VR space.","The base was a simple room, with three types of guns propped up inside. There was a space where we could test-fire them, as well as a place where we could review the rules. A countdown to the start of the attraction was displayed in the air above the room, and it seemed the game would begin in three minutes.","There was also a full-length mirror in the room, allowing me to see what I looked like...... I was wearing a motorcycle suit and a full-face helmet, and my face and other identifying features were obscured. Even when I spoke, my voice sounded as though it had been passed through a voice changer, so apparently it was impossible to tell who someone was at a glance.","Well, otherwise, there would be aspects that made things unfair...... If we looked exactly as we normally did and could identify our opponents from a distance, then if I spotted Lilia-san, I would run away as fast as I could.","The guns used up magic power instead of ammunition, and there was a meter beside each gun that allowed us to check how much magic power remained. Magic power only recovered naturally over time, and there was no reloading, so we had to be careful about how much we had left.","I tried firing a few shots to check the recovery speed, and it seemed reasonably fast. As long as I didn’t get carried away and fire wildly, it seemed like I’d be fine.","Each of the three guns had its own characteristics...... Their shapes were different, but if I compared them to guns I was familiar with, there was one that was like an assault rifle, with a good balance between power, rate of fire, and magic consumption. Another was like a submachine gun, with low power but an excellent rate of fire and fuel efficiency. The last was like a bazooka: it couldn’t fire rapidly, and its magic consumption per shot was by far the highest, but its power was overwhelming...... For now, I think I’ll go with the well-balanced assault rifle.","According to the rules, every time we were taken out and returned to our base, we could change guns according to the situation, so I’ll start with the assault rifle and use it to get a feel for things.","But still, I’m calling it an assault rifle for convenience...... but it really does look quite a lot like an assault rifle...... There’s absolutely no way Alice didn’t have a hand in these things’ designs......","<Afterword>","The Well-Balanced Assault Rifle : [......I shall merely demonstrate perfected marksmanship.]","Serious-senpai : [He’s already setting up a flag......]","? ? ? : [That well-balanced assault rifle is———–]","Serious-senpai : [The game hasn’t even started yet!]"]},{"number":2642,"title":"Chapter 2642 - Re: Demon Realm Amusement Park 22","paragraphs":["When I stepped outside the room serving as our base, I found myself in a city that gave off a somewhat futuristic feel. There were many tall buildings, as well as plenty of obstacles...... The fact that there were so many places to hide meant I would have to be careful of ambushes and attacks from blind spots.","I moved my body around a little, but there was no sense of discomfort. Our physical abilities were supposed to be standardized to some extent, and mine seemed to have been adjusted to those of an average human, so I felt almost no difference...... No, I actually felt like I was moving better than usual...... To avoid making myself feel miserable, I’ll just assume I’m moving about as well as I normally do.","During the explanation, several field gimmicks were introduced as well. One of them was a blue circle about one meter across that I could see nearby. Apparently, if I jumped while inside that circle, I could perform an incredibly high leap.","Quite a large number of them had been placed throughout the field, and by making use of them, it seemed possible to perform stylish actions such as leaping onto the rooftops of buildings and moving around by jumping from one building to the next.","Furthermore, if I jumped using one of these blue circles, I could leap once more while in midair. In other words, I could perform a double jump. On top of that, while in the air, I could apparently make a movement resembling an emergency evasion in any direction at the cost of reducing the durability of my magical barrier. By combining the high leap, double jump, and emergency evasion, it was apparently possible to move through the air with considerable freedom...... apparently.","It seems the Shooting Gallery before II was apparently known for its aerial combat, so I suppose it was designed with an emphasis on aerial battles in mind. Well, there’s no point thinking about it too much, so I’ll try jumping right away, just to see what it’s like.","When I jumped on top of the blue circle, my body shot up in an instant, soaring higher than the buildings...... This is amazing. The sensation when jumping and moving around feels incredibly realistic, and I can perform movements that would be absolutely impossible with my own physical enhancement magic, which gets me really excited.","While feeling exhilarated, I looked toward the wide-open view that had suddenly appeared before me...... and I saw someone else, a short distance away, who had likewise leaped into the air.","I encountered someone right away!? I couldn’t tell who it was from their appearance. Apparently, the combinations of helmet and rider suit colors differed from player to player, so I could use those to identify them to some extent...... but that would only be possible later on after the battle had progressed. When encountering someone for the first time, their identity was unknown.","Incidentally, my helmet was white and my rider suit was black...... The person who had leaped up had a yellow helmet and a white rider suit...... For now, I wanted to find out as soon as possible which combination Lilia-san was using.","There were no stage gimmicks in Shooting Gallery II that interfered with the players, and since physical abilities were also standardized, it was primarily a contest of the players’ sense and technique...... and in that sort of contest, Lilia-san was monstrously strong. She had probably reached a proficient level just by practicing casually in the waiting room...... In a sense, the strategy for clearing this attraction was to avoid Lilia-san as much as possible.","Turning my attention back to my opponent, I saw that they were holding a rather large gun...... a bazooka. Honestly, based on what I’d experienced during the test firing, I personally found the bazooka to be the most difficult gun to use. Its power was tremendous, and since it exploded upon impact, it also had a wide attack range, but it consumed a great deal of magic power. Although it had a long range, its projectile speed was slow and it couldn’t be fired rapidly, giving me the impression that it wasn’t suited for hitting opponents who were constantly moving around.","It seemed like it could be useful for firing into a group that was fighting and taking advantage of the chaos afterward, but......","As I was thinking that, the opposing player suddenly raised their bazooka and fired. We were still quite far apart, well outside the range of my assault rifle, but a bazooka could reach this far...... It could reach me, but the projectile speed was slow, so at this distance, dodging it would be easy. In fact, I could probably avoid it simply by naturally falling after my jump...... Wait, they’re not aiming at me!?","This trajectory...... Ah, shoot! They’re aiming for the rooftop I’m about to land on and trying to hit me with the blast!?","The magical projectile fired from the opponent’s bazooka landed on the rooftop in my path at a perfectly timed moment, causing a huge explosion. I couldn’t afford to get caught in the blast, so I performed a double jump here, changing the timing of my descent, dodging the explosion, and landing on the rooftop.","Then I immediately tried to counterattack, but...... They’re gone!? Did they use the explosion as a smokescreen to circle around me? Right? No...... Left!","When I turned to the left, I saw the player leaping toward me from the rooftop of another building. However, they were now within the range of my assault rifle, and I had the advantage in projectile speed and rate of fire. Intercept...... Eh? They use an emergency evasion to shift their axis, and when I readjust my aim, they use a double jump next? Wait, their judgment is fast...... Eeeeeh!? They use an emergency evasion toward the front partway through the double jump and suddenly come straight at me!? That kind of movement cancel existed!?","Shoot, I won’t be able to get my gun aimed in time...... I’m done for......","The opponent, who had pulled off a technical maneuver in midair as though mocking me, instantly locked onto me before I could react and slammed a bazooka shot into me as they passed by.","A bazooka’s firepower could normally cut the durability of a magical barrier in half with a direct hit, while a headshot was an instant kill. The opposing player landed the magical projectile squarely on my face, and immediately afterward, accompanied by a dazzling flash of light, I was sent back to the first waiting room.","......That was definitely Lilia-san...... There wasn’t the slightest hesitation in her movements, she used the emergency evasion, which consumes shield durability, with incredible precision, and both at the beginning and the end, she locked onto her targets with the bazooka in an instant...... And above all, I had no idea you could cancel the double jump’s movement with an emergency evasion.","I’d been taken out right away, but actually figuring out which player was Lilia-san was a stroke of luck. Yellow helmet, white rider suit...... Got it, I’ll remember that. If I see her again, I’ll run away with everything I’ve got.","There’s no way I could beat someone who, on their first time playing the attraction, had only practiced a little in the waiting room yet could pull off such an absurd maneuver right after the start.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [Well, yeah (if there are no stage gimmicks to interfere with the players), of course (Lilia would be on a rampage).]","? ? ? : [It’s easy to forget because her stomachaches are so impactful, but Lilia-san is genuinely a genius on a level that’s basically a bug in the world......]"]},{"number":2643,"title":"Chapter 2643 - Re: Demon Realm Amusement Park 23","paragraphs":["Although there was the incident of encountering the presumed Lilia-san right at the beginning, there weren’t really any problems after that. I was worried that I might get spawn camped the moment I left the base, but apparently, leaving the base causes you to be teleported to a random location on the map, so I ended up emerging somewhere different from where I started.","After that, I continued progressing while alternating between defeating others and getting defeated myself, and the timer visible at the edge of my vision had dropped to 5 minutes, making it feel like we were finally entering the endgame.","Having played this far, I think I’ve gotten fairly accustomed to it. And my impression after getting used to it was...... yeah, it really was just Lilia-san who was abnormal.","After being taken out by the presumed Lilia-san, I went outside and immediately encountered another player. This one moved in a way that wasn’t all that different from me, and although they managed to reduce my durability by about half, I was able to defeat them.","The other players had varying degrees of skill, but even so, their movements were within what I had expected...... Only the presumed Lilia-san was performing such stylish gun action that I wondered if she was playing a completely different game.","I mean, her movements were incredible, but even more than that, her aim was downright abnormal. She would aim and fire with such speed and accuracy that I seriously wondered if she had auto-aim enabled. The difference in level was just that enormous.","Still, being able to find the presumed Lilia-san at the beginning was genuinely useful. Not only did it allow me to immediately run away whenever I saw Lilia-san afterward, but more importantly, it allowed me to realize how useful the bazooka and jump-canceling were.","After being taken out by the presumed Lilia-san, I decided to try using the bazooka, and it worked incredibly well against the other players during the early stages. When people were still unfamiliar with the controls, it seemed that even a bazooka’s slow projectiles were surprisingly difficult to evade, making it much easier to land hits than I had expected.","I obviously couldn’t pull off something like the presumed Lilia-san’s point-blank headshots while passing by each other, but aiming at their feet and catching them in the explosion worked quite well.","Apparently, this attraction doesn’t have friendly fire or self-damage, so there was no problem detonating it at extremely close range. On top of that, just like it had happened with me, canceling the initial jump with an emergency evasive maneuver seemed to catch people off guard, and there were quite a few opportunities where I could blast a bazooka into an opponent who had been startled into freezing up.","However, that was only the case until the middle stages, when everyone was still getting used to the movement. Once we passed the midpoint, the bazooka could no longer really be called strong. After all, once you became accustomed to the movement, as long as you kept a certain distance, you could easily see the shot coming and evade it with plenty of time to spare.","Because of that, from the middle stages onward, I switched back to the assault rifle I had started with. When fighting with an assault rifle, opponents using bazookas were basically easy prey. As long as I maintained a certain distance, dodged their attacks, and kept firing, I could easily shut them down completely.","Since the submachine gun has a short range and requires you to get fairly close before firing, it’s difficult to dodge its attacks after seeing them coming, and its rate of fire is also high. So when encountering someone with a submachine gun, I had no choice but to accept taking a certain amount of damage.","However, its firepower was relatively low, so if I encountered one while I still had plenty of durability, I could overpower them with the assault rifle through a somewhat brute-force firefight. So, once again, from the middle stages onward, the well-balanced assault rifle was the easiest weapon to use.","And this was something else I noticed partway through: when I spoke, my own voice sounded as though it had been passed through a voice changer, but...... apparently, the other players couldn’t hear that voice. Naturally, I couldn’t hear their voices either, so it wasn’t possible to have conversations or anything like that.","That made me wonder why they had bothered making our voices sound like they were going through a voice changer in the first place, but perhaps it’s simply because the feature doesn’t exist yet, and they might implement things like team battles in the future.","However, it wasn’t as though communication between players was completely impossible; we could communicate through hand signals and gestures.","There was something rather amusing that happened in the middle stages. It was when three of us, including me, all carrying assault rifles, happened to run into each other and engaged in a three-way back-and-forth battle while making use of the obstacles.","When the player wearing a yellow helmet and white riding suit, presumed to be Lilia-san, appeared on that battlefield, the three of us immediately stopped fighting and simultaneously began running away.","It was like...... we had somehow become united in spirit for no reason at all. And it wasn’t just that. One of the players running away with me simply held up three fingers toward us, and both the other player and I understood it to mean “No hard feelings, let’s split up and escape in three different directions”.Without any discussion whatsoever, the three of us fled in different directions at exactly the right moment, throwing the presumed Lilia-san into confusion...... One of us who was directly pursued probably ended up as a sacrifice, but fortunately, I wasn’t pursued and managed to escape safely.","How should I say this...... It really made me feel that when people are faced with an overwhelming threat, their hearts truly do become one.","Of course, the presumed Lilia-san wasn’t invincible either. In particular, the presumed Lilia-san would use emergency evasive maneuvers while sacrificing her durability to engage in stylish aerial combat.","Although emergency evasive maneuvers didn’t consume that much durability, using them repeatedly would still reduce her durability considerably. So there were times when I managed to win after being unable to escape and having no choice but to fight. Thinking about those encounters, if the presumed Lilia-san’s durability had been reduced to the point where a single attack from me would finish her off, while my own durability was still above half, then I could win by charging in while accepting the damage.","......Well, considering that I had virtually zero chance of winning if we encountered each other while both of us were at full HP, the presumed Lilia-san was practically a kind of stage gimmick at this point......","Anyway, since the end was almost here, I thought I’d take a slightly bolder approach while also using the opportunity to rack up some points. With that in mind, I arrived at a fairly large open area in one section of the map...... only to find myself suddenly running into about five players who had entered the area at almost exactly the same time.","This is going to turn into quite a chaotic battle...... or so I thought, but immediately afterward, one of the players hurriedly pointed in a direction. When I turned to look...... I saw a yellow helmet and white riding suit leaping toward the plaza...... The presumed Lilia-san.","I wonder how to describe what I felt at that moment...... The five players who had happened to encounter each other in the plaza, myself included, all simultaneously raised our guns toward the presumed Lilia-san.","......Just when I thought it was going to be a chaotic battle...... It felt like a raid boss battle had just begun.","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [A development where enemies temporarily join forces in the face of an approaching threat...... The fact that Lilia is so overwhelmingly strong that it makes them resolve to fight her as a group of five is just absurd.]"]},{"number":2644,"title":"Chapter 2644 - Re: Demon Realm Amusement Park 24","paragraphs":["A certain kind of raid battle had begun out of nowhere...... Approaching us was, without a doubt, the strongest presence among the participants in this attraction: the presumed Lilia.","Standing against her was an impromptu team of five who happened to be there by chance, myself included.","I instantly organized the information in my head. Right now, we were in a fairly large plaza surrounded by buildings, and the presumed Lilia was approaching from one of the roads connected to the plaza. There were large buildings on both sides, but the road itself was wide.","The presumed Lilia was holding an assault rifle rather than the bazooka I’d seen her with at first. Combining the presumed Lilia’s mobility with the assault rifle’s performance was certainly threatening, but at least we didn’t have to worry about being wiped out by a wide-area explosion, meaning the five of us could bunch together and face her head-on.","Our forces consisted of one submachine gun, one bazooka, and three assault rifles, including mine...... Given this situation, the best formation we could take was......","We hadn’t communicated through hand signals. Yet perhaps people really could unite strongly in the face of an overwhelming threat, because, as though we’d planned it beforehand, the three of us carrying assault rifles, myself included, lined up side by side and moved to the front.","Yes, we were the ones who should move to the front here. If we’re talking range, the bazooka had the longest, but I couldn’t imagine being able to fire the slow-moving bazooka rounds straight at the presumed Lilia and actually hit her. Trying to hit somewhere near her and catch her in the explosion would also be difficult against the presumed Lilia’s judgment and speed.","The best strategy would probably be to stay in the rear at first and fire when an opening presented itself.","The submachine gun had the shortest range, but its overwhelming bullet speed and rate of fire made it arguably the key weapon against the presumed Lilia. That’s precisely why we assault-rifle users had to move to the front and protect the submachine gun.","The presumed Lilia was the type who made use of emergency evasion repeatedly, moving at high speed while attacking with phenomenal aim...... We needed to protect the submachine gun, then, once the presumed Lilia’s durability had been worn down completely, push forward and finish her off.","We lined up in a horizontal row and began attacking the presumed Lilia. No matter how monstrous Lilia’s combat ability was, the physical capabilities of the attraction’s avatars were the same...... There was no way she could make some utterly ridiculous movement and charge straight through the barrage from three assault rifles.","In that case, what the presumed Lilia would do in response to our simultaneous attack was...... Yes, evade with a huge jump from one of the blue circles. And that was precisely...... getting the presumed Lilia into the air was part of our plan.","Emergency evasion was certainly convenient, and combined with the presumed Lilia’s technique, it allowed her to perform such stylish aerial maneuvers that it was hard to believe she was playing the same attraction as everyone else.","However, emergency evasion had limitations as well. Namely, it couldn’t be used consecutively. After performing an emergency evasion, you had to perform some kind of movement action other than an attack before you could use it again.","On the ground, you could perform an emergency evasion, take a step, and then perform another emergency evasion, making it effectively possible to use them almost consecutively. But in the air, the sequence was jump, emergency evasion, double jump, emergency evasion, and after performing those four evasive movements, you couldn’t use emergency evasion again until you landed on the ground.","In other words, if we got the presumed Lilia into the air and forced her to use her double jump and emergency evasion...... then until she fell or landed somewhere, the presumed Lilia would be unable to use emergency evasion again. To make that happen, coordination between the three of us was essential...... We couldn’t talk, and there was no time to communicate with hand signals or gestures.","All we could do was trust that our temporary teammates were thinking along the same lines and make our move.","First stage. Just as expected, in response to the approaching barrage, the presumed Lilia performed a huge jump from the blue circle and leaped into the air...... Immediately afterward, one of the bullets that passed between us struck the submachine-gun user behind us.","You’ve got to be kidding me! It’s already difficult enough to shoot while simply jumping, but during a huge jump that’s considerably faster than a normal jump, she slipped right past the three of us standing in front and landed a headshot on the submachine-gun user!? What kind of monstrous aim is that...... No, but we’re still okay.","Even if it’s the presumed Lilia, she could only fire one shot during that instant of jumping. Unlike the bazooka, an assault rifle required three headshots against an opponent at full durability, or about two if their durability had already been chipped away somewhat...... At the very least, the submachine-gun user wouldn’t be taken out by a single shot.","I was surprised, but I didn’t stop moving. Along with the other two assault-rifle users, I took aim at the presumed Lilia in midair...... First, I casually raised one hand as a signal, then fired.","The presumed Lilia canceled the huge jump with an emergency evasion and dodged, coming to a stop in her ascent around the middle of the building...... within assault-rifle range.","The other two assault rifles immediately fired at her. With shots coming toward the location where she had performed her emergency evasion, the presumed Lilia naturally avoided them by performing a double jump.","But that was exactly what we’d been waiting for. I was already aiming at the point where she would land from her double jump, and I fired again. With that, the presumed Lilia had no choice but to perform her final emergency evasion.","There was a possibility that she might deliberately take a hit from a bullet in order to conserve her emergency evasion, but the other two would cover for that.","Certain that we’d completely cornered her, I watched as the presumed Lilia performed a horizontal emergency evasion and dodged my shot. But that meant she was defenseless until she landed defense...... less...... eh?","The presumed Lilia, who had performed a horizontal emergency evasion, twisted her body and “placed her foot against the side of the building”...... Wait, don’t tell me...... that counts as landing......?","The anxiety that flashed through my mind became reality. The presumed Lilia kicked off the wall of the building, leaped away, and evaded our follow-up attack...... then attacked us from the air.","Of course, we fought back as well, but what unfolded before our eyes was a scene straight out of a nightmare...... Using the walls of the buildings on both sides, the presumed Lilia raced through the air in every direction, putting on a stylish display of absolute domination...... We’d thought we’d cornered her in the air, but we’d actually put ourselves at a disadvantage.","I saw the bazooka user who had been behind us fire at the presumed Lilia. That’s right! There was that option...... If she was flying around using the walls of the buildings, we could fire at the walls and catch her in the resulting explosion.","Even if that didn’t work perfectly, we could at least interfere with her landing on the building walls...... Uh...... I know it’s the slowest projectile of the three guns, but she just shot down the incoming bazooka projectile with an assault-rifle round almost without even looking, making it explode in midair...... What the hell is that monster...... What are we supposed to do here......?","<Afterword>","Serious-senpai : [The protagonist is fighting while devising a strategy with probably the most seriousness we’ve ever seen from him...... It’s in a game, though...... Can this really be considered serious? Should I equate simply taking something seriously with being serious, or does it need a little more tension, a little more weight...... And it’s a game, too...... H- Hmmm...... No, but if I don’t allow this much and count it as serious, it feels like I might never get to see a serious development again for the rest of my life...... No, but compromising as the incarnation of seriousness...... Hmmm.]","? ? ? : [You’re also having what might be the most serious internal struggle we’ve ever seen from someone who claims to be the incarnation of seriousness.]"]}]);
